So far, the Ministry of Tourism has focused on training more than 1,000 spa and wellness professionals in major tourist destinations to welcome national and international tourists by providing satisfactory services and high professional ethics. .
This training course on spa and wellness skills is designed with the aim of training more new skills for those working in the spa and wellness services, both in theory and in practice on existing skills to achieve. Achieve the following goals:
By 2020, Cambodia Tourism will achieve 50% of its jobs by training and evaluating Cambodian tourism professionals.
By 2025, Cambodia Tourism will achieve its job by training and evaluating 100% of Cambodian tourism professionals by participating in promoting the one-on-one staffing campaign.
Recall that with the strong growth of national and international tourism in recent years, the tourism sector has created about 620,000 direct jobs, equivalent to 13% of the total work, and by 2020 and create nearly 1 million direct jobs. And by 2025, about 1.2 million, and by 2030, 2 million, regardless of the indirect employment of tens of thousands more.
Mr. Veng Sakhon continued to talk and thank the people in Kampong Siem district who voted overwhelmingly for the Cambodian People's Party
(Kampong Cham): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Chairman of the National Task Force for Kampong Siem District, on August 7, 2018, met with 1,200 people in order to thank the members and people. Out of 2,426 people out of 2,426 who went to the polls, the majority voted in favor of the CPP.
Speaking in Kampong Trom Krom village, Koh Mit commune in the compound of Kampong Trom pagoda, which is the location of the above program, Mr. Veng Sakhon said that this great result confirms that:
1. The people need peace, social stability, economic growth and development under the leadership of the Royal Government with Samdech Techo Hun Sen as Prime Minister.
2: Clearly see the skillful and wise leadership of Samdech who liberated the country from the disaster of the chronic civil war to a developed country in terms of economy, culture, politics, diplomacy and democracy, face to face on the international stage, especially in ASEAN Community.
3. The overwhelming majority of votes show the strong will of the people who have chosen the path of democracy through the exercise of civil rights as stated in the Constitution, which is the supreme law of the country.
In the happy atmosphere of the victory that Koh Mit commune received, Mr. Veng Sakhon brought greetings from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritbandit, who expressed their concern for the hardships that the people were experiencing due to the disaster. Flood.
At the same time, he highly appreciated and thanked the voters, the Chairman, the Deputy Chairman, the members of the Commune / Village Assistance Team, the local authorities, and the Armed Forces for their hard work and dedication before and during the election. Campaign until the victory today.
In order to maintain this victory, he instructed the authorities at all levels, members of the national working group to help districts, communes and villages to continue to implement the policies of the Royal Government, especially the high-level instructions of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who said:
1: To continue to help local people based on the spirit of honesty, high responsibility and more active, comprehensive and more effective in order to alleviate the difficulties in daily life, solve practical needs and needs in accordance with the priorities and possibilities of the people.
2: Authorities at all levels must strive to implement the 9 policies of the CPP better.
3. Continue to implement the policy of safe villages and communes, strengthen the efficiency of providing all kinds of public services to the people, and the members of the National Working Group must continue to implement the A3 policy without discriminating on the basis of political tendencies. Can lead to the disintegration of our national unity.
In the afternoon of the same day, Mr. Veng Sakhon and his colleagues also continued to travel to Vihear Thom commune to meet and thank the members of the National Working Group on the commune, as well as members of the party, local authorities and the Armed Forces at all levels. Especially for the people who voted on July 29, especially for the Cambodian People's Party.
The ceremony was held at Andong Svay pagoda, Andong Svay village, with the participation of about 400 people. Vihear Thom commune received 2,291 votes out of 2,538 party members, accounting for 90.97%.
