(Kandal): Sixteen families affected by a land grab by a trader raised their hands in prayer to the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, to intervene and find justice for them. Also.
The appeal was made when they brought a complaint to Ms. Men Sam An, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection to cancel their land freezing letter on the morning of August 7, 2018, but was stopped by officials. The Ministry did not accept and continued to complain to Kandal Provincial Hall to ask the Kandal Provincial Board of Governors to help find justice and expedite the issuance of title deeds to them as soon as possible.
Later, Samdech Techo Hun Sen cut off the disputed land from the Cindai Company and handed it over to the above 16 families and hundreds of others by letter No. 563 S.C.N. dated 28 April 2008. Issued by the Office of the Council of Ministers.
She said that after the intervention of the Prime Minister, they returned to normal, until 2015, Khieu Vises came to negotiate to buy their land twice, but they did not sell. Suddenly, in 2016, Khieu Vises complained to Ms. Men Sam An that the 16 families had encroached on their 32 hectares of land, claiming to have bought it from 20 other families who were not named in the S.C.N. Above that.
Due to the above irregular complaints, 16 families also complained to the Kandal Provincial Hall to the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, together with the Prime Minister's Office for further intervention.
In the case that Vietnamese people in Kampong Chhnang province go to pay permanent residence tax, the provincial governor came out to confirm the fact that they go to pay taxes as immigrants, not to live forever
Responding to this criticism, the Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, Mr. Chhour Chandoeun, through Fresh News this evening, explained that the case of Vietnamese people in Kampong Chhnang Province who came to pay the tax is as an immigrant valid for 2 years. Did not apply for the right to live permanently in Cambodia as alleged.
According to the governor, these Vietnamese are not new entrants, as they have been censored by the government since 2002, meaning they are old entrants registered as immigrants and the state No new entrants will be accepted in case any new entrants are found to be deported from Cambodia.
Mr. Chhour Chandoeun said, "We have been censoring this Vietnamese since 2002 and after 2002 we no longer recognize him. Once we have done the census, each Vietnamese citizen has to apply for a two-year permanent residency permit from the Ministry of Interior, and for another two years, they have to apply again. When he announced and had to pay 250,000 riel, the Ministry of Interior issued a card to them.
The governor of Kampong Chhnang province stressed that the Vietnamese who went to pay the tax were not new people, and if they were new, the authorities would immediately send them back to their home countries. Therefore, Cambodians or Facebook users should not There is confusion by some group or individual that inflates this information.
According to the report of the General Department of Immigration, as of 2018, 340 foreigners living illegally and committing various crimes have been deported from Cambodia, including 52 women and many Vietnamese. Also.
