Seize 7 overweight trucks along National Road 4, officials complain about the difficulty in enforcing the law because the perpetrators are rich and powerful
(Preah Sihanouk): Overweight vehicles inspection team this morning, August 7, 2018, raided National Road No. 4 and intercepted 7 overweight vehicles traveling on National Road No. 4. 4.
The operation was led by Mr. Seng Chhuon, Undersecretary of State and Chairman of the Secretariat of the Standing Coordinating Committee of the Overseas Vehicle Inspection Committee of the Ministry of Public Works, with the participation of officials from the Department of Public Works and Transport of Preah Sihanouk Province as well as relevant authorities. Also ..
Mr. Seng Chhuon said that the police seized the seven vehicles on Stung Hav district road after they tried to drive away from O'Chamna scales on National Road 4.
After weighing, some vehicles were overloaded with tons and others overweight. Mr. Seng Chhuon said that after weighing, the officer dropped the goods from the truck and fined the actual overweight according to the law. At the same time, the car owner was asked to make a contract to stop overweight, and if there is a case of overweight later, the car will be stored.
According to official sources, most of these overweight trucks are owned by wealthy tycoons and powerful backs. Officials also complained about the difficulty of enforcing the law on these illegal trucks because the owners were all rich and powerful.
According to the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, in June 2018, officials detained about 212 overweight trucks and fined them more than 500 million riels. Overweight trucks from 5 tons to 46 tons.
According to the report, the number of overweight trucks continues to increase despite the efforts of the relevant authorities to prevent it, which shows the attitude of the transport business for the sake of profit, not to think of road damage. Public interest.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, said he did not want the money from the fine because the fine could not be used to repair the road damaged by the overload. Mr. Sun Chanthol also called on all overweight truck owners to pity and love the road, which is a public property, because each road, the head of the Royal Government, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, tried to find funds to build for the benefit of the people.
