Mr. Som Soreida stated that "the case of Mr. Sam Rainsy requesting to recount the ballots is not possible because Mr. Sam Rainsy is not a candidate on the list of candidates of political parties to stand for election. "So reiterate that this case is not possible because it is against the law."
According to the senior NEC official, the recount could take place when a political party complains of serious irregularities that could affect the election results, at least after the election. One day means that on July 30, 2018, political parties must submit this complaint to the Commune / Sangkat Election Commission, and this commission will make a decision.
He said that if he is not satisfied with the decision of the Commune / Sangkat Election Commission, the political parties participating in the election have the right to complain to the Capital and Provincial Election Commission, and if they are not satisfied with the decision of the Capital and Provincial Election Commission. Vote, he can complain to the NEC again.
Mr. Som Soreida added, "If you come to the NEC, if the NEC finds enough evidence to charge you and believes that the complaint really shows irregularities that affect the results of the election. The NEC can decide whether to reject the complaint or decide to open the security package "A" to check, verify the voting materials and recount the ballots.
According to the Deputy Secretary-General, only two institutions have the right to decide on the recount, the NEC and the Constitutional Council. However, before reaching the recount, only if the complaint is filed according to the hierarchy specified earlier.
According to Som Soreida, demanding an immediate vote count is not possible if an agent or representative of a political party does not register a political party to stand for election. In the case of Mr. Sam Rainsy, who has no right to request a recount, the main reason is that he is not an agent of a political party, not a candidate of a political party in this 6th legislative election. .
"If Mr. Sam Rainsy, an agent of a political party or a representative of a political party, complains about irregularities that affect the election results from the commune level to the NEC and then complains about the announcement of the provisional results, To recount the ballots. But first, there are no ingredients and second, he has no right to sue. This is according to the addition of the Deputy Secretary General of the NEC.
