First: On May 13, 2018, the Special Task Force of the Committee cracked down on the case of opening fake and illegal coffee handicrafts in Duong Village, Sangkat Prek Pnov, Khan Prek Pnov, confiscated 10 exhibits equal to 7 tons and arrested One suspect.
Second: On July 4, 2018, the Special Operations Team of the Committee cracked down on the case of opening a non-compliant patent production site on Lum Road, Sangkat Teuk Thla, Khan Sen Sok, and confiscated 14 exhibits equal to 5 tons.
Third: On July 6, 2018, the Special Task Force of the Committee cracked down on the case of opening illegal pepper and coffee production handicrafts at 2E0, Street 226, Village 13, Sangkat Phsar Doeum Kor, Khan Toul Kork, confiscating exhibits 13 faces equals 18 tons.
The General Chairman of the Committee emphasized that in this crackdown operation, the Special Task Force of the Committee carried out according to the complaint of the original company, in cooperation with the relevant professional institutions in the Committee, and with the cooperation of the local authorities to investigate. About the crime of counterfeit and illegal products to the point of successfully cracking down and confiscating a lot of exhibits.
