Cambodia Beer takes its top 19 customers to Germany and France for a week from 5-12
(Phnom Penh): Every year, Khmer Breweries, a Cambodian brewery, organizes trips to world-famous destinations for its customers. Today, Khmer Breweries took 19 of its top clients on a week-long trip to Nuremberg, Germany and Paris, France, cities that tourists from all over the world have always wanted to visit.
This tour starts from the 5th to the 12th of August 2018. In addition to this tour, Khmer Breweries will also arrange trips to many other countries and cities in Asia, such as Korea, Hong Kong for other customers.
Leang Pov, CEO of Khmer Breweries, said, “On behalf of the management of Khmer Breweries, I am very pleased to have the opportunity to meet with customers of Cambodia and France. Our best in 2018 to travel to Nuremberg and Paris today.
He added that the other two purposes of this trip are to encourage outstanding customers to continue their efforts next year for the success of all and to create good memories with their outstanding customers.
Leang Pov explains why the company selects Nuremberg and Paris:
According to the CEO, Khmer Breweries always provides customers with the best, the most civilized, the most modern and the first to do so, so the company decided to take customers to these famous cities. Customers who can participate in this trip must meet the conditions, just have to sell Cambodian beer and other products of Khmer Breweries to the target set by the company.
