Pursuant to the announcement of the Phnom Penh Capital Administration, 5 notices have been issued on ensuring the well-being and safety of waterways in the rainy season to all owners of waterways, vehicles, passengers, tourists, cargo and port owners. Doing business along the Mekong, Tonle Sap and Tonle Bassac rivers in Phnom Penh.
In the announcement of the Phnom Penh Capital Administration, it is said that in order to ensure the well-being, dignity, safety of waterways, prevent damage to crops, people's houses and river bank collapses in the coming water season, ask the owners of all kinds of water vehicles. And all port owners apply the following measures:
First, adequately equipped with safety equipment, raft bags, jacket bags, fire extinguisher bags on all means.
Second, when traveling in or out of Phnom Penh, the speed must be reduced to 20 km per hour and driving near the river bank, which causes the river bank to collapse, affecting crops and people's homes. .
Third: Do not load passengers, tourists or goods over capacity.
Fourth: Driving at night must have proper lighting.
Fifth, the road up and down the port must be prepared well, clean, not slippery or slippery.
