(Kampot): Mr. Chiao Tay, Governor of Kampot Province, led relevant officials to inspect and rebuild the Stung Keo Bridge to facilitate people to travel and transport after the Stung Keo wooden bridge was flooded. The whirlwind broke out on July 19 recently.
On that occasion, Mr. Chiao Tai said that in the past, the people of Stung Keo commune had a very difficult time traveling by having to change from crossing a wooden bridge to traveling by boat across Stung Keo. But 90 days later, all the people who used to use this broken bridge will travel back to the new wooden bridge, which is a precious gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The provincial governor continued that due to the responsibility of the Kampot provincial administration, especially with love and understanding of the hardships of the people, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, through his own financial support to help build a new Stung Keo bridge for the people.
The new bridge will be built at the site of the old bridge in Anlong Mak Prang village, Stung Keo commune, Teuk Chhou district, Kampot province, with a width of 3 meters and a length of 80 meters, with a total budget of 15,000 dollars. Tuk-tuks, motorcycles, cars can drive through, seeing the difficulties of the people, the bridge will be completed within 90 days.
