Mr. Khim Bunsong told the people and the public to work together to preserve, protect and preserve the environment, natural resources, culture and history in the Phnom Kulen area
(Siem Reap): The Governor of Siem Reap Province, Mr. Khim Bunsong, called on the people and the public to work together to protect and preserve the environment, natural resources, culture and history in the Phnom Kulen area through this potential and sustainable tourism sector to improve livelihoods. Another level of improvement.
Such an appeal was made on August 4, 2018, during a meeting with more than 400 people in Khnong Phnom commune, Svay Leu district at Preah Ang Thom in Khnong Phnom Kulen.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Khim Bunsong stated that Phnom Kulen is a tourist destination, culture, nature and history that is rich in ancient statues and temples embedded in this mountain forest, especially the great king of Phnom Kulen. Places of worship of our Cambodian Buddhists as well as national and international guests come to worship.
According to Mr. Khim Bunsong, the Phnom Kulen area has been attracting the attention of national and international tourists to visit and learn about our civilization, culture, nature and history of Cambodia. He also pointed out that Phnom Kulen is an area that provides irrigation water that flows along the historical river Siem Reap-Angkor to feed people, animals, plants, especially agriculture.
He also pointed out that due to this peace factor, the Kulen mountain range has been developed and these are the people who have faith in the leadership of the Cambodian People's Party, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen. Led the Cambodian ship to the shores of happiness.
At the same time, Mr. Khim Bunsong also brought souvenirs to the 400 people, each of whom received 20,000 Riels. He and she also offered candles, incense and flowers to the Buddha image and sacred objects at the Great Buddha. Svay Rieng provincial administration claims that there were no thieves cutting down trees at Svay Rieng provincial hall worth nearly 1 million dollars
