Land Dispute Between Citizens and Former Craft Industry Officials of 18 Families Long Lasting Resolved in Koh Kong Province
(Koh Kong): The land dispute between 18 families of former handicraft industry officials in Khemarak Phoumin City, which has been protracted for many years, has now been resolved under the continuous coordination of Mr. Phay Thun Plam Keson, Deputy Governor of Koh Kong Province and Mr. Chheng. Sovannda, Governor of Royal Khemarak Municipality, as well as many other relevant officials.
The resumption of this long-standing land dispute settlement took place on August 3, 2018 yesterday. An official from Koh Kod Provincial Hall told Fresh News Agency in Koh Kong province this morning, August 4, 2018: The settlement will be measured to hand over the title to his 18 families.
On that occasion, Mr. Phay Thun Plam Keson said that in order to solve the mechanism to cut the state inventory of the Department of Industry to the 18 families, the officials also agreed with Mr. Cham Prasidh, Minister of Industry and Handicrafts, at the request. Former and lower level civil servants of 18 families.
The Deputy Governor added that the measurement of the ownership plan will determine the size of the land for the practical skills of former and civil servants of the Department of Industry who are enjoying every day.
Mr. Oum Thy Saroeun, a former official who is working in the department, thanked the higher and the provincial level for resolving them with transparency now that they have been enjoying since 1990. Former families and officials of the 18 families will soon be expected to obtain legal titles soon, and they will continue to farm without fear.
It should be noted that the settlement of the land dispute ended with an area of nearly 1 hectare, located next to the Department of Industry and Handicrafts of Koh Kong Province. Cambodian Red Cross distributes humanitarian aid to flood-affected people in Ratanakkiri
