During the handover, Mr. Thong Savun expressed his condolences to many families who lost their property, livestock and rice fields due to natural disasters in the past.
He added that although these humanitarian donations could not be enough to meet the needs of the victims, it was a contribution from the Cambodian Red Cross, the provincial authorities and the Stung Treng branch. The villages are fenced together to help rescue the victims who are in dire need of help.
At the same time, Mr. Mom Saroeun, Honorary President of Stung Treng Branch, thanked the Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Ratanakkiri Province for its support and assistance to the victims who need help and support.
