Things should not happen! A man on a motorbike oversteered and hit a bamboo pole on a bulldozer traveling in the same direction, causing a fatal explosion.
A horrific traffic accident that caused a man on a motorbike to oversteer and hit a bamboo pole on top of a bulldozer, causing the sudden death of the above-mentioned above, which should not have happened in the evening. On August 3, 2018, along National Road 6A, south of Bak Kheng Post, in Kdei Chas Village, Sangkat Bak Kheng, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh.
According to the police, the man who died in the accident was riding a black Honda Dream C125 motorcycle with license plate Kampong Cham 1F-1857 and his name was Phat Soklin, 28 years old. Khmer people live in Thmey village, Krala commune, Kampong Siem district, Kampong Cham province.
However, after the incident, it was observed that the local authorities, cooperation and professional authorities measured and decided to take the bulldozer transporting the bamboo with the motorbike to be stored at the Land Traffic Office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police to wait for a legal settlement. Later and immediately search for relatives to receive the body to prepare for the traditional ceremony.
