(Phnom Penh): The nationwide traffic law enforcement campaign for August 3, 2018, the traffic police force inspected 765 vehicles and found 90 vehicles violating the law (50% motorcycles), 45 education vehicles and 45 fines. This is according to the official report of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the General Commission of the National Police.
According to the report, 458 helmets and goggles were inspected on August 3 and 19 vehicles were fined.
For the results of the three-day inspection from August 1 to 3, the police inspected 2,124 vehicles and found 285 offending vehicles (63% motorcycles), including 150 education vehicles and fines. 135 units.
Minister of Agriculture urges the European Union to continue to work with the Royal Government in the development of Cambodia to achieve its vision of becoming a high-middle-income country
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Mr. Veng Sakhon, on the afternoon of August 3, requested Mr. George Edka, EU Ambassador to Cambodia to continue to join the Royal Government of Cambodia in further development of Cambodia to achieve the vision. Turn Cambodia into a high middle income country by 2030.
Mr. Veng Sakhon's request was made on the occasion that he and Mr. George Edka, Ambassador of the European Union to Cambodia, presided over the award ceremony for the winner of the Best Livestock Breeder Project under the Agricultural Growth Promotion Program. Sustainability and Environment, Fisheries Sub-sector and Animal Production Sub-sector on the afternoon of Friday, August 3, 2018 at the Ministry of Agriculture.
The animal production sub-sector of the General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production received more than 7 million euros to develop and improve animal health and animal production, focusing on three main expected outcomes that have been implemented across 25 capitals. The provinces are: Strengthening animal production systems and institutional management, strengthening the network of village animal health agencies and supporting smallholder farmers.
The winner is an outstanding breeder as part of a program project that selects and encourages the best person to raise animals and grow fodder crops in order to turn them into you. Raising animals commercially and as a model for other farmers.
In this project, 111 chicken farms were established, which spread to more than 1,300 families, an increase of 52,217 chickens. Established 100 pig farms and distributed to more than 400 families, equivalent to 360 pigs.
The program also focuses on planting weeds for fodder, creating 200 sites for more than 420 families on 9,352 ha. Improving the hygiene of 155 slaughterhouses, vaccinating animals, making biosafety, inspecting animal and meat safety, breeding cows and artificial pigs have also been effectively implemented.
The Minister of Agriculture instructed all stakeholders to focus on the well-being, challenges and livelihoods of farmers by developing plans to strengthen the capacity and increase farmers' incomes in line with national economic growth and especially for 2030, which the country Cambodia is expected to become a high-middle-income country.
