Airbus will work with Vietnam to develop the aerospace industry following reports of the signing of an agreement between the European aircraft manufacturer and the Vietnamese Ministry of Science and Technology. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Friday afternoon, August 3, 2018.
Potential areas of bilateral cooperation include the exchange of information on issues related to Earth observation, organization and participation in scientific events, as well as research on satellite technology. In 2010, Airbus was awarded a development contract to build and launch an Earth observation satellite.
The VNREDSat-1 satellite was successfully launched in 2013 and it has enabled Vietnam to better monitor and study the effects of climate change, as well as better forecast and take action on natural disasters. .
Airbus is also developing its industry in Vietnam, where it has trained more than 550 highly skilled Vietnamese workers to boost the sector in Vietnam.
