Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) urges Tay Seng Special Economic Zone Company in Bavet City to cooperate to make it easier for people involved in power grid poles
(Svay Rieng): Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) on August 3 urged Tay Seng Special Economic Zone Company, located in Bavet, Svay Rieng Province, to cooperate with Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) and another economic zone company to facilitate the lighting of electricity poles. Organize well so as not to affect the people. This is according to a press release obtained by Fresh News this morning, August 3.
According to Electricite du Cambodge (EDC), due to the people's dissatisfaction with the electricity poles planted on their land, they do not run in a straight line like the angle of the stove, which includes a row of electricity poles of Electricite du Cambodge (EDC). One row of Seng and one row of Manhattan Economic Zone, so the people asked EDC to help solve.
