According to the report, one person was killed and two others were injured in the accident, which damaged two motorcycles and two cars. Cambodia-China sign protocol on phytosanitary requirements for Cambodian banana exports to China
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of August 2, 2018, Cambodia and China held a signing ceremony of a protocol on phytosanitary requirements for the export of Cambodian bananas to China, held at the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries. Fishing.
The ceremony was signed by Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and Mr. Xiong Bo, Ambassador of the People's Republic of China to Cambodia under the chairmanship of Mr. Hor Namhong, Deputy Prime Minister and Representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The signing of this protocol is the response of the Chinese side at the request of the Cambodian side through the working group of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, which has resumed market negotiations with the Chinese side through the preparation of a work plan for the preparation of banana export protocol. Cambodia to China and agreed on the draft on September 25, 2014 in the Union of Myanmar.
It should be reminded that on March 25-26, 2018, the former General Administration of Quality Inspection and Inspection of the People's Republic of China invited experts from the Ministry of Agriculture of Cambodia to attend a technical consultation meeting to finalize the draft protocol on phytosanitary requirements. Sanitation for the export of Cambodian fresh bananas to China with the former General Administration of Quality Control, Inspection and Quarantine in Beijing
During the technical consultation meeting, the two sides promised that the two sides would determine the time and place for the signing of the above protocol as soon as possible after the merger between the General Administration of Quality Control. Inspection and Chatsalik with the General Administration of Customs of China and the new leadership of the General Administration of Customs.
As a result, a number of protocols were signed, including:
Protocol on the Export of Cambodian Cassava to China between the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and the General Administration of Quality Supervision, Inspection and Quarantine (AQSIQ) of China was signed on December 13, 2010.
Protocol on the export of Cambodian rice to China between the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and the General Administration of Quality Supervision, Inspection and Quarantine (AQSIQ) of China was signed on October 22, 2010.
3. The Protocol on Rice Export to China between the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and the General Administration of Quality Supervision, Inspection and Quarantine (AQSIQ) of China was signed on September 9, 2016.
With the results obtained today, the Cambodian side has been requesting the Chinese side to examine the possibility and expedite the work to import some other agricultural products to the Chinese market, such as: mango, lentils (Tangen). Dragon fruit, pepper, apricot and earwax for further export to China.
