The first 6-star luxury multi-functional building in Cambodia and Southeast Asia officially opened in Sihanoukville
(Preah Sihanouk): Prince Thean Sivan, a multi-functional luxury building project developed by Prince Real Estate (Cambodia) Group, was officially inaugurated this morning, August 1, 2018 by Mr. Chhiv Koursinh, Executive Chairman. Prince Real Estate (Cambodia) Group and Mr. Li Min, CEO.
After studying and putting out a detailed plan for 2018, Prince Real Estate (Cambodia) Group has selected the coastal area located in Village 3, Sangkat 3, Sihanoukville, Sihanoukville Province as a project development site. Prince Thien Sivan, the first 5-6 star luxury multifunctional building in Cambodia and Southeast Asia.
Sihanoukville is Cambodia's largest seaport city, once a private resort for the royal family, known as the "Beach for the King" is one of the best tourist destinations.
With the construction of the "One Belt Road" and many international ventures, Sihanoukville has changed its face by developing into an international city with beautiful beaches. Star hotels, shopping malls, top entertainment venues, popular restaurants, etc. are gathered in this city, making it a popular tourist destination in Southeast Asia.
To the south of the Prince Thien Sivan project is Victory Beach, to the east is the Cambodia-Vietnam Friendship Memorial Park next to the Hawaiian beach, and to the south is the Emario Resort development site, which has beautiful white sand beaches.
The Prince The Sivan project has a total area of more than 300,000 square meters, designed by a top international company. This multi-functional project includes: 5-6 star hotels, boutique hotels, apartments and business centers. Prince Thien Sivan offers world-class residential and commercial services.
The project also includes shopping malls, exhibition halls, international conference halls, residences, commercial services, restaurants, modern swimming pools, speedboats, in particular, the project also features a modern and spacious 25,000-square-meter car park.
As a leading enterprise in the field of real estate development, Prince Real Estate Group currently has more than 800 hectares of reserve land in Cambodia, equivalent to a total development project of more than 10 million square meters. In addition to Phnom Penh, Prince Real Estate Group is expanding its development projects to key provinces such as Sihanoukville and Siem Reap.
