(China): In many parts of China, Internet technology is strengthening medical services and health care, facilitating the treatment process and providing convenience to patients.
In addition, patients can pay for treatment services directly through the in-patient card scanner, rather than standing in line to pay.
"I used to see a doctor here, but I had to line up to pay and take my medicine downstairs," said Zhao Yiping, a resident. But now doctors can also do all this for me through a smart medical system. I just went downstairs to take the medicine to it already. "It's really easy."
In some remote areas of China, the presence of remote medical systems has allowed patients to consult with doctors remotely, which has made it more convenient for residents.
This system has been proven to be an effective way for patients, especially those who are unable to see a doctor directly due to traffic congestion and poor health.
In more than 1,800 prefectures across China, more than 13,000 hospitals already use remote medical services, which greatly reduces the difficulty of accessing medical care in border areas. And remote areas. (China CCTV) A well-known microfinance institution in Cambodia is offering a special program to customers who just pay their loans through TruMoney.
