NEC Officially Announces Number of Election Complaints and Ballot Counting
(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) has issued an official proclamation on the number of election-related complaints and the counting of ballots in the 2018 6th National Assembly Election.
According to the NEC, so far it has received 2,525 complaints, including three from the Cambodian People's Party, 2,520 from the Alliance for Democracy, and two from the Local Democrat Party.
Among them, 34 were convicted and 2,491 were related to the election and vote counting.
