(Kampong Chhnang): Mr. Heng Ratana, Director General of the Cambodian National Mine Action Center (CMAC), on August 1, 2018, called on people all over Cambodia if they find bombs or unexploded ordnance, please do not transport It's itself risky because it can endanger our lives.
Heng Ratana, CEO of CMAC, made the call after a case in Kampong Chhnang province's Samaki Meanchey district, when a group of sand dredgers encountered a US MK82 bomb and dug their own bomb and took it to the police. Commune and district police, but they did not dare to accept because it is not their specialty and also transported to the CMAC in Kampong Chhnang.
Mr. Heng Ratana confirmed that this is very dangerous, please call people do not commit such activities to contact their experts to neutralize, please do not transport like this.
Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign August 1: 114 Illegal Vehicles Found and 54 Fined
(Phnom Penh): The nationwide traffic law enforcement campaign for August 1, 2018, the traffic police force inspected 700 vehicles and found 114 vehicles violating the law (61% motorcycles), 60 education vehicles and 54 fines. This is according to the official report of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the General Commission of the National Police.
According to the report, 387 helmets and goggles were inspected on August 1, 34 education helmets were inspected and 19 helmets were fined. You give up raising pigs and come back to raising them again!
Mr. Srun Pov stated that the increase in the price of pigs was due to the fact that raising pigs in Vietnam, which used to be imported to Cambodia, often had problems in importing more to Cambodia. He said that at present, Vietnamese pigs are imported to Cambodia in small quantities and only Thai pigs are imported to Cambodia in large numbers, thus pushing up the price of Cambodian pigs and attracting more livestock.
He said that now farmers who have given up raising pigs are rushing back to raising pigs, but this raising is still small because when the price of pigs went down, they sold pigs and stopped raising pigs about 50 percent, but by the time Want to re-raise, there are not enough piglets to raise.
However, Mr. Srun Pov stated that this price can not be expected to be stable because it depends on the prices of neighboring countries such as Thailand and Vietnam, which means that if the price of pigs imported from Thailand - Vietnam is cheap. The pork market in Cambodia is also declining.
He stated that the market situation of live pigs in Cambodia is between 8,500 riel and 9,200 riel, especially for this price, pig farmers can benefit and have not seen any signs affecting consumers.
Ms. Leng Sok Khim, a pig farmer living in Kampong Cham province, said that the current price of live pigs is very reasonable and acceptable, selling up to 9,200 riel per kilogram, while previously sold only 5,500. Only 6,000 Riel.
He added that the LDP has filed up to 2,520 lawsuits, and the CPP and the Local Democrat Party have only five. He added that despite the many complaints, the NEC was still able to announce the provisional and official election results in a timely manner.
"Most of the complaints are of the same type, so we can package and issue a decision so it does not affect the announcement of the provisional results and the official results," he said.
