Tomorrow morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to meet with more than 10,000 workers in Por Sen Chey district
Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, said that 14,697 workers from 24 factories in Por Sen Chey district will meet with Samdech Techo Hun Sen tomorrow.
According to Mr. Ith Sam Heng, the 24 factories that allow workers to meet with Samdech Techo Hun Sen tomorrow have 19 Chinese, 2 Korean, 1 Singaporean and 1 Cambodian bosses. There are 21 garment factories, 2 shoe factories and 1 laundromat. All products are exported to international markets and supplied to domestic markets.
It should be noted that Samdech Techo Hun Sen started to open a forum to talk with workers from factories, enterprises and establishments since Sunday, August 2017. So far, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has met with a total of 51 workers, with a total of 700,202 workers.
Through a series of meetings, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has provided many benefits to workers and also harmonized in the garment and footwear industry. Ten companies will recruit nearly 2,000 people through the National Employment Agency
(Phnom Penh): On August 9, 2018, the 10 major companies will announce the immediate recruitment of 1,971 employees in collaboration with the National Employment Agency of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training.
Mr. Chou Leang considered the job forum and other activities of the National Employment Agency as contributing to bring many job opportunities to students who want to find a job. "This forum is really good because it helped me as well as those who are looking for a job to get a job quickly," he said.
He sees this job search service as really good, contributing to significantly reducing the unemployment rate of Cambodians, which is an important part of the strategy to help those in need.
He said his company currently has a total of about 800 employees, some of whom are selected from the NEA job forum.
He also thanked the NEA for facilitating the company to coordinate and provide location for his company as well as other companies to organize monthly job fairs.
Please be informed that in the operation to help find jobs for Cambodians in the first half of 2018, NEA helped to find jobs for about 3,251 Cambodians, registered about 7,590 job seekers will organize 42 job forums.
