(Banteay Meanchey): Farmers and local authorities, water resources officials have been pumping water to loosen canals and rice fields, as well as planting acres of dry rice harvesters, or so-called light paddy, in the early rainy season during the floods. Rainfall continues to rise in the rice fields in the communes of the upper Mongkul Borei River.
