Meanwhile, Mr. Ou Sopheap, Deputy Governor of Mongkul Borei District, also told the news agency that pumping water and rushing to harvest unripe rice and ripe rice is an emergency response to prevent farmers' early season rice from sinking and eventually being damaged because Floodwaters continue to flow from the upper reaches of the canal system.
According to the farmers, a few days ago, the price of fragrant rice and other types of rice were in good condition, which was 12,000 baht, but now it has dropped to only 8,700 baht per ton, equivalent to 1,044,000 riels, a big difference. Very. So let the price of rice be accurate and clear, the price they can get 9,500 baht equal to 1,140,000 riels and also save money for subsistence.
The farmer stated, “One hectare of rice field has run out of money, including a total rent of 12,000 baht, equivalent to 1,440,000 riels. And if the price is cheap, how do we find the money to pay them back? Therefore, let the Royal Government, the authorities, especially the rice collection association, please consider any price we get.
The affected farmers were flooded by torrential rains from Prek canal, Ktan canal, Po canal 2 and other places in the western part of Mongkul Borei river, which flooded many acres of ripe rice and ripe rice. That asked for immediate and targeted intervention of the Department of Water Resources and village, commune, district authorities to help release water.
In this case, on July 31, Mr. Ou Rathrey, Deputy Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, representing Mr. Suon Bavor, Provincial Governor, inspected two pumping stations at the Neang Ket sluice gate, Russey Krok commune, at the Kralor bridge in Banteay Neang commune to Loosen the water to liberate the rice of the flooded farmers in 4 communes: Soeur commune, Chamnom commune, Rohat Teuk commune and Bot Trang commune.
