Letter to readers: Let Cambodia decide on its national destiny!
By: Chao Chak Smok, Kamchay Mear District, Prey Veng Province, August 1, 2018
This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen made his first public appearance after the election to inaugurate the Russey Keo Passenger Terminal.
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian People's Party, appeared in the first public forum on Wednesday morning, August 1, 2018. After the election of the 6th legislature. Samdech Techo Hun Sen's public appearance to inaugurate a passenger ferry terminal in Russey Keo district.
It should be noted that the Royal Government of Cambodia, through the Ministry of Public Works, has organized inland waterway transportation to create a system of interconnected transportation (waterways, roads, railways and airways) to promote the livelihood of People are better off because water transport can transport more at a lower cost, safely and on time without traffic jams.
The Russey Keo dock, which was inaugurated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen this morning, has a concrete area of 968 square meters, a 366-square-meter floating port with a maximum capacity of 180 tons, a 30-meter-long steel bridge and an 84-meter waiting tower. The square is equipped with sufficient equipment, using the entire national budget of approximately 2,351,730,000 Riels, equivalent to nearly 590,000 US dollars.
In addition to the Russey Keo ferry terminal to facilitate this waterway transport, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport has also built four other berths, including: Old Market Pier, Chaktomuk Port, Chbar Ampov Port and Port. Black eyes. Each ferry terminal is connected to a bus station, making it easy to switch between waterways and road / land transport.
The above five passenger berths cost the national budget a total of 6,029,413,000 riels, equivalent to more than 1.5 million US dollars.
