Chan Yutha, a spokesman for the Ministry of Water Resources, confirmed that Stung Treng, which is currently flooded, was not caused by the rising Mekong River, which was due to heavy rains for some time. Today up to 112.5 mm.
At this point, he explained that for Stung Treng province, when the water reaches a height of 10.50 meters, it will lead to flooding some low-lying areas, and Stung Treng city can not be threatened until the water level of the Mekong River reaches 11.50 meters, because Stung Treng city has a dam. A flood built by the Ministry of Water Resources in 2006.
According to the spokesman, for Stung Treng province, the water level of the Mekong River will rise gradually in the next day or two, with the water level rising by 10.84 meters this morning and rising by 5 pm this evening. 92 meters due to lower rainfall in the Mekong River basin in Laos and Thailand.
Mr. Chan Yutha continued that after Stung Treng province, the water level of the Mekong River will increase in Kratie province, then Kampong Cham province and Tbong Khmum province in the next consecutive period.
