(Moscow) - Scientists have revived a species of worm after it was frozen in the cold "Siberia" of Russia for nearly 42,000 years. This was quoted from the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Tuesday afternoon, July 31, 2018.
The group of worms was taken from two organic specimens found in Siberia, one of which is about 32,000 years old, found in an ice core 30 meters below the surface. Another area, taken from a depth of 3.5 meters, is 41,700 years old.
After being removed from the ice, the worms were placed at a temperature of 20 degrees Celsius, and they began to show signs of survival, moving and eating in the next few weeks.
