EU freezes assets of six Russian companies over Crimea bridge (video inside) (Brussels): The European Union (EU) on Tuesday decided to freeze the assets of six Russian companies involved in the construction of a new road and bridge connecting Russia. To the Crimea. According to the agency.
Russia annexed Crimea from Ukraine in 2014, despite a series of condemnations and economic sanctions by the European Union, especially the United States. In addition, after the seizure, Moscow ordered the construction of a bridge worth more than $ 3.6 billion to the Crimea, which was proposed by Russian President Vladimir Putin in May.
But the European Union has strongly condemned Moscow and called Russia's construction of bridges and control of Crimea illegal. In response, the European Union on Tuesday decided to freeze the assets of six Russian companies, as well as ban EU individuals or entities from funding them.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Pisey, Governor of Russey Keo District, came out and completely denied and denied the allegations made by some media outlets on Facebook that the Russey Keo District Authority had led several joint police forces to demolish the house fence. According to Meas Savoeun, Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Justice, this is not true.
On the evening of July 31, 2018, the Governor of Russey Keo District in a press conference rejected the posting of information on Facebook accusing the authorities of using violence against people immediately after the election until the accusation. Adhering to the authorities, the authorities have also arrested minors.
At the same time, the workers even used underage children to buy gasoline to set fire to the protests, which is why the authorities prevented the children from taking gasoline. Use violence and kidnap children. According to the district governor, there are people behind this problem and this problem is happening.
Mr. Chea Pisey continued that what was true was that on behalf of the Russey Keo district authorities received a complaint to resolve the dispute between Mr. Meas Savoeun, a land dispute with a neighbor next to the border for many years, demanding to maintain the status quo. The land remains intact, ie no houses or fences are allowed to be built, pending the settlement of the dispute by a joint commission so that one of the two parties can enjoy the disputed land. Further.
Mr. Chea Pisey stated that after receiving an order from Mr. Khuong Sreng on behalf of the district authorities, Mr. Meas Savien was required to immediately suspend the construction of fences on people's land with valid title deeds, maintaining the land status. To remain the same, otherwise there will be a series of legal administrative measures due to complaints from the people.
It is remembered that during the year 2000, Mr. Meas Savoeun, the former third deputy governor of Preah Vihear province, was arrested by the authorities and sentenced to prison for the above land issue, so the authorities should take more action. This person should not be allowed to cause the above land issue anymore.
