Cambodian Customs and Stakeholders Hold Workshop on Combating Illegal Weapons Trafficking in the World Customs Organization
The workshop lasted for eleven days, from July 31 to August 10, 2018, organized by the General Department of Customs and Excise in collaboration with the World Customs Organization with the aim of training trainers and increasing Capacity for relevant technical officers of the countries participating in the implementation of the Air Transport Security Project against and preventing the illegal trade of all types of small arms (SALW).
He also said that the workshop was an opportunity for all participants to collaborate more closely and to become partners in exchanging information, knowledge and key experiences to effectively fight terrorism.
Mr. Nuon Chanrith, Deputy Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, thanked the World Customs Organization for selecting Cambodia to participate in the implementation of the project and thanked the Government of Japan for providing financial support for the workshop.
He also mentioned that this workshop is a good opportunity for all participants to learn and increase knowledge through discussions and exchange of views directly with the expert team of the World Customs Organization.
