A total of 10 people have been killed and more than 100,000 forced to flee their homes after monsoon rains inundated villages in central and southern Myanmar. This was released by CNN on Tuesday afternoon, July 31, 2018.
Myanmar's Disaster Management Authority has urged people near or along the riverbank to evacuate to safety as the river rises to a state of emergency and floods cut off roads and inundated many villages. .
As of Tuesday, more than 119,000 people in five provinces, especially in the central part of the country, had been evacuated and 70,000 affected by the floods.
