The Federation of Investors Association congratulates Mr. Thong Khon on his appointment as a member of the European Tourism Academy
(Phnom Penh): President of the Federation of Investors, Mr. Ley Sopheap, congratulated Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, on his appointment as a member of the European Tourism Academy from the European Council on Tourism and Trade.
The inauguration ceremony of Minister Thong Khon, a member of the European Tourism Academy, was presided over by Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong on the morning of July 31, 2018 at the Friendship Palace of the Council of Ministers.
Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong said this morning, July 31, 2018, on the occasion of presiding over the representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, at the inauguration ceremony of Dr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism. European Tourism Academy ”with Prof. Dr. Anton Caragea, President of the European Council on Tourism and Trade, at the Friendship Building of the Council of Ministers.
"I firmly believe that under the leadership of His Excellency Dr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, the cooperation between the Council for Tourism and Trade of Europe and the Ministry of Tourism of Cambodia will be further strengthened to Let Cambodia become a world-class tourist destination that offers warmth, charm and quality. ”
Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong continued that under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and the win-win policy has brought complete peace and development in all areas to Cambodia, including tourism, which has brought more tourists. 5 million people visited Cambodia in the past. This is also due to the complete peace throughout the country.
He added that the development of tourism has effectively contributed to the socio-economic development of Cambodia by creating job opportunities, increasing direct income for the people, making Cambodia the most attractive tourist destination in the world.
Meanwhile, Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong confirmed that for the 6th legislative election, Mr. Anton Karaga, together with the delegation, also took the opportunity to participate as an observer on July 29. At the same time, it is hoped that the delegation observed that the election was fair and democratic, with more than 82% of the population voting, which we should encourage the implementation of the democratic obligations of the Cambodian people.
At the same time, the former Cambodian Minister of Diplomacy stated: "I would like to thank the European Council for Tourism and Trade, especially His Excellency Professor Dr. Anton Karaga, who has always supported Cambodia and considered Cambodia as a model for the world in "Develop a tourism sector that distributes income equitably and recognizes Cambodia as a world-class tourism destination."
Mr. Thong Khon said that Cambodia is projected to receive about 6.2 million international tourists in 2018 and 7 million in 2020, bringing in about $ 5 billion, creating 1 million direct job opportunities. . By 2030, Cambodia is expected to receive about 15 million international tourists, bringing in a total revenue of $ 10 billion, creating about 2 million jobs.
