Ministry of Environment clarifies on the broadcast of Hang Meas TV regarding the case of stopping the excavation and restoration of canals in Prek Lpou Lake, Takeo Province
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Environment on July 31, 2018, issued a statement stating that the cessation of canal excavation activities by stopping machinery in the Boeung Prek Lpou landscape protection area at Boeung Bek Chan point, Koh Andet district, Takeo province, due to staff name The government acts without a permit.
According to its clarification, the Ministry of Environment has confirmed that the Ministry of Environment has the authority to manage the Boeung Prek Lpou landscape protection area in accordance with the law on natural protected areas. The Law on Protected Areas states that all use of natural resources, clearing and land use in protected areas must be approved by the Ministry of Environment.
The Ministry of Environment made the remarks after Hang Meas TV aired a ban on digging canals in the Boeung Prek Lpou Landscape Protection Area in Takeo province.
The Ministry of Environment explained that on May 24, 2018, a person named Sand Ratha dug a canal in the protected area of Boeung Prek Lpou Lake at Boeung Bek Chan, Canal 01 and Canal 00, which was dug by the park ranger at Boeung Prek Lpou Landscape Protection Area. Prohibited and stopped the excavation activities by confiscating the machinery as well.
The ministry emphasizes that the excavation of the canal by a man named Sand Ratha was done to sell the water for commercial purposes to the farming community there without a business license.
After being educated and explained by the Takeo Provincial Department of Environment, Sand Ratha agreed to sign a contract and confessed to the Deputy Director of the Boeung Prek Lpou Landscape Protection Area before allowing the excavator to be taken.
