International observers applaud Cambodia's election after observing the election
(Phnom Penh): Representatives of all international observers from various countries and international organizations have expressed their enthusiasm for the National Assembly election in Cambodia after they participated in the election observation and saw the real situation. In the election on July 29, 2018 in Phnom Penh and other provinces.
Representatives of the International Observer Organization from the Shanghai Cooperation Organization (SCO) confirmed that the Cambodian people have actively participated in the election to achieve their political will. The representative from China also confirmed that the election in Cambodia in the sixth mandate was smooth, fair and secure.
Representatives of international observers from Nepal expressed their admiration to see so many Cambodians go to the polls as the parliamentary election process went smoothly. "Cambodia is safe and prosperous, especially the Nepalese observers, who are not afraid to observe in Phnom Penh and other provinces," he said.
Unlike other observers, the Maldives Commission on Human Rights also praised the 6th legislative election process.
According to representatives of the Central Democrats International (CDI), the 6th legislative election process was free, fair and just, without any threats or violence. Seeing the turnout of 82.17% of Cambodians, CDI representatives expressed their deep congratulations on the success of Cambodia as a whole.
The representative of the Italian Trade Union Confederation said that during the election process, he observed that the voters were happy, which is a picture of true democracy, the people have the right to decide the future of their leaders. Many people went to the polls in Phnom Penh and other provinces.
Amb Sergey ORDZHONIKDZE and several other international delegations visited polling stations in Phnom Penh yesterday. The Russian observer said he had seen firsthand the good conduct of the election process without violence and security. Especially the happy and overwhelming turnout of the electorate.
