Over the past 25 years, Tata Technology India has helped many well-known companies and start-ups succeed in their business ventures. Three years ago, these companies ventured into the Chinese market and opened a Chinese headquarters in Shanghai, which is now focusing on the electric vehicle market.
"China has the largest growing economy, with a huge consumer market of 28 million vehicles," said Annan Pade, Asia-Pacific sales manager at Tata Technology. "These are indicators that clearly show the opportunity for us to participate in the market and learn from the market."
It should be noted that in China, only 750,000 electric cars are produced per year, which is less than 5% of the total car production, and by 2020, the Chinese government wants to produce 10 electric cars. % Of total car production.
"Last year in Beijing, NextEV management realized that without Tata, they would have had a hard time, this is a proud time for us to make cars," said Annan Pade. Electricity first and use of personal intellectual property. "What's more, this car can compete with lightweight cars that meet German standards."
"Every car made in India is good for the whole world," he said. "Currently, all electric cars made outside India and sold in India are ineffective."
By 2020, India is projected to become the world's third-largest car market, with demand for cars growing in India, with a population of 1.2 billion.
The electric car market in China is also growing rapidly. Currently, Chinese companies are benefiting from Indian technology, while India is benefiting from Chinese manufacturing skills. (China's CCTV)
