In the first half of this year, 106 investment projects were approved with a total investment of $ 3.5 billion.
(Phnom Penh): In the first half of 2018, the Council for the Development of Cambodia approved a total of 106 investment projects, including 97 new projects and 9 production expansion projects. This is according to the press release of the Council for the Development of Cambodia at Fresh News received on July 28, 2018.
The total investment capital of these approved projects is about US $ 3.5 billion, creating nearly 100,000 jobs.
At the same time, investment in industry and manufacturing increased by 22%, in which 8 garment factories increased from 15 projects in the first half of 2017 to 23 projects in the first half of 2018. According to the Council for the Development of Cambodia, the investment figures show an upward trend in investment in the first half of 2018, with no signs of hesitation or delay in investment.
