TOP NEWS: Greater China announces support for Cambodia's election and hopes the international community will play a constructive role in promoting smooth elections
BEIJING: The Chinese government has announced its support and wishes for the upcoming National Assembly elections in Cambodia on July 29, 2018. This is according to Geng Shuang, spokesman for the Chinese Ministry of Foreign Affairs, who spoke at a press conference on July 27, 2018 in response to questions from journalists.
The official website of the Chinese Ministry of Foreign Affairs reported that during the press conference, some journalists raised the question: "Regarding the Cambodian election, does the Chinese side support or not support Samdech Hun Sen as the next Prime Minister?" There are some opinions criticizing the Chinese side that China has overwhelmingly supported Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen during the election until the 29th, how did the party respond?
"The Chinese side supports Cambodia and the Cambodian people in choosing options that are in line with Cambodia's actual development situation and wishes the Cambodian election a smooth run," a Chinese Foreign Ministry spokesman said.
Please note that Cambodia will hold the 6th National Assembly Election on Sunday, July 29, 2018, with 20 political parties competing. This election has more political parties than the previous term, more national and international observers than the previous term, and more campaign participants than the previous term. Khmer children's point of view: This is Cambodia: Elections under the sound of music!
(Phnom Penh): International observers who followed a large-scale campaign event on the closing day of the election campaign on Friday expressed surprise at the good political situation in Cambodia.
They say that while elections in developing countries or young democracies are more violent, bombings scare people around the neck, but elections in Cambodia take place under The sound of music, dancing and dancing by the supporters of the political party. Both campaign leaders and campaign participants danced without fear.
International observers have been very appreciative of the issue and have expressed surprise at the political situation in Cambodia, saying they have never seen a country as peaceful as Cambodia.
International observers have compared the situation in Cambodia to that of other countries in the world where they used to observe elections. In many countries, such as Pakistan, observers have recently been on high alert as terrorist bombings have become more frequent and have killed scores of people.
In this situation, both observers, campaign leaders and supporters of political parties are on high alert and under constant fear. But the situation in Cambodia is the opposite, which makes them very surprised. The election campaign was quiet, non-violent, and especially the campaign was accompanied by live music and dancing.
In fact, Cambodia, which has a bad reputation on the international stage, is due to those who pollute the environment, distort the truth and constantly fabricate stories that seriously damage the national reputation. In addition to being self-defeating, this extremist group also spends money from scams to hire some foreigners to spread bad news about their country.
A group led by traitors Sam Rainsy and Khmer sold a handful of ideals to foreigners and has been campaigning to slander the real situation in Cambodia for the purpose of seizing power and to gain sympathy in exchange for financial support. Foreign organizations or governments, including Cambodians living abroad, continue their political careers to perform their deceptive plays.
The electoral environment is going well, which is rare in any country. In particular, what is special about Cambodia is the election under the sound of music and cheers, not the sound of bombs and cries like in some countries. This is the real situation in Cambodia.
