Tomorrow, the 6th legislative election will come, please go and vote for everyone from 7:00 am to 3:00 pm!
(Phnom Penh): The 6th National Assembly Election 2018 will come on July 29, 2018 tomorrow. Therefore, all citizens of voting age and whose names are on the voter list, please prepare the documents for the election so that everyone can go to the polls.
What documents do I need and what do I need to do to vote?
To contribute to the smooth running of the parliamentary election, Fresh News 7 questions and answers of the National Election Committee (NEC) to help promote the understanding of the Cambodian people about the election. This.
Question 1: When and where will the 6th National Assembly Election 2018 take place?
Q2: What are the conditions for Cambodian people to be able to vote?
Answer: Firstly, there must be a name on the 2017 voter list of any polling station in the commune / sangkat and secondly, there must be an identification document to be used during the election.
Q3) What are the identification documents to use during the election?
Answer: Must have any of the following documents: Khmer identity card type 1 or type 2 or type 3 or proof of identity used for voting.
Q4: What should be done if Cambodian citizens do not have or are missing or have lost their Cambodian identity card?
Answer: The person concerned must take 3 3 x 4 size photos (taken in front of them) and bring 2 witnesses who have the right to vote and have a residence or accommodation in the commune / sangkat to appear in front of the Commune Commission. The Sangkat organizes the election and the Commune / Sangkat Chief to fill out the application form for the election identification document.
Q5) When is the deadline for requesting identification documents for voting?
Q6: How useful are voter information leaflets?
A: The voter information card is very useful for the people whose names are on the voter list because it provides the voter's personal information about the voter number, the date of the election, the name of the location and the polling station code. This ballot is not valid for voting.
Q7: What if people want to check their names on the official voter list?
