They try to distort history, mislead the people, eradicate the people's memory by distracting the people from propaganda, deception, exaggeration and they dare to violate the law, trample on the rights of others and destroy the fundamental principles of democracy by calling for People are not allowed to go to the polls.
They do not value peace and do everything they can to achieve their power ambitions, even destroying the peace and development that Cambodia has today. Why is peace and development so important for the nation and the people of Cambodia?
If you know that wars are very destructive to the nation and the lives of many people, Cambodia's past experience also shows the reality in some Arab countries torn by the color revolution, also see why so few people like to incite. Got back to war and like to rekindle the flames of war without realizing it? A small number of people, especially the supporters of the Han Dynasty, were so overwhelmed that they were ready to make ants and fish.
What for? In fact, they have never experienced the pain of war, they do not know the magnitude of the pain of losing in the flames of war. Is it fun to see Khmer Rouge forces evacuate more than 2 million people from Phnom Penh? Is it happy to see millions of Cambodians, including our relatives, die unjustly and in unparalleled misery?
Is it fun that people live without the right to freedom, not even the right to believe and believe in religion, not the right to choose a partner to love? Including the lack of access to education while pagoda schools were demolished by the Khmer Rouge or used as cattle barns or manure depots. Not scary, but this is true in Cambodian history.
Do we need a civil war to tear apart and kill each other Cambodians? The answer is that everyone will say no to war, but peace is a necessary condition for the exercise of all human rights. Peace is the first essential element to ensure that a country can begin to have time to organize its development.
Cambodia has moved from a country that has received Blue Hat troops on its territory to a country that sends Blue Hat troops within the framework of UN peacekeeping missions to other countries, which so far have had Thousands of Cambodian troops have been on missions around the world.
This is the pride of Cambodia, a country traumatized by the war, but has restored its global reputation and honor as a country that has taught peace lessons to some countries in the region. That is why peace is a necessity that Cambodia needs, not only people who need peace, even wildlife, need peace and live in peace.
2. Development needed by the people: Nearly three decades of war have devastated Cambodia. The process of rebuilding and rebuilding the country from scratch after liberating the country and the Cambodian people from the Khmer Rouge regime has gone through a difficult path. Cambodia at that time used one hand to prevent the return of the Khmer Rouge regime and the other hand to build the country out of the ashes, blood and tears.
During 1979-1991, some Western governments chose to support the wrong side, opting for a series that promoted disorder, including the Khmer Rouge, and against development-promoting groups. Developments that have led the country to an average GDP growth rate of more than 7% in the last two decades and reduced poverty from more than 50% in 1990 to below 10% by 2018 .
At the same time, Cambodia is a country that has achieved almost all of the Millennium Development Goals. Cambodia is currently a low middle income country and by 2030 will be a high middle income country and by 2050 Cambodia will be a high income country.
The past has clearly shown that when our country is engulfed in the flames of civil war, we lose time to develop the country almost completely, but for our neighbors, such as Thailand, Singapore, etc., quickly thrive on the development of the country. Cambodia has just achieved full peace for 20 years, Cambodia has only restored and developed the country, and this development will continue to grow even more.
Do we want the history that Cambodia has gone through to be repeated? Peaceful country for 10 to 20 years, return to a devastating war again? The answer is no! The miserable Cambodia used to be destroyed almost everywhere, piled up with the remnants of war, the piles of bones, the victims, the graves, the bodies of the elderly and the Cambodian people, overwhelmed by the mental crisis.
Now that Cambodia has restored its new face, peace is complete, the majority of the people are overjoyed, and development has always moved forward. With the fruits of this peace, we must all work together to safeguard this peace and development at all costs, and join hands with the rich, the poor, and the rich to move forward. Go for prosperity together.
Therefore, in order to protect our peace and development that exists today, the people whose names are on the voter list, please go and vote for everyone on Sunday, July 29, 2018! Go to the polls for ourselves and for our democracy and homeland! By: Chao Chak Smok, Phnom Penh, July 27, 2018
