More than 80 students from 5 countries gather at University Holiday Event in Cambodia
This is the second time since 2016 that both universities in Cambodia have organized this program. This year, the University of Health Sciences organized this holiday university focusing on the theme: "School Health: Health Education for Our Future." The Royal University of Fine Arts focuses on the topic: "People's family business: handicrafts in Cambodia."
The events of these two universities are held at different locations. The University of Health Sciences guides students on field trips to the university's laboratories and conducts a variety of activities in Battambang province.
Conferences and workshops organized on a variety of topics are being organized during the university events this holiday season. Group discussions resulted in an exchange of education and general knowledge related to health and culture between students from different countries.
In addition to study tours, the two groups of students also visited various cultural and tourist sites in the provinces and in Phnom Penh to learn about the culture and way of life of the people. The holiday university has successfully completed a friendly and fraternal atmosphere, establishing many relationships and memories between Cambodian and foreign students who speak French from India, Laos, France, Vietnam, etc.
