Samdech Sar Kheng Closes Election Campaign in Prey Veng Province, Voters are Pro-Democracy Proponents
(Prey Veng): During the closing ceremony of the fourth election campaign of the Cambodian People's Party in Prey Veng province, which gathered at the party headquarters in Prey Veng province, CPP activists and about 1,500 people organized a campaign parade. The 6th National Assembly election was held on the morning of July 27 under the leadership of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Vice President of the Cambodian People's Party and many other members.
According to the working group that organized the above program, the fourth election campaign parade started from the provincial party headquarters to five districts, including: Kamchamar district, Sithor Kandal district. Svay Antor district, Pur Rieng district, Peamir district, Prey Veng city and 30 other communes around Prey Veng province with the participation of hundreds of people using more than 50 cars and 200 motorbikes.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng stated that Cambodia is reforming in all areas, the progress that Cambodia is having is under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, who led a peaceful and prosperous and prosperous Cambodia. There are school buildings and roads, electricity, clean water, people have jobs and poverty reduction.
Samdech Krala Hor stated that the election for the Cambodian People's Party will bring peace, development of the country to further progress, make the people live in abundance and have a better life. The Cambodian People's Party has a clear development plan, a rich human resource that leads Cambodia to move forward.
Samdech Krala Hom called on all people to go to the polls. Those who went to the polls were supporters of democracy, and those who supported democracy really lived in harmony with the people of the village. Those who do not go to the polls by incitement are destroyers of democracy. Then they will regret it, let our people consider.
Now the majority will go to the polls, but for those who do not go to the polls, how can we live locally with other citizens? We are not just campaigning to win or lose with other parties in our country, but there are still illegal groups calling for people to exercise their right not to vote.
We would like to emphasize that those who participated in the election were pro-democracy and those who did not vote intentionally were the destroyers of democracy at the instigation of the illegal movement. Day 29, which we have already discovered, and I hope that the vast majority of people will go to the polls every five years to fulfill their obligations.
The upcoming 6th legislative election is a free, fair, equitable and secret universal suffrage in accordance with the principles of liberal, multi-party democracy. In particular, there is no vote fraud.
