Past tax incentives and concessions include:
1: Tax preference for qualified investment projects (2003)
Through the Law Amending the Law on Investment of the Royal Government of Cambodia:
* Income tax exemption for qualified investment projects for a key period plus 3 years plus a priority period of up to 9 years
* Minimum tax exemption equal to 1% of annual turnover
* Exemption from customs duties on the import of production equipment, construction materials, raw materials, semi-finished products for production.
2: Tax Incentives for the Securities Sector (2015)
Through Sub-Decree No. 01. Dated January 05, 2015 on tax incentives in the securities sector of the Royal Government of Cambodia:
Through the Law on Finance for Management 2016, the Royal Government has introduced a tax incentive policy, abolishing the contract tax system and setting the level of taxable turnover, in which the people who do business in God. The Kingdom of Cambodia with an annual turnover of less than 250 million Riels (approximately US $ 62,500) shall not be taxed on that income.
4: Abolition of tax on means of transportation and all types of vehicles (2016)
Through the Law on Finance for Management 2016, in order to facilitate the livelihood and reduce the tax burden of small people, the Royal Government has decided to abolish the collection of taxes on all means of transportation and vehicles for motorcycles (motorcycles) and All kinds of tricycles, tractors and similar machinery, all kinds of water vehicles with up to 150 horsepower.
5: Stamp duty exemption on transfer of ownership (2016)
Pursuant to the Law on Finance for Management 2016, Proclamation No. 273 MEF dated 17 March 2016 on the Collection of Stamp Tax of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, the Royal Government of Cambodia has exempted and granted stamp duty on transfer of ownership. Between father and mother and children, husband and wife, grandparents and grandchildren.
In addition, there is a stamp duty exemption on the transfer of ownership of motorcycles, tricycles, all types of tractors and all types of vehicles up to 150 horsepower.
6: Preference for enterprises with high fiscal compliance (2016)
Through the Law on Finance for Management 2017, the Royal Government of Cambodia has waived value added tax as a non-taxable supply of some of the following supplies:
In addition, through Prakas No. 361 MEF.PrK dated April 3, 2018 of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, the Royal Government through the Ministry of Economy and Finance has issued additional incentives under the burden of the state. VAT on basic food items to facilitate people's daily lives, which include: fish, meat, eggs, animals, sugar, salt, fish sauce, all kinds of soy sauce.
8: Incentives for small and medium enterprises to register voluntarily (2017)
Pursuant to Sub-Decree No. 17 dated 07 February 2017 on Tax Incentives for Voluntary Registration of Small and Medium Enterprises, the Royal Government of Cambodia exempts income tax for two periods Year for small and medium enterprises who voluntarily register for tax.
9: Abolition of slaughter tax and raising the ceiling of taxable salaries (2018)
