To reduce the daily expenses of the people, the Royal Government intervened to reduce the price of fuel by 160 Riels per liter, while the Cambodian oil well is expected to pump by the end of 2019
(Phnom Penh): Looking at the rising price of gasoline and concerned about the living standards of the Cambodian people, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, immediately issued an intervention to solve the problem of rising gas prices for the people. .
Through the measures to help pay for the fuel price of 160 riels per liter, the Royal Government has to lose 30 million US dollars per year.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Prime Minister Hun Sen also restricted the Ministry of Commerce to work closely and monitor the price of oil and asked the oil distribution companies to carefully consider their oil sales. At this point, Samdech wants to emphasize that if the oil company buys oil to store when the price of oil is low and not sold out, should not increase immediately when the world oil price rises.
Finally, after the policy of the head of the Royal Government to help solve the price of gasoline for the people, the Ministry of Commerce, which is the staff of the Royal Government, set the price of fuel at the stations twice a month to control the price of fuel to prevent companies from importing Dare to raise the price of gasoline at will.
At the same time, the Ministry of Commerce has also taken measures against petrol stations throughout Cambodia that do not comply with the regulations of the Royal Government of Cambodia and petrol stations that do not sell enough fuel.
Promoting the introduction of the Royal Government's fuel reduction policy has been praised by the people because the reduction in fuel prices has greatly eased the burden on their livelihoods.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen once said that in just the first five months of 2018, the Royal Government has quietly subsidized to keep oil prices in Cambodia from rising by releasing nearly 83 million US dollars.
As for Cambodia's oil fields, it will not be long, or it can be said that next year, Cambodia will pump oil from its seas.
Simultaneously with the pumping of oil in Block A of the Apsara well, a large refinery project invested by a Chinese company worth more than $ 600 million is under construction in Sihanoukville, and as planned, the refinery will Construction will be completed by the end of 2019.
"The oil project in Block A, the Apsara well, will produce its oil by the end of 2019, and the Cambodian refinery project will be operational by the end of 2019," he said. "So these two projects are in line. Not only that, the oil company in Block A has been trying to liaise with the refinery to facilitate working together on oil production."
Through this social protection policy, the Armed Forces, all types of civil servants, workers, athletes, deminers and vulnerable people receive free health care in all public hospitals and hospitals. Some therapists cooperate with state institutions.
