However, the poor and vulnerable people also receive protection under various forms of social protection, such as the establishment of orphanages, centers for the disabled, maternal and child health centers, support for the poor who come to rest. Free treatment or delivery of children and the provision of education from elementary to higher education.
This policy framework plays an important role in increasing access to social assistance and social security services for public and private sector officials and the people of the informal economy. In order to achieve a better situation in providing social protection services for the Cambodian people in response to the new vision of the social protection system, the Royal Government will strive to develop programs and mechanisms to gradually move towards comprehensive coverage.
To ensure ownership of this important document, the Social Protection Policy Framework 2016-2025 has been developed under the guidance and coordination of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, and there has been extensive consultation between the relevant ministries and institutions.
In fact, the social protection policy continues to be embedded in the policy of the Cambodian People's Party for building and defending the motherland 2018-2023, with Samdech Techo Hun Sen firmly determined to continue to develop and strengthen the social protection system effectively and Sustainability that protects all people from risks without leaving any people outside the social protection system.
