(Phnom Penh): Considering and understanding the hardships of farmers who often face the problem of falling rice prices, such as lower prices from middlemen, the Royal Government led by the Cambodian People's Party has introduced many new mechanisms. To promote and promote agriculture, especially rice, to prevent the decline in rice prices.
In addition to the initial disappearance, 50,000 tons of rice warehouses and 1,500 tons of rice dryers per day in three other areas, including Kampong Thom, Prey Veng and Takeo, were also built through the Royal Government's special credit package. Two drying kilns have already been commissioned, Kampong Thom and Takeo, in early July.
Mr. Kao Thach, Director General of the Rural Development Bank, who is the staff of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and the Royal Government to work to prevent the decline in rice prices, said that the presence of rice warehouses and dryers in potential areas to collect rice. This is to ensure stable rice prices and increase rice prices for farmers to contribute to improving the lives of our Cambodian farmers.
Speaking from Kampong Thom province recently, Mr. Kao Thach confirmed that in the upcoming rice harvest season, people will not worry about the price of rice because the Royal Government of Cambodia is ready to drop loans to mills. Rice to collect rice from farmers at market price.
In addition, the Rural Development Bank always visits farmers directly to understand the difficulties and provide new ideas to help farmers develop their daily work in line with market demand. Seeing the high demand for fragrant rice in the international market, the officials of the Rural Development Bank always visit the farmers and ask the people to increase the cultivation of fragrant rice more than the kind of rice that is difficult to find in the market.
