In addition to the CPP, which has a strength of up to 250,000, marched to close the election campaign in Phnom Penh, six other political parties also marched to close the election campaign. This is according to the report of the National Election Committee in Phnom Penh.
According to the report, the six political parties are the Alliance for Democracy, the Cambodian Nationality Party, the Khmer Rouge Party, the Khmer Economic Development Party, FUNCINPEC and the Khmer United Party. According to the report, the closing ceremony of the election campaign in Phnom Penh had a total of more than 320,000 participants and included 3,670 cars, nearly 1,000 tricycles and motorbikes. More than 8,000 units.
