APSARA Authority team is repairing the Cambodia-Korea Friendship Road
(Siem Reap): Seeing the difficulties of the people traveling on the Cambodia-Korea Friendship Road (Svay Thom Road), APSARA Authority has been renovating to facilitate the traffic for the local people.
Currently, APSARA Authority is carrying out large-scale repair work on the Cambodia-Korea Friendship Road, which is located at the intersection of National Road No. 6 from Svay Thom East Market through Prey Kuy roundabout to Preah Dak Market, with a total length of 750 meters under the budget. 2018 Annual Fund. The project will repair the foundations of the damaged areas and fill in the gaps, making the section of the national road better.
He stated that in the future, APSARA Authority will take measures to restore all drainage systems on the road under the control of APSARA Authority after completing the repair of this road section. He also wished the people on both sides of the road to understand and cooperate to maintain the road for a long time.
It should be reminded that this road was originally a dirt road and was changed to a red gravel road through the project of the Korea Agency for Development and Cooperation (KOICA). In 2009, under a grant from the Republic of Korea through KOICA, the road was turned into a paved road to make it easier for people to cross. Kim Ly Heang, a law student, presents three study experiences to receive a legal scholarship
(Phnom Penh): After graduating from high school or baccalaureate, it is time to look for universities to continue your studies in order to earn a living. Every student aspires to get a scholarship in their favorite subject to help their family, and getting a university scholarship can be called the first step in success in life.
At the same time, each year, law school is a subject that is always interested in students who dream of becoming a lawyer, judge or other profession that serves the judiciary. Before getting a law scholarship, it was not an ordinary thing, and the cost of studying law is also remarkable.
If students do not receive a scholarship, the law requires them to pay around $ 400 to $ 500 per year, not including daily meals. On the other hand, if students get a scholarship, they only spend more than 10 US dollars per year, which is very successful for their family.
Kim Ly Heang, a student at the Royal University of Law and Economics, shared her experience on how to get a legal scholarship. This student is a farmer from Prey Chhor district, Kampong Cham province, who passed the high school exam in 2015 in the joint "C" and received a scholarship from the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports to study law for 4 years at the Royal University of Law and Economics.
During his law studies, due to his habit of hard work, he also recently visited the Kingdom of Thailand and the Republic of India. Currently, Ly Heang is a third year student and also one of the outstanding students in his studies.
Answer the question, what are the factors that made you pass the exam and get good grades and get a scholarship from the Ministry of Education? This outstanding student mentioned three habits when studying in high school, namely from 10th to 12th grade.
During the excavation, Kim Ly Heang said with a stern gesture:
First: Weekly school curriculum learning: Every day, he regularly goes to school according to the school's daily schedule and pays the most attention to classroom activities, such as listening to the teacher's explanations. Record every lesson. This kind of learning is very important to him.
Third, creating a daily schedule at home for yourself: Ly Heang has set a clear time, which at night divides the time to read a book and time for homework. In the morning, divide the time for reviewing lessons and memorizing lessons, problem-solving exercises. Doing so will increase your memory.
Studying is not a simple thing to get good results. Some students use their study time as just to escape work from home. Tutoring takes up to 1,000 riels an hour, and students spend a lot of extra money per day until the end of 12th grade.
According to student Kim Ly Heang, some of his friends did not pay attention to their studies because their families were wealthy. Study time should be the happiest time for them because there is no punishment from teachers, that is, teachers should take care of students, unlike state hours where students have to take care of teachers.
In particular, Ly Heang did not set a bad example because he regretted his family's money to come to school every day. And Ly Heang's struggle is a catalyst for his parents not to regret giving him money to come to school, while this struggling student rides a bike to school up to 20 kilometers to study.
For 12th grade students, before the high school diploma exam, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports always advises students who wish to apply for a scholarship from the Ministry to complete the scholarship application form every year. Priority students for the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports Scholarships include: Outstanding students, poor students, and general students.
At the same time, due to the scholarship, poor students are afraid that the Ministry will not let Ly Heang decide to apply for scholarships as general students because he thinks that he will definitely get a scholarship. And what they really hope for is that he has already strengthened and achieved the main specialization that led to the legal scholarship: Khmer History and Literature.
