Agriculture Minister: Agriculture is not only the backbone of the national economy but is playing an important role in reducing poverty
(Siem Reap): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on July 26, 2018, emphasized that agriculture is not only the backbone of the national economy and has contributed to the development of the country, but also Both have been playing an important role in reducing poverty and ensuring food security and food security.
The emphasis was made on the occasion of Mr. Veng Sakhon, accompanied by Dr. Khim Bunsong, Governor of Siem Reap Province, presiding over the Fair of Vegetable Cloth and Safety Products, organized by the General Department of Agriculture in collaboration with the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries. Siem Reap province this morning, July 26, 2018.
The above exhibition of vegetable cloth and safety products aims to show the achievements achieved through the implementation of the project on the promotion of food production, which is supported by the Royal Government of Cambodia through the Ministry of Economy and Finance on 20 budgets. $ 25 million.
The project aims to produce fragrant rice seeds and safe vegetables to supply the local market and reduce imports, and has been implemented in 11 target provinces: Takeo, Kandal, Prey Veng, Kampong Cham, Kampong Chhnang, Kampong Thom, Kampong Speu, Tbong Khmum, Pursat, Battambang and Siem Reap.
Organizing an exhibition of vegetable markets and safe vegetable products today is the achievement of the implementation of the seventh of the 11 target provinces after Kampong Cham, Kandal, Tbong Khmum, Prey Veng, Battambang and Pursat.
After making a report on the results of the project implementation and welcome by the Director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Siem Reap, Mr. Hean Vannhorn, the Royal Government delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Agriculture and Dr. Khim Bunsong, Provincial Governor.
Minister Veng Sakhon praised and highly appreciated the leadership of the General Department of Agriculture, Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, project implementation officers and farmers in the target provinces of all projects who have worked hard to implement the project. Good results as we saw today.
On that occasion, Mr. Veng Sakhon confirmed to the ceremony that "Agriculture is not only the backbone of the national economy and has contributed to the development of the country, but also has been playing an important role in reducing "Poverty ensures food security and food security."
In line with the process of implementing the Royal Government's policy of in-depth reform and strategic planning in this area, the Ministry has been preparing a vision for the development of Cambodia's agricultural sector 2019 to 2030 in order to turn Cambodian agriculture into a modern, competitive agriculture. Climate change resilience and sustainability leading to increased household incomes, prosperity and well-being of the Cambodian people.
The Minister of Agriculture continued that because Cambodia has maintained peace, stability and good development over the past twenty years, Cambodia has achieved excellent economic growth of 7% per year. Total per capita (GDP) received from $ 300 in 2000 and increased to $ 930 in 2012 and $ 1,435 in 2017.
With the increase in population, tourists and economic growth, the need for civilized and well-being people has improved, the demand for quality, safe and well-being agricultural products in the domestic market Order.
To meet this demand in recent years, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and the Ministry of Economy and Finance have pushed for the development of the first pilot food production project in Cambodia for three years. End of 2016 to 2019.
Through the joint efforts of national and provincial project implementation teams, farmers, agricultural communities and wholesalers, and the private sector in the supply of agricultural inputs and new technologies on cultivation, the preparation of key infrastructure has made the project Now we have made good progress, which has led to the creation of today's event.
The Minister further stated that it is certain that this project has contributed, in particular:
1: Production of pure rice varieties, fragrant rice to stimulate the production of rice, feed and processing to increase rice exports with the trust of foreign buyers is competitive and has the advantage of capturing the market.
2: Transforming vegetable gardening into a vegetable garden, a farm, and transforming traditional farmers into intelligent farmers and agribusinesses.
3. Meeting domestic demand instead of importing vegetable products from neighboring countries.
4: Production has a cell interface and is good in the production chain with:
Increased focus on land, water management and the use of modern cultivation technology
* Production of good agricultural products in accordance with phytosanitary rules and standards, along with packaging, storage and transportation
* Good communication between producers and buyers * Giving customers confidence in buying and eating safely and well
5: Increasing farmers' income in line with current and future economic growth
