(Ratanakkiri): Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Deputy Chairman of the Mine Authority, Mr. Thong Savun, Governor of Ratanakkiri Province, civil servants and nearly 2,000 people on July 25, 2018, held a candle lighting ceremony to donate. Monks at 36 pagodas in Ratanakkiri province.
The Vesa Candle Parade is a demonstration of the spirit of devotion to the path of Buddhism, the state religion, to become more and more prosperous, reaching 5,000 years, and another for the monks to burn and offer sacrifices. The Buddha will study the Dharma-Vinaya of the Samma Samputa on the occasion of the monk's three-month vows.
The chief priests of all pagodas welcomed the encouragement of the provincial leaders, together with the civil servants and Buddhists who brought alms and some food items to give to the monks who remember the rain in all pagodas in The province is a reflection of the care of the monks as well as the field of Buddhism.
Please note that according to the tradition of Buddhism, all monks in the Kingdom of Cambodia are invited to enter the rainy season for 3 months from the 1st day of the month of Assad.
On the day of the rainy season, a king or a royal family lights the four rainy candles every year. Of the four rainy candles, one is to be kept in the statue of the Buddha in the Royal Palace, where the Buddha image is kept. Another candle is kept in the coffin in the place of Preah Tien Vinich, which is the place where the coffin of the royal family is kept. The third candle is kept in Khan Preah Khan, the fourth candle is kept in Preah Vihear Preah Keo Morakot.
On the other hand, His Majesty required that candles be placed at pagodas in the capital and nearby pagodas in the city. That is why there are 19 royal candles. On the day of the Vesa Candle Lighting Ceremony at the Royal Palace, the priests also organized a ceremony to invite the King to Vesa.
