Authorities crack down on security guards guarding large banks disguised as National Police and Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and using illegal weapons!
(Phnom Penh): A group of people who intended to destroy security in the name of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and eight national police were arrested and sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for legal action.
Sources from the authorities said that Mr. Riel Sophin, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court will continue to interrogate a group of eight suspects in connection with the case of impersonation and use of illegal weapons on July 25.
At least eight people on July 24, 2018, were sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court by the police force of the Private Security Management Department of the Ministry of Interior after the police found that they had used The role of the National Police, the military and the illegal possession of weapons to serve as security guards in front of some major banks in Phnom Penh.
According to the report, the 12 suspects used fake national and military uniforms of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces to work as private security guards at several banks in Phnom Penh.
According to the report, the eight suspects to be sent to court include:
First, Sar Virak, a 43-year-old man who pretended to be the police chief, recruited the police to join the National Police Force and armed himself with a fake mission order to the force he selected and sent them to Go as a security guard at the above bank.
Second: Khit Sokhoeun, male, 33 years old, a mastermind disguised as a military officer, recruited the police to join the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and armed himself with a fake mission order to the force he selected and sent them to Be a security guard at the bank.
Third: Name: Loch Meng Huong, Male, 45 years old, Occupation: Security guard at the target bank.
Fourth: Name: Vorn Sophanit, Male, 32 years old, Occupation: Security guard at the target bank.
Fifth: Name: Ly Khan, Male, 38 years old, Occupation: Security guard at the target bank.
Sixth: Name: Phos Soeun, Male, 31 years old, Occupation: Security guard at the target bank.
7th: Name: Krak Teang, Male, 44 years old, Occupation: Security guard at the target bank.
8th: Name: Din Thun, Male, 39 years old, Occupation: Security guard at the target bank.
It should be noted that the police force of the Department of Private Security Management of the Ministry of Interior arrested a total of 12 suspects between 19 and 20 July 2018 at a number of major banks.
