Kandal Province CamControl Finds Dangerous Chemicals in Desserts for Sale at Koki Market, Kien Svay District
(Kandal): In order to strengthen the food safety of the people who buy and eat daily, the CamControl Branch Officer of Kandal Province, led by Mr. Ou Manrin, the CamControl Branch Manager, in cooperation with the officials of the Provincial Department of Commerce and the Market Commission, inspected the quality of goods. Currently circulating in Koki Market, Kien Svay District, Kandal Province.
Mr. Ou Manrin, President of CamControl Branch, said that during the inspection of the quality of goods on the morning of July 24, 2018, CamControl officials and officials of the Provincial Department of Commerce inspected the quality of canned food and other products in order to ensure Food safety for people to use without affecting their health.
According to the branch manager, the inspection team inspected the mobile laboratory of General Department of Camkotrol on the following items: vegetables, seafood, pickles, noodles, fruits, desserts, palm sugar and 57 samples of food. As a result, the team found a sample of the banned chemical borax in a sweet blueberry dessert.
After the discovery, the officers confiscated 2 kg and advised to stop selling and distributed food education leaflets to the vendors who sell at home around the market and the people.
