(Oddar Meanchey): The deployment of schools in rural areas is one of the priority policies of the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, to expand the scope of human resources. The descendants of the people of Oddar Meanchey province, the territory of the former Khmer Rouge battlefield in the past, are also benefiting greatly from this policy.
During a meeting with government officials in Oddar Meanchey province in 2016, Samdech Techo Hun Sen visited almost all schools to meet with teachers and students. During the visit to the school, Samdech Techo Hun Sen saw the lack of school buildings and provided many school buildings as a bond to students in this war zone.
Mr. Pich Ratana, Director of the Department of Education, Youth and Sports of Oddar Meanchey Province, said that during his visit to Oddar Meanchey Province in 2016, Samdech Techo Hun Sen provided a total of 45 school buildings with 440 rooms. The building includes an office and a dormitory building.
To date, all of these buildings have been completed, and many have allowed students to sit and study. On the morning of July 24, 2018, Mr. Kun Kim, Chairman of the Strengthening Committee in Oddar Meanchey Province, personally inspected the study of students in these luxurious and brand new school buildings.
With the study under the roof of this new school building, it is observed that all the students are full of smiles, which shows their joy and happiness for studying under these new school buildings. Through the interrogation, the students all said that they were happy and happy when they studied under the roof of the new school building, which was a gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
With fun, the students are all committed to their efforts to study and absorb knowledge to contribute to building and developing the country in return for Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Mr. Kun Kim, during the inspection of the students and the new school building, said that the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has paid high attention to training human resources. In particular, Samdech Techo has made this training a priority since the liberation of the country from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot on January 7, 1979.
On that occasion, Mr. Kun Kim urged the students to study hard to take the knowledge to participate in the development of their country and hometown to grow more.
According to the report of the Department of Education, Youth and Sports, there are a total of 412 school buildings in Oddar Meanchey province, equivalent to 1,749 classrooms. There are 91 school buildings donated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, equal to 694 rooms.
