The General Commissioner of the National Police issued five guidelines to further strengthen the control and management of explosives in companies, construction sites and businesses.
(Phnom Penh): General Chhay Sinarith, Acting National Police Commissioner of the Ministry of Interior, on July 24, 2018, issued five guidelines on further strengthening the control and control of explosives in Company, construction site and business base. This is according to the instructions that Fresh News received today.
The directive states that the issuance of this instruction is aimed at ensuring the control of explosives in companies, construction sites and businesses, in order to prevent the explosives from falling into the hands of criminals who can be used to commit crimes or terrorism. Risky, dangerous, explosive, causing chaos.
The instruction added that, especially before, during and after the upcoming general election of the 6th mandate, the General Commission of the National Police will introduce 5 points to the specialized departments and the Capital-Provincial Police. Key features include:
First, increase the dissemination of information to companies, construction sites and businesses about the law and introduce standards related to the management of ammunition thoroughly and safely.
Second, to increase the control of weapons, explosives and ammunition on the streets, in public places according to the main targets, and strengthen control measures to prevent and suppress any smuggling, import or transit in the border areas.
Third, send specialized police officers or local police to protect the location and register, control, control the entry, release, storage, explosives, especially the management of warehousing, storage and collection of explosives left over from use (to be diverted to keep Absolutely safe storage).
Fourth, instructing business owners, construction sites and businesses to temporarily suspend the transportation of ammunition and use explosives for one week before and after the 6th general election.
Fifth, the Department of Explosive Ordnance Management must monitor the above implementation and send police officers and professional officers to cooperate with the Capital and Provincial Police Commission to check the targets that are determined to be complex and take professional action by Based on the actual situation.
The following are the instructions of the Acting National Police Commissioner: China provides nearly 80,000 US dollars worth of electronic equipment to the National Institute of Diplomacy and International Relations of Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation on the morning of July 24, 2018 held a handover ceremony of electronic and IT equipment worth about 75,585 US dollars donated by the People's Republic of China through the Embassy. China in Phnom Penh to the National Institute of Diplomacy and International Relations.
The ceremony was presided over by Senior Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, and Xiong Bo, Ambassador of the People's Republic of China to Cambodia.
The handover was made at the request of the Institute to the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia to facilitate the operation of the Institute and the training of diplomats and relevant ministries and institutions of Cambodia after the Institute was officially inaugurated under the presidency of Mr. Senior Minister Prak Sokhon on February 22, 2018.
The Chinese donation now contributes to the sustainability of Senior Minister Prak Sokhon's initiative and strengthen the institution's operational capacity.
According to the Chinese Ministry of Foreign Affairs, this donation is a testament to the support of the Chinese friends in the socio-economic development of Cambodia, especially the development of human resources and infrastructure. This support contributes to the celebration of the 60th anniversary of the establishment of Cambodia-China diplomatic relations in 2018.
It should be noted that after Senior Minister Prak Sokhon took office as the new Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation in April 2016, he initiated the establishment of the Diplomatic Training Institute. This initiative was approved by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The establishment of this institute is an important part of the internal reform of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, including the restructuring of the Ministry's management structure so that the Ministry can respond to the new preparations of the Royal Government of Cambodia in the field. Foreigners are constantly changing and unpredictable, both regionally and globally.
On July 12, 2018, the Chinese Ambassador visited the Institute and gave a keynote address on the Cambodia-China relations to officials of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and relevant ministries on the occasion. 60th Anniversary of the Establishment of Cambodia-China Diplomatic Relations
