Due to the weather problem, Cambodia needs to import 30,000 tons of salt from China to supply the market!
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia will import about 30,000 tons of salt from China to supply the market, which is scheduled to take place in early October 2018.
The decision to import salt from China is due to the fact that Cambodia is facing a shortage of salt to supply demand due to unsustainable salt production due to the rainy weather.
According to the tamarind producer, the risk of salt shortage this year is due to the inability of the Salt Producers Association to produce salt due to the changeable weather this year, which means that it will not be possible to produce salt.
He added that the planned import volume of about 30,000 tons will be sufficient until the end of this year, December, but if not enough will continue to import from other countries. Currently, the association is discussing and looking for a few more countries, that is, whichever country is cheaper, the association will bring to supply in Cambodia.
He added that currently there are about 20,000 tons of salt in stock, which can be supplied until October. So far, the association has not submitted a request for a policy from the Royal Government to import salt, because now it is in the process of preparing for the election, but after the election, the association will submit to the Royal Government.
Please be reminded that every year the production and harvest of salt in Kep and Kampot takes place from September to April. For salt yield, whether it is high or low, it depends entirely on the weather, if there is a lot of rain, the salt will not be high.
