(Kandal): Kandal Provincial Court Investigating Judge Nguon Vuthy has ordered the detention of three defendants, one of whom is the deputy chief of Prek Chrov village, who falsified public documents to encroach on your land. Prek Chrov village, Roka Kong 2 commune, Muk Kampoul district, Kandal province.
According to an official of Kandal Provincial Court, speaking to Fresh News this morning, July 24, 2018, the court decided to detain the three defendants, imprison each of them for 6 years and compensate 20 victims. Million Riels. The decision follows the questioning of one of the accused, who was remanded in custody at Kandal Provincial Prison.
According to the source, the three accused are: Chuob Phat, male, 47 years old, and Im Saroeun, female, 50 years old, both married and living in Prek Chrov village, Roka Kong commune. Second, Muk Kampoul district, Kandal province, and third: Kong Duong, male, 59 years old, deputy village chief, living in Prek Chrey village, Roka Kong commune, second, Muk Kampoul district, Kandal province.
According to the minutes of the Kandal Provincial Prosecutor's Office, on June 7, 2016, Mr. Chhay Ly Heang, an accompanying clerk, questioned Im Saroeun in detail and the suspect confessed. Gave Kong Duong $ 20 to help him issue a certificate of land ownership.
On August 21, 2011, Kong Duong, who served as the deputy chief of Prek Chrov village, issued a land certificate by forging the fingerprints of witnesses An Chanthol and Bou Kim. On the other hand, Mr. Kong Duong, the deputy village chief, pretended to be the village chief and signed the title deed, which is an offense of falsifying public documents under Articles 44 and 124 of the Penal Code.
It should be noted that the three defendants conspired to falsify public documents and encroach on the access road to the houses of the villagers by moving the houses on the road in order to encroach on the public road. Its.
