(Kampot): Cambodia was recently affected by a tropical monsoon in the Pacific Ocean, causing heavy rainfall throughout the country, with heavy rains almost everywhere and causing severe flooding in some places. . In fact, since July, the Kamchay River has been subjected to a series of heavy rains, with alarming water levels reaching 1884.6 cubic meters per second (1884.6 m³ / s).
Every day, Kamchay Hydropower Company sends water status report several times to Kampot Provincial Hall to be prepared in advance. At the same time, the flood protection capacity of Kamchay Hydropower Station was used. Currently, the maximum discharge level is only 1258.2m³ / s and the flood prevention capacity is 4361.0 million m³, which reduces the Effectively affect the flooding of villages along the downstream.
Please be informed that Kamchay Hydropower Project is a project to generate electricity and have the ability to prevent floods, irrigate and even out the seasonal water flow, also improve the water condition of the downstream area.
Since its official opening, it has provided electricity to Cambodia and irrigated agricultural lands along downstream streams and prevented floods, as well as contributed to many beneficial humanitarian work. The society receives good evaluation from the local authorities and the people. Thailand: Nearly "10 million pills" of drugs were seized by the police on the outskirts of Bangkok!
