(Phnom Penh): Cambodia Airways launched its first international flight direct from Phnom Penh to Macau on Sunday, July 22, 2018.
To make this international flight operation a success and easy, Cambodia Airways has launched flights to Macau four times a week, every Tuesday, Wednesday, Friday and Sunday.
The first international flight of Cambodia Airways KR511 took off at 10:45 am from Phnom Penh International Airport and landed at Macau International Airport at 14:05.
Flight KR512 will return from Macau at 21:40 and will land at Phnom Penh International Airport at 23:25. Cambodia Airways decided to fly to Macau because Cambodia Airways also has a market support from partner travel agencies along with many needs from there.
Most of the tourists are Chinese from various cities and provinces of China, passing through Macau before coming to Cambodia. For this reason, Cambodia Airways decided to choose the first international flight to this city.
In addition to the launch of Macau, Cambodia Airways will continue to operate flights to Hong Kong, Taiwan, South Korea, Japan, as well as China and other countries in Southeast Asia, including Thailand, Singapore and the Philippines. For the next project, the company will expand its flights to European countries and Australia.
In addition, the leaders of Cambodia and Macau have met in recent months to discuss expanding tourism and trade cooperation between Cambodia and Macau, China, and to encourage investment. In the aviation sector, there will be direct flights between Macau and Cambodia.
Cambodia Airways hopes that this first international flight will accelerate the development of Cambodia, both now and in the future, as Cambodia is an attractive tourist destination for both national and international visitors and has natural resources. Rich as well as national culture and many interesting prehistoric sites. NASA will launch a vehicle to study as close to the sun as ever!
