It is also nicknamed the "Land of 365 Beaches" due to the many beaches surrounding the islands. The administration of the language and culture of the country was influenced by the British Empire, as the country was under British rule and gained sovereignty on November 1, 1981.
Today, it remains a member of the British Empire, with Queen Elizabeth II as head of state. Antigua is the largest of the two islands and is easily accessible by direct flights from the United Kingdom, the United States and Canada.
Antigua and its flat terrain are best suited for tobacco, cotton and ginger crops. Today, with the independence of the United Kingdom, Antigua's main sectors are tourism and tourism-related services, which account for more than 60% of GDP.
Antigua, as well as other Caribbean countries, has experienced a challenging economic climate in recent years. The government itself has developed and implemented a number of private and public initiatives to stabilize and restructure the economy.
Antigua's investment citizenship program is divided into three categories, with investors and their families being able to choose according to their needs, including:
* Donation to the National Development Fund in the minimum amount of approximately USD 100,000 per application
* $ 200,000 investment in a government-recognized real estate project
* Minimum investment of US $ 1.5 billion directly into any legitimate business.
This Tamarind Hill project offers a beautiful collection of villas designed in the perfect Caribbean style.
