(Tbong Khmum): Mr. Vong Soth, Chairman of Ponhea Krek District, Tbong Khmum Province and Cheach Commune, Kamchay Mear District, Prey Veng Province, on July 22, 2018, led members of the Cambodian People's Party to launch the 6th National Assembly Election Campaign. Of the Cambodian People's Party in 8 communes in Ponhea Krek district, Tbong Khmum province and 1 commune in Kamchay Mear district, Prey Veng province, with more than 2,000 members.
In the opening ceremony of the campaign of the Cambodian People's Party started at 07:30 in the morning with the speech of Mr. Vong Soth, Chairman of the Task Force for Ponhea Krek District, Tbong Khmum Province and Cheach Commune, Kamchay Mear District, Prey Veng Province. The campaign marched from Anlong Chrey village, Kak commune, Ponhea Krek district, divided into two shifts for the march.
The first turn starts at 7:30 am, leaving Kak commune, Ponhea Krek district, led by Mr. Vong Soth, departing along National Road 8 to the right corner in 3 turns, turn right through Cheach commune, Kamchay Mear district and continue to Dauntei commune and Kandol Chrum commune arrives at National Road 7 and turns right until Stung Market, then turns left towards Popel commune, then turns back to National Road 7 and continues towards Ponhea Krek District Party Office to rest.
As for the second turn, at 2 pm, Mr. Vong Soth took the members from Ponhea Krek District Party Department to continue on National Road 7 to cross Veal Mlou commune and then continue to Krek commune before returning to meet with Trapeang Phlong commune to end the full day march.
It should be noted that 20 political parties competed in the 6th legislative election, and for the third campaign on the morning of July 22, five parties were seen campaigning.
On the opening day of the election campaign on July 7, 2018, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Cambodian People's Party has led the country through many difficult stages that have made Cambodia achieve a change of face. The most proud new.
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, who has been the Prime Minister of Cambodia for about 33 years, also highlighted the great achievements of the nation over the last two decades. Major achievements include:
1. More than 20 years ago, Cambodia was the host country of the United Nations Blue Hat soldiers to carry out peacekeeping operations in this miserable, conflict-ridden territory. Cambodia has now become the country that sends its troops to wear blue hats to participate in UN peacekeeping operations in some of the world's hotspots.
2. Cambodia, formerly known as the Killing Fields, an insecure area, a landmine that everyone feared, has now become a "Peace Island" and a popular tourist destination in Southeast Asia. Millions a year.
3. Cambodia, formerly known for its use of weapons to seize power and to change governments, has now become a country that adheres to the principles of liberal, multi-party democracy through regular elections. Free, fair and just so that the people can elect their representatives to lead the country as a rule of law, unwavering respect for the rule of law and a sovereign state with complete independence and territorial integrity.
4. Cambodia, formerly a country under siege and isolation, both politically and economically, has now become a country that is actively integrating itself with equal rights and equality in all regional and international affairs.
Damascus: Russia and France for the first time have sent large amounts of humanitarian aid to the town of Ghouta, near the southwestern Syrian capital Damascus, after the city was seized by Syrian government forces. Back last April. This is according to a quote from the Chinese newspaper CGTN on Sunday evening, July 22, 2018.
A Russian military transport plane carrying about 50 tons of humanitarian aid and medicine has arrived in Syria after leaving the central French city of Chateauroux, according to a statement from the Russian Defense Ministry.
The aid, which includes medicine, medical equipment, clothing and temporary tents, will be delivered to the people of Ghouta, who have just been liberated by government forces after five years of war.
