Minister of Water Resources led a team of experts to close a large dragon hole in the Stung Stung Prek Tnaot Dam overnight to prevent leaks
(Phnom Penh): After receiving the news that the Stung Prek Tnaot delta dam was flooded and formed a large dragon hole at the bottom under the dam, then Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, led a team of officials to control the machinery to close the dragon hole. In the middle of the night on July 21 to ensure the safety of the people in Dangkor district as well as in Phnom Penh.
The Stung Prek Tnaot delta dam is located in Sangkat Tien, Khan Dangkor, and tonight's intervention was carried out in a timely manner with care for the safety of the people, not to threaten the safety of the people. That.
Mr. Chan Yutha, spokesman for the Ministry of Water Resources, said that the operation will continue until this morning to increase the size and compression of the Stung Prek Tnaot dam to be stronger than before to ensure the safety of the people. Long lasting and highly effective.
The spokesman also confirmed that the flood situation in the upper part of Stung Prek Tnaot, which extends from Kampong Speu province, is also declining, so people living near the river and the lower part of Stung Prek Tnaot is no longer a threat from floods.
However, the Ministry of Water Resources and authorities are still urging people across the country to be vigilant in protecting themselves and their property from the dangers caused by rain, thunder, lightning or other natural phenomena in This rainy season all together.
On the morning of July 22, 2018, the Minister continued to lead professional officers to help prevent this dragon hole from expanding and occurring elsewhere.
