Expert: Improper treatment of sports injuries can lead to chronic illness and disability, so get the right treatment
(Phnom Penh): Currently, all kinds of sports are gaining a lot of attention, especially among young people, both experts and ordinary athletes, because playing sports can bring peace and good health for everyone, but Playing sports can be dangerous at any time, even with proper training.
However, for the treatment of injuries due to improper sports, experts in the treatment of injuries due to sports claim that can cause two major dangers: first: causing chronic, incurable disease and second: can Disables the victim for life. Therefore, experts encourage victims to seek treatment or see a specialist for proper treatment.
Seeing these dangerous factors, there is a topic "Treatment of injuries due to sports" that Royal Hospital Phnom Penh organized a workshop on the morning of July 21, 2018 to share experiences as well as Provide some necessary advice to the Cambodian public and athletes.
He also advised that if an athlete had an accident, he should stop playing immediately and seek professional help to treat or end the accident so that the old injury does not recur.
Speaking at the seminar, Mr. Narin Tharabun Chungcharoen, Director of Royal Phnom Penh Hospital, stated that if you are injured due to sports, you can come to Royal Phnom Penh Hospital for consultation because Royal Phnom Penh Hospital has clear experts for treatment. In this case, the hospital also cooperates with the Olympic Committee, other football associations to save them in time.
The director of the hospital also added that the Royal Phnom Penh Hospital has enough medical equipment to be ready for rescue as well as surgery for sports injuries. The Royal Hospital is also accredited by FIFA, and every two years, FIFA regularly inspects the equipment.
