The Ministry of Transport and the General Department of Road Transport continue the campaign to get driver's licenses for truck drivers in the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone.
(Preah Sihanouk): The National Social Security Fund (NSSF) has assigned the Road Traffic Safety Working Group for the Protection of Workers (OHPF) in collaboration with the General Department of Road Transport of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport. Continuing the campaign to organize driver's license examinations for truck drivers for workers who do not have an automated driver's license (Online) for truck drivers located in the Sihanoukville Economic Zone.
The driving test for drivers of trucks carrying workers was held on July 20, 2018, the main purpose is for all drivers of workers to have a driver's license and have a driver's license in accordance with the category. Vehicles transporting workers as required by law.
The driving test campaign was organized with a total of 67 participants, including 26 unlicensed drivers and 41 non-compliant drivers (Category D). ). This exam procedure includes both theoretical and direct driving tests.
This driver's license exam is organized and controlled by the online computer operating system of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, which requires all driver's license applicants to follow the instructions correctly.
According to the report of the second quarter of 2018 of the working group, the number of traffic accidents on workers has decreased by 10% compared to the first quarter of 2018. There were 8 cases of traffic accidents caused by workers' trucks.
The working group of the Ministry of Transport and the Ministry of Transport will cooperate with the General Department of Transportation to conduct training, examination and provide driver's licenses to the drivers of trucks carrying workers so that they have a driver's license in accordance with the type of vehicle prescribed by law. All in accordance with the high recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The working group also called on all truck drivers to: * Obey traffic laws strictly * Do not overload workers * Inspect vehicles before leaving to transport workers * Check the car regularly * Exam to get a driver's license in accordance with the type of vehicle * Participate in the training of the working group on the road traffic law * In particular, adhere to the 10 ethics of the National Road Safety Commission.
