(Phnom Penh): A senior official of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has expressed concern about the threat of the Prek Tnaot River in Dangkor district in Phnom Penh and Kandal Stung district, Kandal province, if the water level continues to rise and there is no timely intervention.
Faced with this problem, on the afternoon of July 20, 2018, the Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, Mr. Lim Kean Hor, led the technical officers and took the machinery to prevent the Stung Prek Tnaot Dam in Kampong Speu Province to close the leak ) That happened there.
Chan Yutha, director of the cabinet and spokesman for the Ministry of Water Resources, confirmed that "at this time, the Minister has led a technical team and machinery to prevent leaks occurring at the Stung Prek Tnaot Dam and pour more soil to avoid impact. "Worse."
The senior official confirmed that the water level of Stung Prek Tnaot in the upper part has improved, except in the lower part, but according to the assessment of the Minister of Water Resources, if we can prevent within 10 to 12 hours. In the future, there will be no more concerns about the threat of flooding in Dangkor district of Phnom Penh and Kandal Stung district, Kandal province.
As an additional measure, the minister ordered the sluice gates to be lowered to reduce rising water levels at the bottom.
