Senior Minister Sun Chanthol announces that he will improve the section of National Road No. 4 between km 115-116 so that it does not flood like now
(Preah Sihanouk): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, has announced that he will upgrade National Road No. 4 between km 115-116 in Stung Samrong village, O'Bak Rotes commune, Kampong Seila district, Preah Sihanouk province. Than now.
The announcement of the Senior Minister was made during his visit to inspect the flood situation on National Road 4 this morning, July 20, 2018. Inspection of the flood situation on this road was also attended by the Governor of Kampong Speu, Mr. Vy Samnang and the Governor of Sihanoukville, Mr. Yon Min.
Mr. Sun Chanthol pointed out that the section of National Road No. 4 between km 115-116 in Stung Samrong village, O'Bak Rotes commune, Kampong Seila district, Preah Sihanouk province is always flooded during the rainy season due to the low geography here. . Therefore, to solve this problem, he will raise the road to this place higher than now, as well as build a bridge to open the water to flow through this place.
Please note that National Road No. 4 has been loaned by the World Bank about 110 million US dollars to repair and rehabilitate this road. The road will be repaired and rebuilt during 2019, with the width of the road widening from 7 meters to 11 meters.
