The Royal Government handed over 1565 plots of land to the people on the land of the former National Radio in Sangkat Stung Meanchey 2, this morning, the Governor of Phnom Penh handed over to the people
(Phnom Penh): Residents of Damnak Thom 1 and Russey 3 villages, Sangkat Stung Meanchey 2, Khan Meanchey, nearly 2,000 families, equal to 1565 plots of land, were given land titles by the Royal Government after living without a title deed. The announcement was made on the morning of July 20, 2018 at Wat Non Mony, Sangkat Steung Meanchey 2, Khan Meanchey, presided over by Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh.
Mr. Sarin Vanna, Director of the Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs of Phnom Penh, said that this land was originally state land, seeing that the people did not have a title deed, the Royal Government also gave and registered. Systematic land, in which 1565 plots of land were provided to the people.
He also said that the posting of data on the newly registered plots now aims for all landowners to check the name of the landowner, the spelling, the type of property and the size of the land. If you do not understand or doubt the data related to your plot, you have the right to ask the official to explain the contents of the plot data to inform the Administrative Committee of all its objections to review and correct.
This posting lasts for 15 days from July 20 to August 11, 2018, regardless of Saturday, Sunday or holidays.
On that occasion, Mr. Khuong Sreng urged local officials to work on Saturdays and Sundays to hand over to the people quickly to avoid long-term recurrence. He continued that we have done our work for the people and still you have to help us, you want to celebrate, and we want to celebrate. So do not forget to go to the polls on July 29, 2018.
