Khmer Breweries Builds Football Schedule for Preah Sisowath High School Nearing Completion
(Phnom Penh): The construction of the football table sponsored by Khmer Breweries for Preah Sisowath High School is nearing completion, and the sponsorship of the football star is part of the Khmer Breweries' "Clean School" campaign. Carola flags, concrete roads and football stars have already been built for some schools.
Dr. Im Sothearith, Communications Director of Khmer Breweries, said, "Participating in the renovation of the school not only enhances the beauty of the school, but also makes the nursery a comfortable place for students. When the school is clean, the students want to come to school more and more. After school, you have a football table that can play more sports, so they study well and healthy.
Preah Sisowath High School football table has a standard size for 11 players per side with two main poles and can be divided into three small tables for games or training with six small poles. The football table is covered with artificial grass, surrounded by concrete canals to avoid flooding, equipped with modern lighting, can play football at night, especially with a net around to prevent the ball from falling out.
In the past, the company has helped to improve the infrastructure on the campus of Chea Sim Samaki High School, Tuol Ampil High School and Dangkor Primary School.
