(Preah Sihanouk): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, this morning, July 20, 2018, led officials as well as provincial authorities to inspect National Road No. 4, which was flooded due to heavy rains. Today.
During his visit to inspect the road this morning, Mr. Sun Chanthol also met with Mr. Hun Many, Member of Parliament for Kampong Speu, Mr. Vy Samnang, Governor of Kampong Speu, as well as relevant officials in Kampong Speu.
The meeting also discussed the impact on people affected by the floods and heard reports on the impact on road and bridge infrastructure in the province.
Mr. Vy Samnang said that the recent floods have caused many roads and bridges, while the agricultural crops of the people in Kampong Speu province have not been evaluated yet. However, the floods did not endanger the lives of the people, the authorities launched an operation to evacuate people to safety in time.
Mr. Vy Samnang also claimed that the modernization of information technology systems is also a part of helping to solve flood problems in a timely and effective manner. He said that due to the modernization of information technology, the dissemination of flood problems to the people was faster and the measures to evacuate and release water were also timely.
Mr. Hun Many said that due to the frequent floods in Kampong province, measures to evacuate and rescue people were timely. However, he claimed that the rescue efforts continued to ensure that no one was killed in the floods.
Regarding the road, Mr. Sun Chanthol said that this section of National Road No. 4 at km 116 is flooded almost every year, so the team is studying to improve the road as well as build a bridge at some point to open the water. Let it flow fast.
The minister said the World Bank had provided about $ 110 million in loans for the rehabilitation of National Road 4, with the widening of the road from 7 meters to 11 meters. In addition, will also learn about flood relief.
Please note that during this road inspection this morning, in addition to inspecting the section of National Road No. 4, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol will also inspect National Road No. 3, No. 33, No. 31 and 41. These roads were badly damaged after heavy traffic and transportation after National Road 4 was flooded. INNOTALITY Annual Work Visit to Phnom Penh
