(Phnom Penh): Trains were a popular means of transportation during the French colonial period, as well as during the Reastr Niyum War and during the 1980s and 2000s for Cambodians traveling from Phnom Penh to Banteay Meanchey or from Phnom Penh to Go to Sihanoukville because at that time the Cambodians did not have many means of transportation. However, since 2006, the train has not been operational due to the deterioration of the railway.
Recently, the railway from Phnom Penh to Sihanoukville was put into operation, and in 2018, the railway north of Phnom Penh, namely the railway from Phnom Penh to Poipet, Banteay Meanchey province, was also reopened. The launch of the Phnom Penh-Poipet railway has made the people who used the railway in the past reminisce about this railway line.
Nowadays, due to the variety of means of transportation, not many Cambodians choose to travel by train to travel to Sihanoukville or to Battambang, Banteay Meanchey or Poipet. That.
On July 19, 2018, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, wished to inspire interest in Cambodia's railways and to recognize the Royal Government's efforts to rehabilitate the railways. Bring about 600 locals in Koh Thom to experience the taste of train travel from Phnom Penh to Kampong Chhnang.
With their first train trip, they were observed to show a happy smile on their faces. Remarkably, on each train, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol played the guitar and sang some commemorative songs in Koh Thom district, a new song that made the atmosphere of the trip even more enjoyable and refreshing. .
Most of the people from Koh Thom never knew about traveling by train. Through this first train trip, they were thrilled mixed with a lot of fun.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol told reporters that the train tour for the residents of Koh Thom, his hometown, is to let people know about the train and want to inspire them. Support train travel, which is an important means of transportation in Cambodia.
In addition, the people of Koh Thom want to see the progress of the country and the efforts of the Royal Government in the development of the country as well as the rehabilitation of Cambodia's railways.
