Court issues arrest warrant for 3 Chinese in connection with attempted murder of Cambodian woman in Por Sen Chey district
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of July 19, 2018, Mr. Bunthy, the Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, ordered the detention of three Chinese nationals in the case of attempted murder of a Cambodian woman in Po Sen Chey district and sent him to PJ prison. Wait for the council to open the trial later.
The judge's decision comes after Deputy Prosecutor Sin Vir: charged the three Chinese men with "attempted murder" under Articles 27 and 199 of the Penal Code.
According to the authorities, before the incident, the three Chinese men took a sharp metal and drove a car with a license plate to chase the victim while she was driving to eat. A coffee shop in Por Sen Chey district.
After the violence, the victim was taken to the rescue, while the car was almost completely damaged. According to the authorities, this case happened at 11:45 am on July 13, 2018 in front of Test Cafe, Veng Sreng Street, Choam Chao 2 Village, Sangkat Choam Chao 2, Khan Por Sen Chey.
Before the incident, the victim was driving with another woman, intending to eat at the test cafe, and just the victim got out of the car, suddenly a group of two armed men driving a car came to act. Hit the victim, causing her to fall, seriously injuring her, and hit the victim's car, causing the glass to shatter.
After the action, the assailants drove the car and fled. The authorities of Po Sen Chey district intervened and chased the perpetrators until they reached the Russian Federation Road in front of Pochentong Airport. And two pieces of steel and have built a case to be sent to court according to legal procedures.
