Free public bus travel for bus card users provided by Wing or Wing account card!
(Phnom Penh): Wing Specialized Bank has announced that it will not charge for public transportation in Phnom Penh for customers who use the bus card provided by Wing or Wing account card from today until the end of July 2018.
To receive this offer, customers must have one of the two cards for the tabs on the electronic machines fitted to the 155 buses. The public bus card provided by Wing has two options for customers.
The blue card is for students, the elderly, monks, factory workers, the disabled and children under 1 meter tall, which customers can ride 180 times for free. The blue card costs 4,000 Riel, which customers can top up for free at all bus stations.
The green card is for general customers. This card costs 10,000 Riel and has 6,000 Riel in travel card, which customers can top up at any Wing Agent anywhere. You can open a bus pass throughout the public bus station in just a few minutes.
For customers with a Wing account card, they can go to the Wing agent, public bus station or Wing Specialized Bank head office to activate the bus billing system. Public bus card is a new technology under the collaboration between Wing Specialized Bank and Phnom Penh Capital Hall Administration, which was launched on June 19.
