Minister of Agriculture: The ongoing "Food Production Promotion" project has helped boost the production of fragrant rice and safe vegetables to supply the local market and reduce imports.
(Battambang): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on July 19, 2018, confirmed that the General Department of Agriculture has been implementing a project to promote food production, which has received financial support. $ 20.25 million from the Royal Government of Cambodia through the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
The Minister of Agriculture added that the project aims to produce fragrant rice seeds and safe vegetables to supply the local market to reduce imports by implementing in 11 target provinces: Takeo, Kandal, Prey Veng, Kampong Cham, Kampong Chhnang, Kampong Thom, Kampong Speu, Tbong Khmum, Pursat, Battambang and Siem Reap Province.
This statement was made on the occasion of Mr. Veng Sakhon presiding over the cloth market exhibition in Battambang provincial town, organized by the General Department in collaboration with the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Battambang province on the morning of July 19. This 2018.
The exhibition in Battambang above was also attended by Mr. Hoeung Sakun, Deputy Governor, Ministry leaders, together with Mr. and Mrs. civil servants, students, traders, farmers, vegetable farmers, community safe vegetable production, a total of about 200 people. .
Interested in this opportunity, Mr. Deputy Governor, please support because the project has helped to promote and increase the production of vegetables and safe products, supply to the local market, reduce imports, ensure public health.
On this occasion, the Minister of Agriculture commended the leadership of the General Department of Agriculture, Provincial Department of Agriculture, project implementation officers who worked hard to implement the project to achieve good results, especially thank the Royal Government for its support. The budget to implement this project focuses on the production of fragrant rice seeds and safe vegetable production.
At the same time, Mr. Veng Sakhon also set out 4 main principles to reduce the import of vegetables and ensure income for small and medium farmers to participate in promoting economic growth and especially to develop fruit and vegetable production to ensure public health. Employment for local people to reduce poverty and migration through:
1: Change the direction of production from production for family consumption to production for agribusiness, change the production of vegetables in the garden to production in the field.
2: Incorporate production techniques such as seed selection, application of fertilizers, drip irrigation systems, net houses to reduce risks, increase production productivity on the same land, ensure quality and safety of vegetables through good agricultural practices (GAP)
3. Improve the production line according to the plan or according to the specific program according to the market demand by farming according to the contract
4: In addition to production, manufacturers must consider and examine the possibility of packaging, storage, processing and delivery of products to market.
He added that both production mechanisms and production technical principles have been actively contributing to the development of the agricultural sector development policy 2019-2030, which is to develop Cambodia's agricultural sector to modern agriculture, agricultural mechanization, resource competition and climate change. .
To ensure accuracy, fairness, transparency and competitiveness, the Minister advised the General Department of Agriculture to do its utmost to provide quality and safety certification of vegetables, fruits and other products to community producers and farm owners.
A girl drowned in a pool while her parents were busy working outside, leaving her with her 70-year-old grandmother
(Preah Vihear): Parents almost fainted after realizing that their lovely little daughter was tragically drowned after they were busy working outside the home, sending their little ones This is for the old grandmother to see. The incident happened at 4:30 pm on July 18, 2018 in Thkeng village, Quick commune, Rovieng district, Preah Vihear province.
Colonel Say Det, Rovieng District Police Inspector, said this morning, July 19, 2018, that before the incident, the father, a police officer, went to work as usual at the station, while the mother, a teacher, went out to transplant rice. In the field, by sending the little girl victim to the grandmother, who is over 70 years old.
The colonel said that while the grandmother was not interested in her grandson, she disappeared for a while, making him try to find her by visiting her neighbor's house. When she could not be found, the neighbors were shocked to find the little girl drowning in the pool, and she died in the most shocking way.
He added that the pool where the little girl drowned was about seven feet high, filled with rainwater. After examining the body, the authorities handed over the family to perform the traditional ceremony.
Rovieng District Police Inspector said that the little girl who died was named Tum Chakrya, a 2-year-old girl. With the loss of his beloved daughter and to mourn the loss, Mr. Hor Bun Hour, Governor of Rovieng District, led the district team to bring 785,000 Riels to mourn.
