The destruction of all these games is to continue to promote the implementation of safe village-neighborhood policy. And this is not the first time that the Chbar Ampov District Unity Command has cracked down on Tu Game, which is a source of crime in the district.
According to the Chbar Ampov district governor, who led the force in cracking down on and confiscating the game consoles in the past, the Chbar Ampov district authorities cracked down on and confiscated the game consoles from the communes.
The district governor continued that the crackdown on gambling places, especially this shooting game, because it is a source of gambling that has affected the students' education, making them avoid learning from school, and these games. A source of other crimes such as theft and robbery.
Separately, the owner of the location was confirmed by the governor that the district has educated and advised them not to run this kind of business anymore because it is contrary to the policy of the Royal Government on village-sangkat policy. It is safe to not gamble locally and the owners have signed a contract with the authorities to stop this business.
