(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, this morning, July 19, 2018, brought a total of 500 people from Koh Thom district, Kandal province to take the train from Phnom Penh to Kampong Chhnang province.
The preparation of the people of Koh Thom to travel by train in order to promote support for travel by train north of Phnom Penh (Phnom Penh-Poipet), which the Royal Government of Cambodia was completely reconnected on July 4. 2018 has passed after failing to operate for many years.
Bringing people on the train also wants to show people the government's efforts to restore Cambodia's rail system, which was disrupted and destroyed during the war. In addition, people in Koh Thom want to know the taste of train travel, most of them have never traveled by train.
The section of railway from Poipet to Phnom Penh was completely rehabilitated and reopened on July 4, 2018. The rehabilitation of the railway from Phnom Penh to Poipet, Banteay Meanchey province has cost about 96.6 million US dollars. Of that, about $ 13 million belongs to the Asian Development Bank and another $ 83.6 million is from the Royal Government.
