(Svay Rieng): Mr. Men Vibol, Governor of Svay Rieng Province, on the morning of July 19, 2018, attended the inauguration of the OWSO and the Svay Rieng Provincial People's Office, which are new achievements of the Royal Government in Reform decentralization and deconcentration by bringing services closer to the people.
The ceremony was presided over by the Deputy Governor, Mr. and Mrs. Member of Provincial Council, Director - Deputy Director of Provincial Administration, representatives of the three forces, heads of departments and units around the province, governors and all relevant officials. In the single exit unit and the provincial citizen office.
Mr. Men Vibol stated that the establishment of the One-Stop-Shop and the Provincial People's Office is an achievement that confirms the new success of the Royal Government in the reform of decentralization and deconcentration by Bring services closer to the people by delegating power to sub-national administrations.
He said that these two mechanisms will make the provision of administrative services to the people better, more accurate, quality, efficiency, efficiency, transparency and accountability, as well as providing high trust to the people who receive services and reflect. See the attention to promote good governance of public services as well as promote the collection of revenue into the national budget and eliminate the collection of fees in excess of the law.
At the same time, the provincial governor instructed the chairman, deputy chairman and front-line officers of the OWSOs to do their best to fulfill their duties and responsibilities in accordance with laws and regulations, in particular. There must be cooperation and solidarity between all relevant units so that the unit can run smoothly, ensure the provision of services to the people correctly and quickly, without causing congestion in providing services.
He also requested all relevant departments to help promote and encourage people to receive services through the OWSO mechanism, without having to receive applications for services at the department after the unit opened. To be officially launched.
