WASHINGTON (Reuters) - U.S. researchers at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT) say the amount of diamonds buried beneath the surface is 1,000 times higher than estimated, but they are likely to increase. There is no chance of seeing the sun or appearing in jewelry stores. This is according to a quote from the Chinese newspaper CGTN in the morning of Thursday, July 19, 2018.
These naturally occurring treasures are at depths that have never been drilled before, at a depth of about 145 to 240 kilometers above the surface of our planet. . Researchers at MIT say that although we could not get the diamonds out, they were 1,000 times larger than we had ever imagined. .
The discovery was made using technology that analyzes how sound waves travel through the earth's surface. Scientists have discovered an enormous amount of this treasure in a type of rock called Cratonic, which looks like a mountain that sinks from the top to the Earth's core.
