Ministry of Commerce and Battambang provincial authorities are seeking a solution to the fall in corn prices along the Cambodian-Thai border
(Battambang): The Ministry of Commerce, Battambang Provincial Administration and corn collectors on the afternoon of July 17, 2018 attended a meeting to find solutions to the price of corn prices in the Cambodian-Thai border districts.
In this regard, the Chamber of Commerce insures the kiln, while the traders collect the seeds as a guarantor to buy, store and resell to find a market for Cambodian farmers no longer have to worry.
The meeting was held in the presence of Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Battambang, Mr. Kith Pheara, Director of the Department of Trade Policy and Mr. Oknha Phu Puy, President of the Provincial Chamber of Commerce, with the participation of the Director of the Provincial Department of Commerce. Buy agricultural products from Sampov Loun district, Phnom Proek district, some participants.
Ms. Ros Manmuy, Member of the Provincial Chamber of Commerce and Vice President of the Cassava Association of Sampov Loun District, described the difficulties of farmers in the past in collecting corn kernels. Sell to Silo in a hurry, forcing money to grow twice a year.
She added that sometimes collectors have a hard time because the corn is still young, which is why the price of corn is so low at 3.6 baht per kilogram and makes them unhappy to sell at that price. As for the export of traders, Thai traders despise the low price, this is a problem.
She requested the Ministry of Commerce and the provincial administration to help find a solution to this market and price issue.
Mr. Oknha Phu Puy said that in order to strengthen the corn market of farmers in the border areas in the future, all corn farmers must first organize a clear community as a responsible person to coordinate in Collecting corn from farmers is easy, especially with warehouses for quality corn dryers, with clear deadlines, which communities sell before or after, do not overlap and have good order, making the farm more expensive.
He added that the storage of dryers and money for collection is no longer a problem, so we built a warehouse of dry rice, which we did in Battambang recently.
Mr. Kith Phara suggested that he fully agreed with the opinion of Mr. Phu Puy by organizing a clear community farmers to support the collection of corn in time to serve our farmers do not face the problem of corn market. The next day. "In today's meeting, we are not only talking about corn, but also potatoes, beans and other crops," he said.
Mr. Nguon Rattanak said that the working group that met today will go to study the farmers' corn market as well as organize our farmers as a community and decided to go directly to the target point tomorrow morning. In order to solve the problem from the next day, let's solve the agricultural market for our people to be successful in the future as well.
Please be informed that last week, the people as well as traders exporting corn to Thailand asked the leaders of the Ministry of Commerce and Battambang provincial authorities to help negotiate with the Thai side in Sa Kaeo to make both corn. The bases of our Khmer farmers can be imported through the mouths of Phnom Dey (Khmer) and Khao Din (Thailand) without having to peel only the seeds.
Citizens and traders say that allowing Cambodian farmers to export their corn by shelling only makes it impossible for our people to use their agricultural products to the best of their ability. Peel a squash, grate it and squeeze the juice.
The exporters confirmed that the request was only to be implemented like the mouth of O'Anlok in Battambang province, while the Thai side was the gate of Suon Som in Chanthaburi province, Thailand, which allowed our Cambodian corn to enter both the grain and the core. Once.
