Kampong Speu Provincial Governor Orders the Demolition of Illegal Buildings on the Indian Reservoir (Lake Tasal) and Confiscates Many Construction Materials
(Kampong Speu): Coalition forces led by Mr. Prum Vannak, Deputy Governor of Kampong Speu Province, in cooperation with Deputy Prosecutor Ou Phat, on the morning of July 17, 2018, under the strict order of Mr. Vy Samnang, Governor of Kampong Speu Province, demolished disrespectful buildings. A law on the Indus Reservoir area (Boeung Tasal) by confiscating a lot of construction materials.
An illegal structure was found to be stolen for the purpose of a restaurant in O'Ancha village, Ta Sal commune, Oral district, Kampong Speu province, found on July 13, 2018 on state land, reservoir area and development project Of the state.
Mr. Prum Vannak stated that at the above village-commune point, according to the inspection, there was indeed illegal construction on the Tasal Dam Reservoir and on the order of the provincial governor, a committee was set up to demolish it. Today.
According to the same source, this building is built on state land with a size of 12 meters by 24 meters, in the form of a karaoke shop and a kind of slum construction on the Tasal Reservoir Dam, popularly known as the Indian Dam, one of the natural attractions in the area. Many more in Kampong Speu.
Mr. Nhanh Cheab Hung, Director of the Provincial Department of Water Resources, said that the construction in the Tasal area was built illegally and was built as a solid structure as a shop, now it has been demolished and almost 70% of the above construction has been completed. Already broke up and a team inspected.
The governor of Kampong Speu province strictly does not allow the construction of encroachment on this state land, and today ordered the demolition team and many construction materials were confiscated as state property. The National Bank of Cambodia strictly prohibits banking and financial institutions from withdrawing ID cards or family books to guarantee credit.
(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia (NBC) on July 17, 2018, warned to revoke the licenses of any banking, financial and rural credit institutions that continue to remove ID cards, family books and residence books as collateral. On providing credit to the public, because doing so is against the law.
A press release from the National Bank of Cambodia, received by Fresh News on the afternoon of July 17, 2018, stated that the National Bank of Cambodia has previously announced a ban on accepting identity cards or family and residence books for Guaranteed to provide continuous loans, namely from March 2016, but so far the National Bank still sees that some institutions do not comply with the announcement of the National Bank of Cambodia.
The National Bank of Cambodia has warned that "in the event that any rural banking and financial institution or credit institution continues to operate and does not comply with the National Bank's notification, it will be subject to severe disciplinary action." The revocation of business licenses in accordance with Articles 52 and 56 of the Law on Banking and Financial Institutions in force.
The National Bank of Cambodia also urges the public to be careful and avoid using identity cards or family and residence books as collateral for loans.
General Department of Immigration deports Chinese nationals from Cambodia in connection with damage to property and social unrest in Sihanoukville
(Phnom Penh): The Investigation and Enforcement Department of the General Department of Immigration on the afternoon of July 17, 2018, deported 5 Chinese nationals in connection with the crime of intentionally using violence to damage the property of others. Preah Sihanouk Province on July 13, 2018.
Speaking at a press conference, Lt. Gen. Ouk Haysila, director of the Investigation and Enforcement Department, confirmed that after cracking down on the five Chinese nationals involved in the violence, the department would deport them from Cambodia to their home countries. It is impossible to return to Cambodia again.
According to the director general of the department, in addition to causing violence, the five Chinese nationals also had another crime: coming to work in Cambodia illegally, without a valid work permit.
Lt. Gen. Ouk Haysila also requested the relevant authorities and citizens to cooperate in providing information to all foreigners who are secretly staying and committing crimes to the nearest authorities to prevent the commission of other crimes.
In addition, the director of this department also said that in the first 7 months of 2018, the General Department of Immigration, in cooperation with the Capital-Provincial Police Commission, arrested foreigners who came to work and stay illegally and were fired. From Cambodia, 667 people equal to 30 nationalities, including 125 women (including homeless foreigners).
More than 20 years of land dispute between military families and 59 families in Ta Kream commune, Banan district and Khleang Meas commune, Bavel district, Battambang province have been successfully concluded
(Battambang): On July 17, 2018, Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Battambang Province, chaired a meeting to discuss and resolve the land dispute between the families of the army, represented by Mr. Plan Sophalla and representatives of the people related to the land dispute. Prey Preal point, Slap Pang village, Ta Kream commune, Banan district and Khleang Meas commune, Bavel district, Battambang province, at Battambang Provincial Hall.
In connection with this dispute, the provincial administration has set up a working group to resolve the remaining disputes from the land registration according to the old policy, new activities, led by a deputy provincial governor and relevant competent authorities as members of the dispute resolution team, continuing to mediate. Many times between the army and the people to end this land dispute.
After this morning's mediation meeting, both parties agreed to end the dispute by agreeing on the following principles:
First, the family of the ex-army, represented by Mr. Plan Sophalla, agreed to give an additional 4 hectares of land to the people (by taking the southern road from the west intersection) at the request of the people. Thus, the people received a total area of 948,974 square meters for the distribution of 59 families and the families of former military families received a total area of 477,934 square meters for the distribution of 35 former military families.
Second, the people agreed to accept the area of 948,974 square meters, which was agreed between the parties to the dispute to distribute to 59 families by themselves and the families of the ex-army to take the area of 477,934 square meters for distribution. The families of 35 ex-servicemen and some of the remaining land were cleared for roads.
After concluding the dispute, both sides thanked Samdech Techo Prime Minister Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, Senior Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and Administration. Battambang province, which helped to coordinate until they agreed on a win-win strategy to the end today as well.
