Virtualization technology integrated into China's education program (Video inside) (China): The first package of a national curriculum project on virtualization experiments has been released by the Chinese Ministry of Education. The project aims to provide practical education to students through the integration of virtual reality technology in the classroom.
105 virtual projects have been released to the public and are divided into various categories, including biology, mechanics, information, electronics, communications, transportation, and health sciences.
At Jiao Tong University in Shanghai, virtual reality technology and 3D modeling are being used to teach congenital heart disease in young children. This advanced technology not only provides students with a realistic picture of the surgery, but also reduces the difficulty of collecting samples as well as reducing the presentation time.
"So we can say that virtualization helps solve the world's problems in teaching and conducting practical experiments," said Ou Yan, director of the higher education department at the Ministry of Education. "The technology also fills a gap in the performance of college students in China."
According to China's Ministry of Education, by 2020, 1,000 experimental projects for virtual reality teaching will be launched.
"So we think that if we continue to promote this virtual project, it will play an important role in improving the quality of higher education in China, promoting fairness and fairness," said Ou Yan, director of the Higher Education Department of the Ministry of Education. Cultivate talented professionals as well. "This is an effective and innovative way." (China's CCTV)
