(Phnom Penh): As the 6th National Assembly election day is approaching, the public, especially the electorate, would like to know that the ink dipped in the fingers of voters imported from India is of good quality. How good is it, how much is it, and how much is it worth?
These questions will be addressed in the meeting on the conduct of the 2018 6th National Assembly election campaign and security at polling stations and vote counting, as well as a demonstration of the quality of the ink. Fingers will not be removed at 10:00 am on July 17, 2018 at the office of the National Election Committee (NEC).
He said that all the indelible finger ink was bought from India. It was shipped to Cambodia in two legs, the first leg arrived in Cambodia on July 5, 2018 and the second leg arrived in Cambodia on July 7.
The demonstration of the quality of this hand dye was held on the morning of July 17, 2018 at the meeting hall of the Ministry of Interior after the members of the National Election Committee (NEC) presented the process. Of the 2018 6th National Assembly Election Campaign and Security at Polling Stations and Ballot Counting.
Mr. Tep Nytha, Secretary General of the NEC, claimed that after examining and experimenting with hand-dipping ink from India, it was confirmed that the hand-dipping ink used in the 6th National Assembly Election 2018 Good quality is the same as the ink used for the Commune / Sangkat Council elections in the fourth mandate.
Mr. Choy Teng, a representative of the Cambodian People's Party, who was also a participant in the ink test, confirmed that the ink was of high quality because he had soaked it and he had washed his hands with plain water, body soap and body wash. Bathroom and nail polish remover, but his hands still stick to his finger paint.
After going through this test, Mr. Choy Teng expressed his confidence that people will have confidence in this hand-painted ink, that is, they will not have to worry about fraud and vote again.
He also confirmed to the media that the hand-dye that will be used on the upcoming election day can be used to convince the people and also not to let the crooks deceive the masses.
In addition to political party representatives, representatives of civil society organizations also believe in the quality of this hand-painted ink. Mrs. Phan Sovancharya, President of the Association of Former National Servants, also confirmed that the quality of this hand dye is really good, 100% correct according to the NEC, because after soaking your hands, wash all the water and wash a lot. Stage and still not as clean as normal hands.
Ms. Sovann Chakrya claimed that during and after soaking the hands, the experimenter's fingers did not react and affect health, as some suggested. She also called on voters not to worry about the quality and side effects of the hand dye.
