(Phnom Penh): Getting around the city is easier with Grab, but have you ever wanted a trip that was even more amazing? Now with Wing Online MasterCard and Grab, traveling around your city will never be as complicated as before. All you have to do is connect your Wing Online MasterCard to the Grab app and you're ready to go.
When you book a trip through Grab, you do not have to worry about paying or waiting to receive any money, as your travel expenses will be automatically deducted from your Wing account. So when you travel to your destination, you do not have to remember anything because your fare is already calculated.
For customers who have used Grab, they will get 50% discount (up to 8,000 Riel) for 20 Grab trips. The offer will be valid from today until the end of 2018, after the two companies have partnered to provide a new level of mobile travel payment services.
Jojo Malolos, CEO of Wing Specialized Bank, said that the integration of Wing Online MasterCard and Grab really provides many benefits for customers who like to travel smart and up-to-date and do not like to carry a lot of cash. Body.
It is our vision to provide an environment for cashless travel payments. It's not entirely creative if you use a smartphone app to book a trip, but worry while traveling whether you have enough cash or pocket money in your pocket.
With Wing Online MasterCard, we will handle all your travel expenses and you can relax and enjoy the scenery on the road while you travel. This is a further emphasis from Jojo Malolos.
To receive this offer, Wing customers simply activate their Wing Online MasterCard by simply clicking on the "Online Card" button located in the Wing smartphone app. There, customers can fill in and verify some information and have enough balance to register the card.
Wing Online MasterCard gives customers the power of fast, easy and secure payment with just two or three clicks on their mobile device. This is like creating a new world of overseas shopping where even customers without a bank account can do those things.
