At the same time, Mr. Tep Nytha continued that hand-dye and materials used for the 6th National Assembly Election 2018, which will be held on July 29, the NEC. Transport to some provinces gradually as well.
Please be informed that the NEC also invited the Indian company that produces this ink to demonstrate the quality of ink to the participants. He said that the show is for representatives of political parties and national and international organizations to try to know the quality of the ink.
The NEC ordered 51,000 bottles of hand-dipped ink from India with a budget of approximately $ 800,000 and delivered to Cambodia on July 5, 2018. These inks are used at more than 20,000 polling stations across the country, with each bottle required to use two bottles of ink. Cambodian Ambassador to South Korea urges Korean companies to invest in agricultural management technology in Cambodia
