A Russian woman has been arrested by US authorities for allegedly interfering in Washington's internal affairs.
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - A Russian woman has been arrested and charged with meddling in US politics, the US Department of Justice has said. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Tuesday morning, July 17, 2018.
Maria Butina, 29, was arrested Sunday in Washington, D.C., according to the US Department of Justice. The statement added that Butina acted as a Russian agency through the development of relations with the American people and organizations influencing US politics.
