Excavator touches underground medium voltage line, causing power outage in some areas within Koh Pich Development Zone
(Phnom Penh): Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) confirmed that on July 16, 2018 at 16:16 pm, there was a power outage from the second substation (GS2-F11A) due to the construction site in Koh Pich used to tell the excavator to find the pipe. Leaving the Elixir building, it touched an underground medium voltage (MV) line, causing a power outage in some areas in the Koh Pich City Development Zone, Sangkat Tonle Bassac, Khan Chamkarmon, Phnom Penh.
Electricite du Cambodge (EDC) added that the technical team connected the electricity to customers for re-use at 17:24 pm.
