Mr. Em Chanmakara added that the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia has carried out many activities at each stage in the development and promotion of the disability sector to grow continuously.
The Secretary General of the Disability Action Council stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia has taken care of people with disabilities by enacting the Law on the Protection and Promotion of the Rights of Persons with Disabilities for the past nine years. The Royal Government of Cambodia has also developed a national disability strategy successfully implemented within five years.
The development of the Law on the Protection and Promotion of the Rights of Persons with Disabilities and the development of the National Disability Strategy have helped people with disabilities in Cambodia and promoted people with disabilities to avoid discrimination and stigma, especially Fully capable of exercising full rights. This is an addition by Mr. Em Chanmakara.
In addition, we look at the actual activities of the Royal Government of Cambodia under the implementation of the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, with Mr. Vong Soth as Minister, with many activities with relevant partners both at home and abroad to promote the disability sector. In Cambodia, such as the creation of almost everywhere to facilitate the travel of people with disabilities.
Mr. Em Chanmakara continued that the Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the Disability Action Council, a staff of the Ministry of Social Affairs, cooperated with many ministries such as the Ministry of Tourism, the Ministry of Land Management, the Ministry of Urban Planning, the Ministry of Health and many other institutions. People with disabilities and especially give priority to people with disabilities to work like normal people.
Health care for the disabled is the responsibility of the state, physical therapy and the provision of artificial rehabilitation equipment are also provided by the state, for education is also included in the integration class, employment growth and employment. Of people with disabilities is also highly encouraged, facilitation for people with disabilities is also considered and corrected, etc. This is according to what the Secretary General, Mr. Em Chanmakara, confirmed.
Mr. Em Chanmakara, Chairman of the Disability Action Council, thanked the leaders of all ministries, public and private institutions, civil society, national and international media, all citizens, especially people with disabilities, who have contributed to the Royal Government to promote the rights and The welfare of people with disabilities in Cambodia to progress as it is today.
