Letter to readers: Preap Kol and Ath Thorn use the name of the European Union to intimidate and threaten Cambodia?
In the message that Mr. Preap Kol explained in his live release, he tried to imply that he was an important person who at all times the EU came to see him to find out the overall situation in Cambodia before the EU. May issue statements and make any decisions.
You are not interested in not being able to see this point. In the first part of the presentation, he tried to emphasize his role and the importance of his relationship with the European Union, as his live broadcast did not represent him or the institution he was working for.
Although the debate has raised concerns rather than inciting, intimidating and threatening the government, which is Preap Kol's personal intention, he seems to show the ambiguity of these issues.
Ath Thorn Hak added to the situation in a live broadcast, stating that he was very concerned because he had been working closely with the workers. However, both of them, between Preap Kol and Ath Thorn, tried to emphasize the principles and measures of the EU to suspend or completely remove the preferential policy, raising four main issues.
These include: disrespect for human rights, the right to do politics without harassment, and the rights of associations without oppression, workers' rights, freedom from coercion, and the right to form unions and respect democracy. Who would have thought that the two above are human rights experts, if they raise the first few points, it is all a common human rights issue.
However, these are still described by human rights experts as inconsistent, with Preap Kol saying that the EU has raised only three points and Ath Thorn has raised four others. Separated. Ath Thorn tries to get into the big issues involving workers who benefit his group, while Preap Kol draws on human rights, democracy and politics to benefit his political bias.
