(Siem Reap): Seeing the hardships of the people in Daun Keo commune, Puok district, who had to cross the dilapidated old bridge to Siem Reap, APSARA Authority decided to build a new concrete bridge to facilitate the travel of People in Daun Keo commune, both dry season and rainy season.
For many years, Daun Keo commune residents have used a wooden bridge that crosses the Dead Elephants, crossing the road on the back of the western baray to Siem Reap. The wooden bridges are dilapidated and travel is unfavorable during the rainy season due to heavy flooding and sometimes flooding of adjoining villages.
Mr. Ram Vichet, Technical Officer of the Water Management Department of APSARA Authority, said that the new concrete bridge connects Daun Keo commune to Siem Reap city. He added that the old bridge is small and travel in the rainy season is difficult and dangerous if it continues to be used.
Construction of the new concrete bridge began in late June 2018 and is scheduled to be completed in the next three months, with a length of 24 meters and a width of 3.5 meters.
