Of the two temples, the Temple of Preah Vihear has a lot of advocacy because during the time that Cambodia proposed to include this temple as a World Heritage Site, when Cambodia had bad relations with Thailand and the country claimed the Temple of Preah Vihear as their property. They. After Cambodia included this temple as a World Heritage Site, Thailand raised troops to invade Cambodian territory in the area of the Temple of Preah Vihear.
The temple of Preah Vihear was built to dedicate to Hinduism, Preah Iso. The temple faces north on Dangrek Mountain, with a steep slope from south to north. The temple of Preah Vihear has two ancient stairs, the northern staircase leading up to the five gates and the other staircase ascending from the east with a steeper slope than the northern staircase.
The process of listing Preah Vihear as a World Heritage Site has encountered many obstacles and took many years. In 2006, the World Heritage Committee agreed to accept Cambodia's request and sent a team of experts to inspect the condition of the temple. In 2007, the World Heritage Committee decided to include the Temple of Preah Vihear in the World Heritage List in 2008. The 32nd meeting is being held in Canada.
