(Phnom Penh): In the first half of 2018, the National Bank of Cambodia decided to close 50 rural credit institutions operating in Cambodia due to non-compliance with the regulations and laws of the National Bank of Cambodia. This was confirmed by Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor General of the National Bank of Cambodia.
Mr. Chea Chanto confirmed this in the meeting to review the results of the first half and the direction of the second half of 2018 this morning, July 14, 2018.
The National Bank of Cambodia has not yet confirmed the names of 50 rural credit institutions that have been shut down.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Chea Chanto said that the National Bank of Cambodia has been working to implement a series of macro-prudent measures such as capital setting, credit risk management and liquidity, and strengthening the certification of rural credit institutions. Reduce changes in the economic cycle and increase the strength of the banking sector.
"In the first half of this year, the Cambodian economy has continued to grow, especially in the export and tourism sectors, with strong growth in the construction sector and the continued recovery of the agricultural sector, which has led to rapid economic growth," he said. "
