Minister of Agriculture sets out measures to encourage leaders and officials to perform their duties better
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on July 13 met with the leaders of the Ministry and the leaders of all units under the Ministry to manage civil servants and set out some measures to Perform tasks well.
Speaking at the ceremony, Mr. Veng Sakhon laid out six important measures for the Ministry's leadership to implement, including:
1. Cooperate and support the National Election Committee to ensure that the 6th National Assembly election is free, fair and just, as well as to ensure security for the election.
2. Respect and strictly implement the Law on the Election of Members of the National Assembly and the regulations and procedures for the 6th National Assembly Election on the use of state materials and means.
3. Increase attention to the management of subordinates by paying attention to strengthening unity and internal unity and solving difficulties and inactions better.
4. Strengthen and implement their roles and responsibilities in accordance with the law by striving to serve the people, resolve requests and requests effectively and get the satisfaction of the people.
5. Strengthen the leadership and encourage agro-forestry and fishing communities to participate in activities to conserve natural resources, prevent crime and reduce conflicts at the local level.
