(Phnom Penh): The new Ambassador of the Republic of Turkey, Ms. Ayda Unlu, in a courtesy call with Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh on the afternoon of July 12, 2018, confirmed that on behalf of the new Ambassador of The Republic of Turkey intends to forge an alliance with the Phnom Penh administration so that the two countries, Cambodia and Turkey, can have better relations, especially in the areas of tourism and investment.
Ms. Ida Unlou said that as soon as she arrived in Phnom Penh, she was very happy to see that Phnom Penh has developed in all areas, and what is better and more interesting is that the Cambodian people are friendly. .
"Phnom Penh has grown very fast and Phnom Penh has a good infrastructure and Phnom Penh has been ranked as a clean city in Asia," said the Turkish Ambassador to Cambodia.
She said that all these good things she will take to the leadership of Turkey to ask for an alliance with each other, because the relationship between the people and the people with this alliance will lead to both countries. There is more potential.
He added that the growing population in Phnom Penh and the influx of people from the provinces has led to a steady influx of people, which also caused Phnom Penh to face a number of challenges, such as public order, garbage and traffic congestion. Working to improve.
Mr. Khuong Sreng further stated that in Phnom Penh, in the last two years, the crime rate has decreased significantly, which has led to an increase in the number of investors, the increase in tourism, and the warming of diplomats in carrying out diplomatic work. Its.
He added that in a few days, Cambodia will be ready for the election, meanwhile, we have already prepared order and security for all parties. Regarding the desire for an alliance with the Phnom Penh Capital Administration, Mr. Khuong Sreng confirmed to Ms. Ida Unlou that Cambodia welcomes the establishment of an alliance with the cities of Turkey, saying that this is the principle of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
The Governor of Phnom Penh continued that under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Cambodia completely ended the war in 1998. Moreover, Samdech prevented the color revolution backed by some superpowers.
Mr. Khuong Sreng also mentioned that democracy in Cambodia, Cambodia does not need war, and the dissolution of a party because the party leaders are illegal, we apply the law, no matter which party or institution, if illegal. Must be convicted before the law.
It should be noted that the Turkish government decided to open its embassy in Cambodia at the end of 2013. The opening of an embassy in Cambodia shows the good relations between Turkey and Cambodia and will bring benefits to both. The deployment of embassies in Cambodia is also an expression of support for the political regime in Cambodia, especially the constitutional-led regime.
