North Korea changes the timing of talks over the handing over of US military remains, leading US officials to sit idly by ...
SEOUL: North Korean officials appear to have sold a delegation from the United States by failing to appear at a pre-arranged meeting to discuss the return of dead US soldiers. Disposal of bones from the Korean War from 1950 to 1953 back to the motherland. This is according to a quote from the Russian newspaper Sputnik on Friday morning, July 13, 2018.
However, the meeting was rescheduled for Sunday, but the new date was not announced until after US officials spent a while waiting. Growing up on the border between North and South Korea.
According to sources familiar with the matter, after a call to interrogate the North Korean side, US officials were informed that the talks were being rescheduled, with North Korea seemingly wanting the presence of a commander. The U.S. military is at a meeting to expedite the handing over of US military remains.
The issue of returning US troops from North Korea to the United States has been a long-standing issue between the two countries since the Korean War ended with a ceasefire in 1953. According to the US Department of Defense, nearly 8,000 US troops involved in the war have not been repatriated.
