In 2017, the number of students from the One Belt One Road project was 317,000, accounting for nearly 65% of the total number of international students in China.
For example, Hohai University in Jiangsu Province has more than 4,500 international students applying for 2018. That is, almost twice as much as before compared to 2017. And half of the students who applied were from countries along China's One Belt One Road project.
"When we offer scholarships, we give priority to students from other countries in the One Belt One Road project," said Zhang Haichun, director of the Department of International Students at Hoai University. "We have some required curriculum for students from these countries, such as postgraduate courses in environmental engineering for the One Belt One Road project."
These policies have attracted many students from these countries, as well as boosted student exchanges on various subjects between China and those countries.
"We need the cooperation of all Chinese companies, the Chinese government and the governments of other countries for this reconstruction process," said Niza Faisal al-Qayim, a doctoral student at Hoai University. "I want to be a bridge between China and my country to strengthen cooperation and better bilateral relations."
Peking University has organized a new course for international students from 40 countries along the One Belt One Road project. And graduates share their experiences of student exchanges between China and these countries.
