Cambodian Ambassador to South Korea Uses Psychology to Reassure a Depressed Cambodian Worker
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Ambassador to the Republic of Korea, Mr. Long Dimanche, used his skillful psychology to explain to a Cambodian worker who was suffering from depression almost to death, until this young man woke up with a sense of struggle. To overcome the obstacles ahead.
The successful use of psychology to explain depressing behavior took place on July 11, 2018, while Mr. Long Dimanche had a face-to-face meeting with depressed Cambodian workers at the Cambodian Embassy in Korea.
Mr. Long Dimanche said, "I met and encouraged my brother Ty Sarong, a construction worker who was mentally ill and depressed because his family in the district had problems until he could not eat and could not sleep and reached A heart attack will cost you your life. I also described how to reduce stress, reduce depression and encourage more effort, especially health care, do not let it fall like this again.
He added that after receiving the request of his brother Ty Sarong who wanted to go to Cambodia for medical treatment, the embassy team also donated money to buy a plane ticket for him.
Meanwhile, Mr. Long Dimanche called on the parents and families of some of our workers who came to work in Korea not to try to put the burden of endless problems, it will cause our nephews to have serious mental health problems leading to heart attack. . As long as you have a good life and health, you can earn more money and build a sustainable future.
