(Hanoi): Of the six subjects of the high school graduation exam in Vietnam, held in late June, most students scored the lowest in history and English. This was quoted from the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Thursday afternoon, July 12, 2018.
According to statistics from the Vietnamese Ministry of Education and Training, 83.24 percent of Vietnamese students' scores were lower than average, while the most popular score was 3.25 out of 10, with 527 students scoring. The score is zero and only 11 people get 10 full points. In English, 78.22% of the students dropped by a majority of only 3 points, while 732 students got zero marks and 76 students got 10 full marks.
The three-day exam, which was attended by more than 900,000 students at the end of June, was even more important as the results were used for high school graduation and entrance exams. Study at the university. The rate of students passing the exam nationwide is 97.57 percent.
In this exam, Vietnamese students took 4 exams with 6 subjects including literature, mathematics, foreign languages, plus 3 subjects that can be in the social sciences or real sciences.
