Mr. Khim Bunsong: Preventing eligible voters from voting is a provision of the NEC law.
(Siem Reap): On the occasion of meeting with the staff of the Provincial Administration on July 12, 2018, Mr. Khim Bunsong, Governor of Siem Reap, said that to go to the polls or not to go to the polls and to vote for political parties. Any that the people trust is the right of the people, but if any person acts in any way to prevent people who have the right to vote not to go to the polls is a violation of the law.
The Governor of Siem Reap Province further clarified that the prevention of people going to the polls is a provision in Article 142 of the National Assembly Election Law of the National Election Committee (NEC). The article provides for a fine of 5 million to 20 million riels, with the NEC not yet considering other criminal penalties.
According to Mr. Khim Bunsong, any person who commits fraudulent activities to obstruct the election, such as causing aggression, loss of confidence in election secrecy, confusion, loss of confidence in the election, disruption of the election process. Disrupted the order during the election, disrupted the counting of ballots, etc.
