Ministry of Water Resources reaffirms water level in Stung Sangke, Battambang province
(Battambang): Mr. Chan Yutha, spokesman of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, on the afternoon of July 12, 2018, came out to confirm to Fresh News that the water level in Stung Sangke, Battambang province has started to decrease from This afternoon, completely safe and no problems, so let all the people in Battambang do not worry about the water situation above.
Mr. Chan Yutha stated that the reason for the remarkable rise in the water level of Stung Sangke was due to continuous rain in the catchment area of Stung Sangke in the upper part, which caused the water to rise. Increased at the multi-purpose dam in Rattanak Mondul district. As the number increased, the ministry also opened the multi-purpose water gates to release some water.
According to Mr. Chan Yutha, the multi-purpose water gate has 7 gutters and each gutter is 1 meter 7 meters high, so the water is released from this reservoir and the water is released through Stung Sangke to Banan district, which is a dam. The Ministry diverted to the canal and the other part to flow into the Sangker River, which caused the water of the Sangker River to rise, but did not affect the safety of Battambang city.
He added that now at the top of the Sek Sak Dam, the gates have been lowered, and the Ministry has opened the seven gates with a height of 1 meter 7 meters, but now only 1 meter is left, and the gates of the Kanghat Dam have also been lowered, so the water Only part of it flows into Stung Sangke, while the other part flows out through the main canal into Banan, Sangke, Maung Russey and Ek Phnom districts. He confirmed that the diversion measures will start to recede this evening.
At 4 pm on the same day, the Ministry closed two sluice gates completely, leaving five sluice gates and dropped them to 1 meter. This is an additional confirmation from Mr. Chan Yutha.
