The Constitutional Council urges all political parties to file a complaint to the Constitutional Council to focus on the law and the subject matter of the complaint.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Prohm Vichet Akhara, Deputy Secretary General of the Constitutional Council, urged all political parties to file a complaint with the Constitutional Council to focus on the quality of their complaints, with clear content and objectives. On the quantity of the lawsuit.
Mr. Prohm Vichet Akhra said this morning, July 12, 2018, on the occasion that the Constitutional Council held a ceremony to promote the authority of the Constitutional Council to resolve disputes related to the National Assembly election to Senators, members of the National Assembly, representatives of the NEC, representatives of the 20 political parties that participated in the 2018 6th National Assembly Election at the White House, Chamkarmon State, Phnom Penh.
The Constitutional Council official added that recognizing the importance of parliamentary elections and recognizing some of the necessities that require all political parties to have a deeper understanding and reflect on transparency and justice in the period. In this election, all political parties must be aware of the powers of the Constitutional Council.
In this regard, the Law on the Election of the National Assembly, Article 33, paragraph 1, stipulates that any candidate who is rejected or the list of candidates of any political party that is rejected by the National Election Committee or the party concerned. The politician has the right to appeal in writing to the Constitutional Council no later than 5 days after the date of receipt of the rejection letter.
Article 62 of the same law, paragraph 6, states that if the protester or objector is not satisfied with the decision of the National Election Committee, that person or his / her representative can appeal in writing to the Constitutional Council within 5 days. No later than the date of receipt of the decision rejected by the National Election Committee. North Korea sends senior officials to Russia to attend 2018 World Cup closing ceremony
