In addition, the General Commissioner instructed the builders to have the quality and technical standards set by the Ministry.
Minister of Agriculture sets four key principles to reduce vegetable imports and ensure income for small and medium farmers
(Prey Veng): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, presided over this morning, July 12, an exhibition of vegetable and safety products organized by the General Department of Agriculture in collaboration with the Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries. Prolonged.
Speaking on that occasion, Minister Veng Sakhon instructed the General Department of Agriculture to do its utmost to provide certificates of quality, safety, vegetables, fruits and other products to ensure market transparency, truthfulness and fairness in competition.
First, to divert production from production for family supply to production for commercial agriculture, to transform vegetable gardens into vegetable farms.
Second: Incorporate production techniques, selection of varieties, use of drip irrigation system, use of net houses to reduce risks, increase productivity on the same land.
Third, improve the production chain, produce according to a clear plan or program, produce according to market demand and need to follow the Good Agricultural Practices (GAP) and contract farming.
Fourth, it is necessary to consider the processing of packaging to increase the value added, storage and transportation of products to the market to provide efficient and timely services.
According to the Minister, both production mechanisms and techniques have been fully contributing to the formulation of the policy on agricultural development from 2019 to 2030, which is to turn the Cambodian sector into a modern, competitive agriculture, climate change, and especially to respond. And the economic growth of the nation.
