According to a petition from the Council of National Unions of Cambodia, through the EBA, the EU is Cambodia's second largest trading partner. The EBA has created tens of thousands of jobs, provided billions of dollars in income to hundreds of thousands of workers, and lifted millions of their rural families out of poverty. They also continued their studies.
The petition further states that on behalf of the leadership, members of the National Union Council of Cambodia, which has the role of protecting the interests and freedoms of all workers, the National Union Council of Cambodia urges Europe to carefully consider the impact of Withdrawal of the EBA from Cambodia will have a direct negative impact on the jobs and livelihoods of nearly 3 million workers and their families.
According to the National Union Council of Cambodia, all workers are not politicians and should not suffer from the removal of the EBA from Cambodia for political reasons.
Ruling party leader to lead closing campaign on July 27
(Phnom Penh): The leader of the Cambodian People's Party, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will lead the closing ceremony of the election campaign on July 27, 2018.
