An emergency is about to be declared! Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology calls on Battambang residents to be extra vigilant as the Sangker River rises to 12 meters
(Battambang): The water level of Stung Sangke in Battambang province on the morning of July 12, 2018 has risen to 12 meters. With this rising water situation, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has called on people to be very careful because it is close to declaring a state of emergency.
On its Facebook page this morning, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology confirmed that a series of heavy rains at the Cambodian-Thai border in Samlot district, Battambang province, caused water in the multi-purpose reservoir in Battambang. Rattanak Mondul district increased sharply on July 11, 2018 yesterday.
During this period of heavy rainfall from 9 to 12 July 2018, the water level of the river has risen to a height of 12 meters, while recently, the water level of Stung Sangke was only at the bottom of the river.
