Two motorcycles collided head-on in Banan district, killing one man and seriously injuring another
(Battambang): Two motorcycles driving in opposite directions at high speed collided completely, causing the young man to die while being taken to the hospital and one person was seriously injured. The incident happened at 4:30 pm on July 11, 2018 at a point along National Road 57 in Group 14, Phnom Sampov Lech Village, Phnom Sampov Commune, Banan District, Battambang Province.
Mr. Mey Chhengly, Chief of Phnom Sampov Commune Administration Post, said that before the incident, the victim was traveling from east to west, overtaking a bulldozer and colliding with another motorbike driving in the same direction. On the contrary, they collided head-on, causing a man to die at 7 pm on his way to Battambang Provincial Hospital.
Currently, the two motorcycles were dragged to be stored at the Banan District Police Inspectorate, while the bodies of the victims were taken by relatives for a traditional ceremony.
