The 4th National Convention on Intellectual Property Complaints, held in the eastern Chinese province of Shandong on Monday, aims to protect intellectual property and combat unfair competition.
"The Supreme Court will try to protect intellectual property and provide a fair competition," said Tao Kaiyuan, vice president of the Chinese Supreme Court.
"We will use all available legal means to stop illegal labeling and effectively manage the registration of trademarks," said Thao Kayyuan. We will adhere to the principle that all trademark registrations must be made to truly serve the use of the trademark. "We will also comply with Article 4 of the Trademark Law of the People's Republic of China to prevent the use of counterfeit trademarks."
After Germany won the World Cup in 2014, German beer sold better in China. But German beer sales last year fell 3 percent as the Chinese market was overcrowded. According to the German Brewers Association.
Xi Hailong is a local liquor distributor. He collected a wide range of imported beers, including 10 brands of German beer. Xi acknowledged that sales of beer in China have been slow.
"Famous German beer sales are still popular in China, despite low profits," said Xi Hailong. "So due to current market demand, all beer distributors have no choice but to continue importing."
German football fans may be disappointed that the German team lost this match. But for German beer distributors, they are very happy to sell so much beer.
