(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pich Vicheathor, Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, on the afternoon of July 11, 2018, decided to release one accused and issue another detention order on the case of “Intentional Violence Aggravated "stabbing a male neighbor, causing serious injuries.
Judge Pich Vicheathor's decision to release him came after Deputy Prosecutor Seng Heang decided to charge the couple "with aggravated intentional violence" under Article 218 of the Penal Code.
In connection with the charges, Deputy Prosecutor Seng Heang told reporters that he had opened an investigation and decided to charge Sled Youssou, a 34-year-old Cambodian-Muslim man, and Tbos Samros, a 27-year-old woman. Khmer Muslim wife resides in Group 8, Village A, Sangkat Chrang Chamres 2, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh, on charges of "aggravated intentional violence."
According to the charges, the accused faces between two and five years in prison and a fine of 4 million to 10 million riel, not including compensation for mental illness to the victim.
Judge Pich Vicheathor followed the procedure by issuing a detention order for his husband and releasing his wife under judicial supervision.
It should be reminded that the Russey Keo district police arrested the two accused on July 6, 2018 at their house after they violently used knives, bread and metal pipes to beat the victims. The victim was a 38-year-old Cambodian-Muslim man living near the accused's house, causing serious injuries.
