(Phuket): Thai authorities have confirmed the discovery of another body believed to be the latest missing body in the sinking of two Chinese tourist boats off the coast of Phuket, Thailand. Last week, the death toll rose to 46. This is according to the release by Xinhua on Wednesday evening, July 11, 2018.
The search operation in recent days has been carried out by a joint operation between Thai and Chinese rescue teams across the Blue Sea. The latest bodies, which raised the death toll to 46, were found underwater by professional divers.
Of the 45 bodies previously found, five were cremated and two were transported back to China at the request of the families. The rest of the bodies are waiting for a decision from the families of the bodies.
