NBC Governor calls on people to take care of and plant more trees and stop deforestation
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, on July 11, 2018, led the National Bank officials, people and students in Koh Koh commune, Santuk district, Kampong Thom province to plant about 2,000 seedlings. Wat Santuk Krao to help increase the green cover and to celebrate the "Tree Day".
On that occasion, the Governor called on the people, including students, to take care of the existing forest and stop all deforestation and continue to plant trees everywhere to preserve the environment and extract oxygen for human and animal life. Prevent natural disasters as well.
Mr. Chea Chanto said, "Forests are the lifeblood of the planet for human and animal life in general, and if one day the forest is clearly lost, it will increase greenhouse gas emissions in the atmosphere. "There will be changes such as global warming, floods, droughts, extinction of animals, plants and declining agricultural yields."
The governor added that the "Plant Day" was established by the Royal Government of Cambodia since 2002, and was celebrated on July 9 under the Royal Crusade of the King of Cambodia. Mr. Chea Chanto stated that "Tree Day" is celebrated every year and has provided great benefits and value in inspiring people to participate in planting trees and stop all deforestation. .
It should be noted that in the past, Santuk district, Kampong Thom province, under the leadership of the leadership of the National Bank of Cambodia, always celebrated this "Plant Day" every year and planted many trees in Trapeang Trom village, Ty Po commune on an area of approximately Nearly 6 hectares and planted in some other places such as schools, pagodas and public roads. Phnom Penh Military sends 14 suspects in drug case to court
