After an investigation by the police, the 14 suspects confessed to the criminal charges and were sent to court by the Phnom Penh Military Police to be punished according to the law. Letters from Readers: Protecting Our Voting Rights and Democracy in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia began to adopt a liberal, democratic, multi-party political system in 1993, following elections by the United Nations in the spirit of the Paris Peace Agreement of October 23, 1991.
This democracy has grown and lasted for 25 years so far and will be firmly implemented through the holding of elections every five years according to the Constitution and with the participation of many political parties to contest. Win seats in the National Assembly.
Once again, in July 2018, the whole of Cambodia has been continuing the democratic process by holding the 6th National Assembly election with the participation of 20 political parties to win the trust of the people. Take 125 seats in the National Assembly.
Now the Cambodian people are ready to go to the polls on July 29, and the right of the people to vote is to protect their democracy and their right to vote. Survived because to get this right, Cambodia had to swim through many regimes and many people gave up their lives. Citizens of other countries want regular elections like Cambodia, but they are not so lucky.
Therefore, in the face of this threat, the Cambodian people must stand up and be united against the attempts to destroy the Cambodian nation by the traitors and their bosses. Khmer citizens will stand up at all times to defend the rights and freedoms enshrined in the Constitution and the law by going to the polls according to their will and rights.
The Cambodian people will always be strong in defending democracy and peace in Cambodia, which all the people, together with the leaders of the Royal Government of Cambodia, have worked together to build and protect from the beginning. At all costs, we must safeguard the peace, rights, freedoms and democracy that exist now for generations to come.
