Mr. Kun Kim: Anlong Veng district will not be developed if Samdech Techo Hun Sen does not change his life to end the war
(Oddar Meanchey): On July 11, 2018, the fourth day of the election campaign, Mr. Kun Kim, a candidate for the National Assembly in Oddar Meanchey province, continued to search for votes from people in Trapeang Prey commune, Anlong Veng district, Oddar Meanchey province.
Anlong Veng district, Oddar Meanchey province, was the last stronghold of Khmer Rouge soldiers after CPP-led resistance forces overthrew the regime on January 7, 1979. War for territory between the government forces and the remaining Khmer Rouge troops in the area occurred frequently, making the lives of the people and the remaining Khmer Rouge troops very difficult.
Anlong Veng district was the last area where the Khmer Rouge army agreed to surrender to the Royal Government of Cambodia through the victorious policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the policy of national unification at the end of 1998. As Prime Minister at the time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen risked his life to enter the camps of Khmer Rouge soldiers to negotiate directly.
In a meeting with the people this morning, CPP candidate Kun Kim said that without Samdech Techo Hun Sen's win-win policy of 20 years ago, Anlong Veng district would not have been able to achieve peace. Anlong Veng district can not be developed as it is now, the people of Anlong Veng are not living like today.
Mr. Kun Kim stated, "These achievements are due to Samdech Techo Hun Sen taking life as capital and many CPP fighters have sacrificed their lives." "We must all protect these achievements and peace so that no one comes to destroy it and Cambodia does not have a destructive war like in the past."
Mr. Kun Kim pointed out to the people of Anlong Veng district that Cambodia used to be a poor and food insecure country, but now it has become a country with enough food and rice to export abroad, a country that has achieved high economic growth, reduced Poverty comes to the lowest level and leaves low-income countries to lower middle-income countries.
The candidate, a senior official of the Cambodian People's Party, reminded the people that the election on July 29, 2018 is very important for the fate of the country and the people of Cambodia. He said that if the people decide to vote, the nation will continue to improve their lives.
"The decision of the people for this election is a decision to elect the leader of the country. If the decision is right, we will continue to grow, but if the decision is wrong, it will bring the country back. Do not be angry with the oxen to hit the cart. Mr. Kun Kim confirmed.
Major union leaders in more than 100 factories hold a meeting to submit a petition to the European Union to continue providing EBA to Cambodia
"We strongly urge the European Union to provide EBA to Cambodia so that we and our families can continue to earn a living and earn a living," according to a joint statement issued by 112 union leaders. And continue to improve working conditions and freedom of association in Cambodia.
The call comes after union leaders in Cambodia were deeply concerned by reports that the European Union was considering withdrawing the EBA, which is benefiting the Cambodian people. The tax will have a negative impact on the livelihoods of nearly 800,000 workers and millions of other Cambodians, all ordinary people.
The Cambodian Union considers that the EU EBA provides direct employment and income to workers and their families. Massive EU orders and the provision of EBA to Cambodia have also led to a series of increases in the minimum wage for workers, and much improved working conditions and freedom of association compared to the beginning. Of a garment factory in Cambodia.
(Svay Rieng): Mr. Man Sokhon, Deputy Director of CamControl Svay Rieng Branch, in cooperation with Svay Rieng Provincial Department of Commerce, this morning, July 11, 2018, led his subordinates to inspect fruits and vegetables at Tapov Market, where chicken thighs were found. More than 7 kilograms of damaged chicken wings and many other defective goods were put up for sale at Tapov market, Bavet city, Svay Rieng province, and were confiscated and burned.
Mr. Man Sokhon stated that under the guidance of Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce and Mr. Mak Pichrith, the Royal Government delegate in charge of the Director General of CamControl, Camcontrol in Svay Rieng Province has inspected the goods many times. Today's items in order to ensure food safety for people and improve their health because it is very important in society and daily life.
He added that food safety is a joint responsibility of professional institutions, importers, producers, distributors and consumers, because health is a key factor in the survival of the people. Life.
He confirmed that the professional officers inspected various items in the location of Tapov Market and now found more than 7 kilograms of defective goods, chicken thighs and chicken wings, 3 cans and some cakes. In particular, confiscated and banned food that is prohibited by law to seriously affect the health of imported goods through the corridor.
The sellers also agreed to stop selling defective products beyond the expiration date because they were aware of the health effects when using defective products.
At the same time, Mr. Man Sokhorn called on the people as well as all students in Svay Rieng to be careful about eating food to check the date label clearly before buying to eat to participate in promoting well-being together. And CamControl officials will continue to inspect the goods in the markets in Svay Rieng more often.
