CamControl officers found two gas stations and depots in Russey Keo district selling insufficient fuel at the counter and retail price
(Phnom Penh): On July 11, 2018, CamControl officers found two gas stations in Khan Russey Keo that sell less fuel at the counter and retail price.
The inspection of the quantity and quality of fuel at some stations and depots was carried out by the fuel inspection team of the General Department of CamControl of the Ministry of Commerce through a mobile fuel laboratory vehicle led by Mr. Nhung Wen, Deputy Director of the Department in collaboration with Expert staff of the laboratory in order to protect the economic interests of consumers of all types of vehicles and prevent fraud.
Mr. Nhuong Wen said that the quality and quantity control is based on on-site monitoring equipment, such as: The scale has a specific size for measuring the amount of oil fired from the counter in different sizes, with a capacity of 5 liters 10 liters and 20 liters. The octane and cetan indexes are used in mobile laboratory vehicles, while the retail price is based on the Ministry of Commerce's announcement on the retail price of fuel at stations.
As a result of quality control and quantity of fuel of the above 5 stations, 3 locations are compliant in terms of both quantity and quality, 01 location is not compliant in terms of quantity and 01 location is not compliant in terms of quantity and retail price.
The deputy director also called on all vehicle users to consider in choosing a gas station / depot by choosing a reliable company that uses new equipment, sells regular gasoline or super and diesel in good quality and in full liters.
