Ministry of Tourism Establishes Mobile Teachers to Train Tourism Professionals in Businesses and Remote Provinces
(Phnom Penh): A senior official of the Ministry of Tourism announced that the Royal Government of Cambodia, with the Ministry of Tourism as its staff, has set up mobile trainers to train hospitality and tourism skills in businesses and distant provinces to meet the needs of the labor market. And develop tourism professional skills in Cambodia for the better.
This was confirmed by Mr. Pak Sokhom, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, on behalf of Minister Thong Khon, on the occasion of presiding over the certification ceremony for the 1,300 successful trainees who have undergone training in hospitality and food and beverage services. The certification ceremony was held at the National Institute of Education on the morning of July 11, 2018.
With the support of Dr. Ley Sopheap, Director of the Cambodian Institute of Tourism and Hospitality, 22 mobile trainers volunteered to join the Ministry of Tourism to share knowledge and train Cambodian youth on hospitality and tourism skills in businesses and distant provinces. ⁇. At the same time, Secretary of State Pak Sokhom also praised and appreciated the 22 volunteer mobile trainers.
The above 22 trainers include: Business Owners, Management Levels in Tourism Services in Phnom Penh who have received pedagogical training, technical skills training from the Ministry of Tourism and the National Committee of Tourism Professionals through cooperation with the Trainers Club. Tourism Professionalism.
Mr. Chuob Ratana, Director of the Office of Tourism Standards Assessment, said that the Ministry of Tourism has paid attention to the training of tourism professionals by setting up mobile trainers, such as this morning, 22 mobile trainers volunteered to participate. With the Ministry of Tourism to share knowledge and train Cambodian youth on hospitality and tourism skills in remote provinces, as well as other tourist destinations outside of Phnom Penh and the surrounding area.
He stated that tourism businesses, hotel services and travel services can contact the above mobile teachers to share experiences and facilitate ASEAN skills training within the framework of the implementation of the Mutual Recognition Agreement on ASEAN Tourism Professionals (MRA). -TP).
