Ministry of Tourism announces loan program for students in tourism
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism on July 11, 2018 announced the loan program for students in the tourism sector to contribute to the socio-economic development, increase income and create a lot of direct and indirect job opportunities. To the people and by tourism as a sector with convenient conditions.
According to a press release from the Ministry of Tourism, obtained by Fresh News today, this is to ensure the provision of quality services under the good cooperation between the Ministry of Tourism and the private sector, especially training schools. Tourism professionals, associations in the tourism industry and banking and financial institutions.
According to the Ministry of Tourism, so far, many banking and financial institutions are ready to provide scholarships for students in the tourism sector with conditions that are convenient for loan applicants. Up to 6-7 years) with low interest rate, no collateral required, and multiple payment options, including:
First, during the study period, the borrower can pay only about 4 USD per month for the loan amount of 500 USD.
Second, during the study period, the borrower can pay the principal and interest of about US $ 46 per month for one year for the loan amount of US $ 500. Once the job is done, the borrower can repay both the principal and interest of about $ 46 per month per year for a loan amount of $ 500.
The ministry added that young people, students, company staff, tourism professionals and the general public can communicate directly with banking and financial institutions that offer loans in the field of tourism, including:
1: ACLEDA Bank Plc. 2: Canadia Bank Plc. 3: Futaba Microfinance Plc. 4: Hattha Kaksekar Limited 5: KREDIT Microfinance Institution 6: CMK Microfinance Institution
The Ministry of Tourism would also like to inform you that according to the information, banking and financial institutions that provide loans for students in the tourism sector also have a policy to provide loans for study in other fields.
It should be noted that on the occasion of the Second International Conference on "Implementation of the Agreement on Mutual Recognition of ASEAN Tourism Professionals" held on June 21, 2018 at Sokha Residence Hotel, Phnom Penh, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister Of Cambodia also congratulated the participation of all private banking and financial institutions in preparing the student loan project.
