The benefits that civil servants, teachers and the Armed Forces have received from this reform are as follows: First, the annual salary increase that has already been implemented; Second, the payment of salaries through the banking system. To ensure transparency and avoid corruption. Third: In the future, payroll will be made twice a month, once every two weeks.
The three-phase salary reform has made civil servants, teachers as well as the armed forces happy because their salaries increase every year according to the economic situation, and the payment of salaries also ensures transparency. By avoiding corruption and bureaucracy, and finally, they do not have to wait for a long salary until the end of the month. Only two weeks can pay half the salary to use.
Of course, in general, not only civil servants, but also employees in the private sector are always eagerly awaiting their salaries at the end of each month. If they sometimes miss a month and open a day or two later, they also complain because they need to pay regularly. But these difficulties will be gone in the future for civil servants after the principle of paying twice a month will be implemented after the CPP wins the election again.
Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen has already announced that this principle will be implemented from 2019 onwards. This is only within the framework of the same salary reform. In addition, civil servants, teachers and the armed forces also receive overall benefits from peace and development, as well as from policies to reduce gasoline prices, electricity prices, water prices, and benefits from the National Social Security and Retirement Funds. And so on.
As experienced civil servants, teachers and members of the armed forces who have gone through many social upheavals, we really do not want to see the darkest and most painful past come back to haunt us and our country again. No more. Unfortunate propaganda and divisive politics that want to cause social unrest in the style of a color revolution like in the Middle East is the biggest danger for Cambodia that we must all prevent.
To prevent the return of the dark past and to maintain the peace and prosperity of our country, we must all go to the polls on July 29 and vote for the Cambodian People's Party. To ensure that we have what we have today and continue to travel together to make our future and that of our children even brighter.
