Mr. Phan Nady stated that no other temple has an octagonal temple like the one in the area of the Sambor Prei Kuk temple of the Khmer people in Southeast Asia at the same time. In the former city of Vichai of the ancient kingdom of Champa (now in Vietnam) there are also octagonal temples, but only those temples were built after the temple in the area of the temple of Sambor Prei Kuk Khmer.
Among the nearly 300 temples in the Sambor Prei Kuk area, there are about 10 octagonal temples, some of which have broken roofs and walls, but some are still in good condition, he said.
Please be informed that the Sambor Prei Kuk temple site was declared a UNESCO World Heritage Site on July 08, 2017 in Krakow, Poland.
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has already announced the designation of July 10 every year as a day to remember the designation of the Sambor Prei Kuk and Preah Vihear temples as World Heritage Sites.
On July 15, the Royal Government of Cambodia will also celebrate the anniversary of the registration of the Temple of Preah Vihear and Sambor Prei Kuk as a World Heritage Site at the National Olympic Stadium of Cambodia, which will take place under Presided over by Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit.
