GENEVA: The Swiss government decided on Tuesday to file a lawsuit against the United States with the World Trade Organization (WTO) over tariffs on steel and aluminum, sparking outrage in many European countries. This is according to the Swiss Ministry of Economy quoted by Reuters on Tuesday afternoon, July 10, 2018.
In a statement, the Swiss Ministry of Economy said, "Based on Swiss perceptions, the increase in tariffs that the United States claims was made to protect national security is unreasonable."
