Land Border Police Arrested After Threatening to Receive Money from Three Victims in Preah Vihear Province
(Preah Vihear): A suspect, a Border Police Officer No. 793, was arrested by the Preah Vihear Provincial Police and sent to the Preah Vihear Provincial Court for prosecution for threatening to extort money from three victims by telephone. People in Preah Vihear province recently.
Preah Vihear Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Yin Chamnan told Fresh News on July 10, 2018 that the arrest of 793rd Border Police Officer was indeed after receiving a complaint from the victim that there was a case. Threaten to demand money from him over the phone.
He said that after receiving complaints from victims, his police force cooperated with the police force of the Criminal Police Department of the Ministry of Interior, the police force of the Land Border Protection Department and the force of the Department of Technology Crimes to arrest people. This suspect was on July 7, 2018.
Major General Yin Chamnan confirmed that the suspect who was detained by the police was named Ear Hok Lim alias Neng, 39 years old, a police officer of the 793rd Border Guard Corps, residing in Chattang Village, Teuk Krahorm Commune, Choam Ksan District, Preah Vihear Province.
According to the suspect's confession, he told the police that he first threatened on July 1, 2018 at around 1:17 AM by calling Leng Ton, male, living in Dang Phlit village, Chhep Pei commune, Chhep district. In Preah Vihear province, under the guise of Loeng, the mastermind of the robbery, he had just been released from prison and threatened to demand $ 1,000, but the victim said he had no money and would wait another two or three days.
At that time, the suspect called Eng again, pretending to be the Deputy Prosecutor of Preah Vihear Province and threatening to demand $ 500. At that time, the victim begged for only $ 100, waiting to be given later.
