(Phnom Penh): Residents of Phnom Penh will enjoy free travel on public buses in Phnom Penh from today until July 31, 2018. This offer is only for customers who pay for travel using public bus and Wing card.
The special is another Wing effort to improve the city's public transport system following the official launch of the first public bus card three weeks ago. Public bus cards allow passengers to pay for travel by simply tabbing the card on the electronic machines fitted to all 155 buses.
Jojo Malolos, CEO of Wing Specialized Bank, said: "This offer will enable people to travel more and spend less money, promote the spirit of travel by public transport and provide a travel experience. "A new, more convenient way."
In addition, all Wing Cardholders can also use their Wing Card to activate the bus billing system at the booths at the bus station or WING Specialized Bank Headquarters. For Wing customers who use a cardless account, they are required to create a Wing card or purchase a green card to pay electronically when boarding a public bus.
The interesting thing about this public bus card is that it also comes with a Wing account that allows customers to make transactions such as money transfers, phone top-ups, bill payments and online shopping. Well! Remember what else? Create a public bus card now and travel for free around Phnom Penh.
