To maintain good relations, South Korea decided to "suspend annual military exercises"
SEOUL: In the face of improving relations with North Korea, South Korea on Tuesday decided to "cancel the planned Ulchi" military defense exercise, which was previously a targeted exercise. And assess the combat readiness capabilities of this East Asian country. This was quoted from the Chinese news agency Xinhua in the morning of Tuesday, July 10, 2018.
According to a joint statement from the Ministry of Defense and the Ministry of Public Administration and Security of South Korea, the decision was made during a cabinet meeting of President Moon Jae-in. According to the recent security situation, along with the suspension of joint South Korean-US military exercises next month.
Immediately after the first summit with North Korean leader Kim Jong Un in Singapore on June 12, US President Donald Trump vowed to end all provocative exercises with South Korea. Tbong as long as negotiations continue with Pyongyang.
