(Phnom Penh): At 3:15 am on July 10, 2018, a fire broke out in Mittapheap village, Sangkat Russey Keo, Khan Russey Keo, burning 59 houses, equivalent to 66 families. . This is according to the report of the Director of the Fire Prevention and Extinguishing Department of the Ministry of Interior, Major General Net Vatta, obtained by Fresh News on July 10, 2018.
According to the department, the fire was caused by an electrical fault that started from the house of Sin Yin, a 56-year-old Vietnamese man who runs a motodup with his wife Ravi, a 55-year-old Vietnamese man who sells goods. Homes at the scene have caused a series of fires to spread to 59 houses, both large and small, equivalent to 66 families.
During the rescue operation, the fire brigade used 32 fire trucks, including 22 vehicles of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, 6 vehicles of Chroy Changvar District, 1 vehicle of Russey Keo District, and 3 vehicles of the Ministry of Interior. And two water traffic marines, using 129 feet of water.
