The Royal Government of Cambodia will celebrate the 10th anniversary of the registration of the Temple of Preah Vihear as a World Heritage Site together with the celebration of the 1st anniversary of the registration of the Sambor Prei Kuk Temple as a World Heritage Site on the afternoon of July 15. 2018 at the National Olympic Stadium, Phnom Penh, according to Mr. Chuch Phoeun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts.
The celebration will be presided over by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen. In addition, there will be the participation of about 9,000 diplomats, leaders, government officials, citizens and youth.
Mr. Kim Sedara, President of the National Authority of Preah Vihear, said that on the morning of July 15, at the Preah Vihear Temple in Preah Vihear Province, there will be a celebration of the 10th anniversary of the registration of the Temple of Preah Vihear as a World Heritage Site. From government officials and about 1,500 people.
Mr. Phan Nady, Director General of Sambor Prei Kuk National Authority, said that this morning, July 15, at the Sambo Prei Kuk temple site in Kampong Thom province, a ceremony was held to celebrate the one-year anniversary of the registration of the Sambor Prei Kuk temple site as a World Heritage Site. Also, with the participation of the Governor of Kampong Thom, government officials and the people accompanied by various musical arts of the people there.
