Details: A case of fire at a needle factory in Po Sen Chey district, completely destroying materials, the police used 41 fire trucks and 46 water trucks
(Phnom Penh): A fire at a needle factory in Po Sen Chey district, Phnom Penh, completely destroyed property, with the police using 41 fire trucks and 46 water trucks. This is according to the report of the Fire Prevention and Extinguishing Department of the Ministry of Interior, which was received by Fresh News on the night of July 9, 2018.
A report from the Fire Prevention and Extinguishing Department confirmed that a fire at a needle factory in Phnom Penh's Po Sen Chey district had completely destroyed property, with 41 fire trucks and 46 water trucks, including a fire truck from the police. Phnom Penh 21 units and use 30 trucks of water.
Please be informed that at 2:20 pm today, a fire broke out at Mikodo Needle Factory in Phnom Penh Special Economic Zone along National Road 4, Phleung Cheh Roteh West Village, Sangkat Pleung Cheh Roteh, Khan Por Sen Chey. Phnom Penh. The factory is a 45-meter-by-69-meter galvanized stone structure. The owner is Kim Sovannaphum, male, 33 years old. Occupation: General Manager and International Trade (Factory Representative).
The cause of the fire was determined to be caused by an electrical fault that caused 30% of the factory fire, including some equipment, including 10 injection molding machines, 3 dyeing machines, and 1 injection molding machine. , 3 needle dryers, burn 100% finished product.
The fire did not spread to nearby factories and did not cause any deaths or injuries and was extinguished at 4:00 p.m. Very symphonic! Chea Sim Boeung Keng Kang High School teacher was electrocuted due to technical error
(Phnom Penh): Sadly, a teacher at Chea Sim High School in Boeung Keng Kang was electrocuted due to a faulty power line.
Victim name: Sou Sothea, Male, 47 years old, Occupation: Teacher at Chea Sim High School, Boeung Keng Kang, Nationality: Khmer, Address: # 42, Sangkat Teuk Laak 3, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh.
Sources said that before the incident, the victim came to fix the water system in a rented house at the scene, the victim installed a pump motor to the first floor and second floor. . When the victim connected the power line, it was technically wrong, causing an electric shock at the scene.
After the incident, nearby residents reported to local authorities. By the time the police arrived, the victim had lost his life. Immediately, the police contacted the specialized police of the Technical, Scientific Office and the court doctor to examine the body of the victim, confirming that the victim really died by electric shock.
Later, local authorities made notes and handed over the bodies of the victims to their families for a traditional ceremony in their hometown.
China continues to learn more about occupational health and safety in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): A senior official of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training of Cambodia on July 9, 2018, received a delegation from the Director General of Emergency and Occupational Safety of the People's Republic of China to discuss work and find out more. About the health and safety situation implemented in the employment sector in Cambodia.
Leng Tong, director of the Ministry of Labor's Department of Labor Medicine, told reporters that during a meeting between Huy Han Song, secretary of state at the Ministry of Labor, and a delegation from China's Director General of Emergency and Occupational Safety and Health. The Chinese side wants to understand the health and safety of work being carried out in Cambodia to continue to send investors to Cambodia and help protect Chinese investors in Cambodia.
On the other hand, China wants to help Cambodia in training human resources in occupational health and safety by inviting Cambodian officials to attend training courses in China, which has already done two sessions and is scheduled to be held in October. This face again.
Mr. Leng Tong stated that in terms of occupational safety, the Chinese side is focusing on improving the health and safety management system in Cambodia. Because most Chinese investors used to invest in the garment sector, but now they are turning to the construction sector, so China needs to protect its investors, both employers and workers.
However, the two sides agreed to exchange additional study visits with each other, especially on occupational health and safety, in order to ensure the well-being of both workers and employers operating in Cambodia.
It should be noted that in the past, in some factories, there have been challenges related to the fainting of workers, but in the first six months of 2018, the fainting has decreased a lot due to the high attention of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
