Phnom Penh Governor Holds a Meeting with Authorities and Authorities in 12 Districts to Launch New Measures to Strengthen Security, Safety and Order
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of July 9, 2018, the Phnom Penh Municipal Unity Command held a meeting with the competent forces and the 12 Khan authorities to introduce new measures to strengthen security for the special people. Strengthening security, order and safety in the election campaign that has been taking place these days.
Mr. KHOURN Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, said that the opening of this meeting was for the authorities and all competent forces to strengthen security and safety for the people, especially the security protection during the election campaign.
The Governor of Phnom Penh confirmed that during these days, during the election campaign in Phnom Penh, there was better security and order, and this work, the Phnom Penh Municipal Unity Command will do better to make things better. Warm to the people in Phnom Penh.
He said that the improvement did not come easily, it really came from the authorities and our competent forces together working day and night. The Capital Governor also instructed the authorities in all 12 districts to continue to pay more attention to protect the safety and security of the people, especially to prevent and prevent burglary and looting.
For the 12 Khan authorities, a working group shall be established, divided into night and day shifts, in addition to the existing work, and if there are any problems or no problems, they must report to the Phnom Penh Capital Administration every 4 pm every day. That is, this working group must carry out work until the election is completed.
At the same time, the governor instructed the authorities in all 12 districts to report to the Phnom Penh Unity Command at 4 pm every day. He encouraged both the police and the military police, as well as the local authorities, to continue to strengthen security and order without forgetting themselves during the election campaign and the counting of ballots by the district authorities. 12 Must be on duty 24 hours a day.
