(Preah Vihear): As of noon on July 9, 2018, the car accident in Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province on July 8, yesterday, the death toll has risen to 3 while 5 others are The injured were taken to Calmette Hospital.
Dr. Sok Veasna, director of Preah Vihear Provincial Referral Hospital 16 January, told Fresh News that a family car accident in Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province, has so far killed three people and injured five others. Another was seriously injured and was treated at Calmette Hospital in Phnom Penh.
Mr. Sok Veasna said that the accident caused a female victim to die on the spot and seven others with minor injuries were sent to the hospital 16 January, Preah Vihear, but before entering. At the hospital, a girl died. The other six victims were immediately rescued by doctors. The man driving the car was the most seriously injured.
He added that after the first aid team due to the serious condition was sent to Calmette Hospital, the hospital on 16 January did not charge a fee for their transportation. But so far, according to the source of the victim's family, a man from Taikung, the car with the most serious injuries, died this morning. Therefore, in the case of car overturning in Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province yesterday, 3 people were killed and 5 people were seriously injured.
Please be informed that this horrific incident happened at 3:00 pm on July 08, 2018, yesterday along National Road 62 at the point beyond the entrance of Yeang village, Yeang commune, Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province.
Choam Ksan District Police Inspector Colonel O Seng told Fresh News before the accident that the car was speeding in a north-south direction with all eight passengers in it. 3 males, 5 females. At the scene, the car suddenly broke the left rear wheel, causing many cars to overturn.
After the incident, the police found that a woman died on the spot and 7 others with minor injuries were sent to the hospital on January 16 in Preah Vihear province.
The district inspector said that the car that overturned and caused many deaths and injuries was a gray Lexus 330 with license plate Phnom Penh 2S-3198 and all the victims lived in Ponley village, Ponley commune, Mongkul Borei district, Takeo province. He said the car and body were returned to the family to be buried in their hometown.
