(Phnom Penh): Another 16 Cambodians were helped by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs to return home after they cheated brokers into marrying Chinese foreigners and some could not stand the work. This was confirmed by Mr. Chum Suntory, spokesman for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation this morning, July 9, 2018.
Mr. Chum Suntory confirmed that the people who intervened to return to their hometowns include:
1. Seven Cambodian women from Kampong Cham, Kampong Chhnang, Kratie, Takeo, Battambang and Phnom Penh who were tricked into marrying illegally in China. The Cambodian Embassy in China intervened to provide accommodation and food, as well as travel documents for the seven women to return home. The seven Cambodian women returned to Cambodia on July 4 and 5, 2018.
3. Three young Cambodian women, aged between 13 and 16, from Banteay Meanchey province, who were victims of human trafficking at the Poipet International Gate on July 4, 2018.
4. A Cambodian housewife who could not afford to work in Saudi Arabia was assisted by the Cambodian Embassy in the Arab Republic of Egypt to facilitate her repatriation and return to Cambodia on the morning of July 4, 2018.
5. A Cambodian woman who cheated a broker and was arrested by Chinese authorities for living illegally was intervened and repatriated by the Cambodian Consulate General in Xi'an, China. The victim returned to Cambodia on July 3, 2018.
