(Pursat): In the past, there have been a series of deaths due to traffic accidents, driving motorcycles and driving cars, hitting bulldozers, especially trailers, trailers, timber trucks that drive at night. In fact, a man on a motorcycle hit a tractor-trailer while transporting timber, causing the sudden death on the spot, while the driver of the tractor-trailer trampled the shadows.
The above unprotected traffic accident happened at 7:09 pm on July 8, 2018 on the rubber road No. 155 in Prek 1 village, Samrong commune, Phnom Kravanh district, Pursat province.
Phnom Kravanh police said that before the incident, a man was seen riding a white MSX motorcycle without a license plate in the direction from west to east. The driver of the bulldozer saw the incident and fled the scene.
This is the problem with tractor-trailer trailers driving at night on paved roads or national roads without proper lighting or reflection, especially the scissor lift truck.
According to the report, the victim was identified as Khen Yont, a 28-year-old Cambodian man from Kien Koh 1 village, Ta Men commune, Thmor Kol district, Battambang province.
The bodies were handed over to relatives for traditional rites. Separately, the exhibits of motorcycles and bulldozers, trailers, tuk-tuks transporting wood were temporarily stored at the Samrong Administrative Police Station to continue to search for the owner face to face to solve the procedure.
