The 5th National Assembly has ended its mandate, and throughout this mandate, the National Assembly approved 109 draft laws and proposals.
(Phnom Penh): The National Assembly of the 5th legislature closed its full term for 5 years from July 9, 2018 onwards. Throughout the fifth term, the National Assembly passed 109 draft laws and proposals.
Leng Penglong, Secretary General of the National Assembly, told Fresh News that the process of the National Assembly throughout the fifth mandate was good and in accordance with the Cambodian Constitution. He said that the entire process of the National Assembly has helped promote democracy in Cambodia to run well.
It should be noted that the National Assembly of the 5th legislature held its first session under the high presidency of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia on Monday, September 23, 2013. Deputies were sworn in at the Royal Palace before taking office that afternoon.
The National Assembly convened under the chairmanship of Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, Senator of the National Assembly, to elect the President, the Vice President of the National Assembly, the Chairman of the Vice-Chairman of the Committee on Expertise and Trust of the Royal Government on September 24, 2013.
However, the opening of the first session of the National Assembly was also frustrating as 55 lawmakers from the CNRP did not attend the first session and took the oath of office at Angkor Wat. Instead, 68 CPP lawmakers were sworn in without a minority MP.
However, after nearly a year of suffocation, CNRP lawmakers, now disbanded by the Supreme Court, have returned to the National Assembly under political compromise.
If nothing changes, the National Assembly of the sixth mandate will be formed at the end of September 2018, more than a month after the National Assembly election on July 29, 2018.
Ministry of Labor urges all business owners and establishments to pay their workers before July 27 to facilitate voting
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on July 9 issued a notice urging all factory owners, enterprises and establishments to pay their workers before July 27, 2018. To facilitate the participation in the 6th National Assembly election, which will be held on July 29.
The ministry further stated that in case the factory owners are unable to pay their wages on time, the workers should be allowed to receive at least 50% advance payment before July 27, 2018.
Japanese authorities have warned that the death toll from floods and landslides caused by heavy rains in the western part of the country may continue to rise as the death toll rises to 90 and 58, respectively. Others are still missing from last Thursday until the morning of the new week. This is according to the release by Japanese TV NHK on Monday morning, July 9, 2018.
As of 9:30 a.m. Monday, the death toll had risen to 90, with three people seriously injured and 58 still missing.
