Be careful every time you drive! Two killed, six seriously injured in car accident after speeding in Preah Vihear province
(Preah Vihear): At least two people were killed and six others were seriously injured and taken to hospital. This case is caused by a car with broken tires after driving fast on the road.
This horrific incident happened at 3:00 pm on July 08, 2018 along National Road 62 at the point beyond the entrance of Yeang village, Yeang commune, Choam Ksan district, Preah Vihear province.
Choam Ksan district police chief Brigadier General O Seng told Fresh News this afternoon that before the accident, the car was speeding from north to south with eight passengers on board. Both drivers, 3 males and 5 females. At the scene, the car suddenly broke the left rear wheel, causing many cars to overturn.
The district inspector said that the car that overturned and caused many deaths and injuries was a gray Lexus 330 with license plate number Phnom Penh 1S-3198, and all the victims lived in Ponley village, Ponley commune, Mongkul Borei district, Takeo province. He said the car and body were returned to the family to be buried in their hometown.
Separately, Sok Veasna, director of the 16 January Referral Hospital in Preah Vihear province, said that of the seven people who were sent to the hospital, one died before being taken to the hospital, while the male driver did not hope. Survived because of serious injuries. However, doctors are taking care to treat the victims as much as possible.
