Khmer children's point of view: Sit back and think, what do we gain from the leadership of Prime Minister Hun Sen?
(Phnom Penh): If we do not look at it from all angles, we do not realize that we have all been benefiting greatly from the Royal Government led by Prime Minister Hun Sen.
The greatest achievement that we must not forget is to save the country from death during the Khmer Rouge regime. The second great achievement that we Cambodians must remember is to end the civil war and bring peace under the famous victorious politics. The third major achievement that Cambodia has never seen in its history is the rapid development and infrastructure of roads, bridges, schools, shopping malls and congested vehicles.
In particular, if we look in more detail, we will see more clearly that in addition to these great achievements, people from all walks of life are benefiting more from the leadership of the Royal Government, the CPP, with Prime Minister Hun Sen as Head.
Practical: Workers receive a lot of benefits. In addition to the $ 170 minimum wage, they have many other benefits: free bus rides, reduced electricity tariffs, social security, especially for pregnant women with special budgets. 3 months maternity leave with up to 120% pay and other benefits. In the future, they will benefit from more pension policies.
Women in poor families also benefit greatly when they become pregnant. They will receive three stages of benefits, from pregnancy to childbirth until the child is two years old.
