Before leaving for the election campaign, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced many policies of the Cambodian People's Party for the implementation of the sixth mandate, in which he also mentioned the policy to reduce the price of electricity.
He stressed that the Royal Government led by the Cambodian People's Party will expand the electricity supply from the national grid to all villages in 2019 and 2020 and continue to reduce electricity prices.
"I reassure my compatriots across the country that the Royal Government, led by the Cambodian People's Party and I, the Prime Minister, will implement a reduction in electricity tariffs for all types of consumers across the country," he said. For 2019 and 2020, the following goals.
First, for now, large-scale consumers of all kinds who buy electricity from substations through high voltage gates or buy through medium voltage gates of substations in Phnom Penh or buy medium voltage gates from substations in the provinces. The high voltage price is 503 riels per kilowatt hour and in 2019 will be reduced to 474 riels per kilowatt hour 474 riels.
Second, for industrial consumers who buy through sub-transmission lines and medium-voltage transmission lines through the distribution network in Phnom Penh at 676 Riel and in the provinces 672 Riel in 2019 will fall to 596 Riel in 2020. Will fall to 592 riel.
Third: For commercial and administrative users who buy through sub-transmission lines and medium voltage lines of distribution areas in Phnom Penh, the current price is 676 Riel in the provinces, the price of 672 Riel in 2019 will be reduced to 645 Riel and at In 2020, it will come down to 640 riels.
Fifth, for the purchase of electricity for pumping water for agriculture from 9 pm to 7 am, the current price of 480 riels will remain the same in 2019 and in 2020.
Sixth, for the use of electricity in schools, hospitals and health centers, which is currently implementing the price of 770 riels will fall to 610 riels in 2019 and remain the same in 2020.
Samdech Techo stated that these are the actual electricity prices that will be implemented in 2019 and 2020 if the CPP wins the election and the Royal Government led by the CPP will consider further reduction of electricity prices as much as possible. Possible.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also said that in order to implement the policy to reduce the price of electricity, the state must sacrifice $ 40 million in tax revenue per year, which is a measure to facilitate people's livelihood and help increase competitiveness. Attract investment in the country.
