(Kampong Chhnang): At least one man died instantly at the scene and six others were seriously injured in a traffic accident between four motorcycles and four cars collided along National Road No. 5 Opposite the gate of Wat Phnom Champouk, about 100 meters south of Chrey Bak bridge in Andong village
Snay, Andong Snay commune, Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province.
According to the traffic police officer at the scene, the accident happened at 7:00 pm on July 6, 2018, when a Titan car collided with a motorcycle, causing a man Khem Savoeun alias (Pov), a resident of Meanchey village, Kork Banteay commune, Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province, died on the spot.
Fifteen minutes after the incident, while people were slowing down to stop, a five-lane truck carrying cement was traveling from north to south, apparently braking incorrectly and crashing into another, causing six other people to be seriously injured. .
Police said that a total of four vehicles, including a Tacoma car, a Tico car, a Titan car and a jeep. Separately, the 4 motorcycles are 2 C125, 1 motorcycle and 1 tuk tuk.
The victim was taken by ambulance to Kampong Chhnang Provincial Referral Hospital for treatment, while the car and motorbike were taken by the traffic police to be stored at the Land Traffic Office of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Police. Next time.
