The IDC-CDI was founded in 1961 and has 94 members, political parties, organizations or associations from Europe, Latin America, Africa and the Asia-Pacific, whose ideas and activities are guided by the principles of central democracy and humanism.
For more than a decade, the Cambodian People's Party, under the wise leadership of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party and Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, has adhered to the values of democracy. Central and became a full member of the IDC-CDI family at the Executive Committee Meeting in Lisbon, Portugal in April 2016.
The CPP considers this to be a recognition of the CPP's efforts to jointly promote common values and principles in strengthening democracy in the world, which makes societies more just and prosperous. The Cambodian People's Party believes that peace, stability, friendship and responsibility are necessary conditions for development, avoiding a culture of violence and preventing extremism in order to bring harmony to all our people.
