At least 24 people have been killed and 32 others injured in an explosion at a fireworks store in Mexico City. This is according to the press release from Sputnik on Friday morning, July 6, 2018.
According to local authorities, the tragedy happened this Thursday at 9:30 a.m. (local time) at a factory fireworks depot in the Tultepec region of the region. Northern Mexico. The bomber struck shortly after noon in front of a police station, killing at least four people and wounding two others.
With the advent of interconnected roads and bridges, it is now easier for people to travel and more convenient to transport goods, leading investors to reduce costs. More on their delivery.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, who is a staff member of the Royal Government of Cambodia and is building prominence in his work, stressed that the road and bridge infrastructure system plays an important role for the national economy, which is like a blood vessel. In the human body as well.
Most of the roads and bridges in Cambodia, the Royal Government of Cambodia borrowed money from abroad to build, of which China provided the largest loan for this construction amounting to about 2,553 million US dollars.
Even though these loans are used to build roads and bridges for the benefit of the nation and the people, some Cambodians still have a negative reaction every time they hear that the Royal Government borrows foreign money to build infrastructure.
In response to the negative reaction to foreign loans, a question has been raised that compares between borrowing foreign money to build roads for the benefit of the nation and the people with not borrowing money from the country to build roads and leave Cambodia still lacks this road and bridge transportation system, which one is more profitable?
Answering this question, Mr. Sun Chanthol pointed out that it would be wrong to borrow money to buy an official car, but borrowing money to build a road is not wrong, on the contrary, it brings great benefits. Lots for the national economy. He added that there is no country in the world that does not lend money to promote national development.
Mr. Sun Chanthol further stated that the loan was also balanced by the Royal Government with the national income, not just the borrowers could not repay the loan.
"Our government is not just borrowing, they have rules. Please be informed that the rules allow each country to normally lend about 40% of the total national income. Today in Cambodia, we borrow less than 30 percent, so we still have many opportunities to borrow more, but the Royal Government, we do not just borrow, change, borrow something to be effective, not to be lazy. Senior Minister Sun Chanthol emphasized.
(China): The Chinese government has announced that it will continue to develop "e-agriculture" projects in rural areas across the country. The project aims to help farmers easily connect to the internet and use information technology.
In 2017, e-commerce projects were officially launched to support 756 provinces in China. The project generates a total of $ 190 billion in online retail revenue and 28 million jobs for rural people. In addition, big data technology is also being used in agriculture.
Currently, one-third of all villages under the project have access to information systems for access to public services, e-commerce and training for farmers.
An official from the Chinese Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Affairs added that the "e-agriculture" project would be further developed to promote the collective development of primary, secondary and tertiary industries in rural areas.
