Anniversary of Preah Vihear Temple and Sambor Prei Kuk Temple as a World Heritage Site will be held in mid-July
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia will celebrate the 10th anniversary of the registration of the Temple of Preah Vihear as a World Heritage Site together with the celebration of the 1st anniversary of the registration of the Sambor Prei Kuk Temple as a World Heritage Site this afternoon. July 15, 2018 at the National Olympic Stadium, Cambodia, Phnom Penh.
This statement was made at a press conference on the morning of July 5 in the presence of Mr. Chuch Phoeun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, Mr. Hab Tuch, Director General of Culture of the Ministry of Culture, Mr. Phan Nady, Director General of Sambo Prei Kuk National Authority, Mr. Kim Sedara, President of National Authority Preah Vihear and Mr. Som Ratana represent the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia at the Ministry of Culture.
Secretary of State Chuch Phoeun said that the Royal Government of Cambodia, with the Ministry of Culture as its staff, will celebrate the 10th anniversary of the listing of the Temple of Preah Vihear as a World Heritage Site and the one-year anniversary of the registration of the Sambor Prei Kuk site. As a World Heritage Site on July 15 from 4 pm at the National Olympic Stadium, Phnom Penh.
The Secretary of State said that the celebration will be presided over by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen. In addition, there will be the participation of diplomats, leaders, civil servants, citizens and about 9 youth Thousands, too.
The President of the National Authority of Preah Vihear, Mr. Kim Sedara, said that on the morning of July 15, at the Preah Vihear Temple in Preah Vihear Province, there will be a celebration of the 10th anniversary of the registration of the Temple of Preah Vihear as a World Heritage Site. Attended by about 1,500 government officials and citizens.
Mr. Phan Nady, Director General of Sambor Prei Kuk National Authority, said that this morning, July 15, at the Sambo Prei Kuk temple site in Kampong Thom province, a ceremony was held to celebrate the one-year anniversary of the registration of the Sambor Prei Kuk temple site as a World Heritage Site. Also, with the participation of the Governor of Kampong Thom, government officials and people accompanied by various musical arts of the people there.
The representative of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, Mr. Som Ratana, also said that in the celebration of the 10th anniversary of the registration of the Temple of Preah Vihear as a World Heritage Site, together with the celebration of the 1st anniversary of the registration of the Sambor Prei Kuk Temple as a World Heritage Site. On July 15, 2018, about 4,000 members of the CPPCC will also participate in this event.
Mr. Hap Tuch, Director General, said that the festival also has many cultural programs such as performing arts, dances and cultural songs, screening of some promotional videos.
Please be informed that the Temple of Preah Vihear was registered as a UNESCO World Heritage Site on July 7, 2008. Meanwhile, the Sambor Prei Kuk temple area was registered as a UNESCO World Heritage Site on July 08, 2017.
