Tbong Khmum Provincial Authority Celebrates International Day Against Drugs Under the Theme "Join Together for a Drug-Free Life and Our Community"
(Tbong Khmum): This morning, July 05, 2018, Tbong Khmum Provincial Authority organized the International Day Against Drug Abuse for this year under the theme "Join together for life and our community free of drugs" at Memot Market. In Memot district.
The ceremony was presided over by Mr. Thong Sokunthea, Deputy Secretary General of the National Authority for Combating Drugs and Mr. Ly Leng, Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, with the participation of the Provincial Board of Governors, Departments around the province, monks, relevant government officials, teachers and students. Crowds of balloons and drug parades around Memot Market to raise awareness of drug-related issues.
According to the report, Mr. Kun Sophea, Director of the Secretariat of the Provincial Drug Control Committee, said that in the first quarter of 2018, the operation cracked down on 150 cases, including 119 cases of trafficking and storage and 24 cases of use. A total of 263 people, including 27 women, were arrested and 453.74 grams of methamphetamine (ice), 3 cars, 20 motorcycles, 8 scales, 3 small arms, knives, swords and other items were seized.
At the same time, Mr. Thong Sokunthea also read the message of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, which set out the rules and strict measures of 7 important points to make this anti-drug campaign more effective.
Speaking on the occasion, Mr. Ly Leng, Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, said that despite the authorities' efforts to crack down and arrest people involved in drug trafficking, the distribution activities will continue, especially in rural areas. .
He said that through the ceremony held now is to increase the support from all quarters to increase the effectiveness of prevention, prevention, fight and eradication of drug trafficking, distribution and use even more strongly in the territory. Tbong Khmum province as well as throughout the country.
At the same time, on behalf of the Chairman of the Provincial Drug Control Committee, Mr. Ly Leng requested the provincial authorities at all levels and all stakeholders to participate in disseminating the effects of drugs and encourage local people to report on these issues. Use and help exchange drugs to local authorities to crack down on time and the village - commune is safe for all.
