National Bank of Cambodia: The microfinance sector currently has 1.9 million depositors and received $ 2.3 billion in deposits.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor-General of the National Bank of Cambodia, said that the microfinance sector currently has 1.9 million depositors and received $ 2.3 billion in deposits. Provides a total of $ 4.8 billion in loans to approximately 1.8 million customers.
This statement was made by the Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia on the occasion of presiding over the graduation ceremony of 165 people in the 24-25th Master of Banking Technology at the Koh Pich Theater on the morning of July 5. 2018.
According to Governor Chea Chanto, the microfinance sector currently has $ 5.5 billion in assets and has provided a total of $ 4.8 billion in loans to a total of 1.8 million clients. Total deposits were $ 2.3 billion, with a total of 1.9 million depositors.
He added that the provision of loans has improved the living standards of citizens by responding to the financial services needs of customers in their daily business, and now the number of adults using formal financial services has increased. Rapidly up to 75% of the total adult population, an increase of seven times compared to 2005.
It should be noted that the banking sector has been actively involved through the provision of comprehensive and environmental financial services that have improved the lives of the people and reduced poverty in Cambodia.
On that occasion, Mr. Chea Chanto also highly appreciated the success of the students who successfully graduated in banking in the Banking Technical Study Center. Obtaining a Master's degree in Banking Technology now is a success and a source of pride for all children, parents, guardians, professors and the nation.
